$ P(X=0)=\frac{1}{8} $, $ P(X=1)=\frac{3}{8} $, $ P(X=2)=\frac{3}{8} $, $ P(X=3)=\frac{1}{8} $

$ P(0 < X < 3) = P(X = 1) + P(X = 2) = \frac{3}{8} + \frac{3}{8} = \frac{6}{8} = \frac{3}{4} $

Correct Option: (2)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.936Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (53, 19, NULL, NULL, 'The area (in sq. units) of the region bounded by y = -1, y = 2, $ x = y^{3} $ and x = 0 is equal to 1.4

2.8

3. $ \frac{17}{4} $

4. $ \frac{15}{4} $', NULL, '[{"text":"1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Bounded by y = -1, y = 2, $ x = y^{3} $, x = 0.

$$

\begin{aligned}

A &= \int_0^2 (y^3 - 0) \, dy + \int_{-1}^0 (0 - y^3) \, dy \\

\int_y^3 dy &= \frac{y^4}{4} \\

\int_0^2 y^3 dy &= \frac{16}{4} - 0 = 4 \\

\int_{-1}^0 (-y^3) \, dy &= -\left(0 - \frac{1}{4}\right) = \frac{1}{4} \\

A &= 4 + \frac{1}{4} = \frac{17}{4} \\

\end{aligned}

$$

Correct Option: (3)

The general solution of the differential equation $ \frac{dy}{dx} = -4xy^{2} $ is given by

1. $ 2x^{2}-y=C $ : C is an arbitrary constant

2. $ 2x^{2}-\frac{1}{y}=C $ : C is an arbitrary constant

3. $ 2x^{2}+\frac{1}{y^{2}}=C $ : C is an arbitrary constant

4. $ 2x^{2}+\frac{1}{y}=C $ : C is an arbitrary constant

Options:

A. 1

B. 2

C. 3

D. 4

Answer: B

Solution:

$$\frac{dy}{dx} = -4xy^2$$

$$\frac{dy}{y^2} = -4x \, dx$$

$$\int \frac{dy}{y^2} = \int -4x \, dx$$

$$-\frac{1}{y} = -2x^2 + C$$

$$\frac{1}{y} = 2x^2 - C$$

$$2x^2 - \frac{1}{y} = C$$

$$\left| \text{Correct Option: (2)} \right|$$', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.936Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
