  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(A) Devonian</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(I) Gnetales</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(B) Carboniferous</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(II) Cycads</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(C) Jurassic</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(III) Seed ferns</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(D) Cretaceous</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(IV) Progymnopserms</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)(I), (B)(II), (C)(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)(IV), (B)(III), (C)(II), (D)-(1)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)(III), (B)(IV), (C)(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Devonian (Progymnosperms), Carboniferous (Seed ferns), Jurassic (Cycads), Cretaceous (Gnetales).', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.976Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (133, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The inner cell mass of the embryo contains some cells which can give rise to all the tissues and organs. They are known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Ectoderm","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Blastomeres","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Trophoblast","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Stem cells","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Correct Answer: (4) Stem cells

Explanation:

The inner cell mass of a blastocyst contains pluripotent stem cells.

- Can differentiate into various tissues

- Used in regenerative medicine', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.976Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (134, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Zygote or embryos upto 8 blastomeres can be transferred into the fallopian tube for further development. The procedure is known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gamete intra fallopian transfer (GIFT)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Intra-uterine insemination (IUI)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Correct Answer: (1) Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)

Explanation:

Explanation:

ZIFT involves transferring a zygote or early embryo into the fallopian tube.

- Done after in vitro fertilisation

- Suitable for women with normal tubes

Why others are wrong:

- (2) GIFT: Transfers gametes, not zygote

- (3) ICSI: Injects sperm into egg, not a transfer method

- (4) IUI: Transfers sperms into uterus

CUET Tip: Recall assisted reproductive techniques.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.977Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (135, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Cyclosporin A, which is used as an immunosuppressive agent, is produced by:', NULL, '[{"text":"Staphylococcus","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Penicillium notatum","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Trichoderma polysporum","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Monascus purpureus","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Solution:

Correct Answer: (3) Trichoderma polysporum

Explanation:

Cyclosporin-A, an immunosuppressant, is produced by T. polysporum.

- Used in organ transplant to prevent rejection

Why others are wrong:

- (1) Staphylococcus: It is the bacteria on which Alexander Fleming was doing experiment.

- (2) Penicillium notatum: Produces penicillin

- (4) Monascus purpureus: Produces statins

CUET Tip: Tabulate microbes and their products', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.980Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (136, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The pyramid of biomass in the sea is -', NULL, '[{"text":"Always upright","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Upright","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Inverted","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Neither inverted nor upright","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Correct Answer: (3) Inverted

Explanation:

This refers to the inverted pyramid of biomass in aquatic ecosystem.

CUET Tip: Watch for NCERT diagrams in ecosystem.

Figure 12.4 (c) Inverted pyramid of biomass-small standing crop of phytoplankton supports large standing crop of zooplankton', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.980Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (137, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the given structures in correct sequence of transcription unit when we move from left to right?

(A) Terminator

(B) Promoter

(C) Structural gene

(D) Transcription start site', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B), (C), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (D), (C), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (B), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Correct Answer: (2)(B), (D), (C), (A)

Explanation:

This sequence follows the correct order of molecular biology steps.

- Based on NCERT diagrams

CUET Tip: Practice NCERT flowcharts and diagrams.

Figure 5.9 Schematic structure of a transcription unit', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.981Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (138, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the scientists associated with the antibiotic "Penicillin":

(A) Alexander Fleming

(B) James Watson

(C) Ernest Chain

(D) Howard Florey', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) and (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Correct Answer: (4) (A), (C), and (D) only

Explanation:

Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming, and its medical use was developed by Chain and Florey.

- All three received the Nobel Prize

CUET Tip: Remember key discoveries and scientific achievements.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:37.981Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (139, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the given taxa of invertebrates in terms of their increasing numbers.

