• The closest synonym is Irritable.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.090Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (341, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Select the most appropriate word or phrase to complete the following sentence:-

Once you $ \underline{\text{}} $into the routine, you will find the work is quite easy.', NULL, '[{"text":"are settled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"had settled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"settled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"will settle","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '- When a sentence uses a future result ("you will find…") and starts with a time conjunction like "Once" (or if, when, as soon as), the verb in the "Once" clause must be in the Simple Present tense.

- "are settled" is the grammatically correct Simple Present (in the passive voice) needed here. The other options are incorrect tenses (past perfect, simple past, simple future).', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.091Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
