(A) craftsmanship and profound spiritual depth, features

(B) ancient Indian architecture, celebrated for its intricate

(C) iconic temples, stupas, and forts that showcase', NULL, '[{"text":"(C), (A), (B), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (B), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Ancient Indian architecture, celebrated for its intricacy, showcases iconic temples, stupas, and forts, a blend of artistic brilliance and advanced engineering, features craftsmanship and profound spiritual depth.

B $ \rightarrow $ introduces subject: "Ancient Indian architecture…"

C $ \rightarrow $ specifies what it showcases: "iconic temples, stupas, and forts"

D $ \rightarrow $ adds detail: "blend of artistic brilliance and advanced engineering"

A $ \rightarrow $ concludes qualities: "features craftsmanship and profound spiritual depth"', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.119Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (390, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Select the word opposite in meaning to the given word:-
Novice', NULL, '[{"text":"Amateur","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Expert","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Artist","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Priest","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Expert : highly skilled and experienced; opposite of novice (inexperienced).

Why not others:

Amateur : similar to novice, not opposite.

Artist, Priest : unrelated to experience level.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.120Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (391, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct option:

I asked many people the way to the station but of them had any clue about it.', NULL, '[{"text":"none","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"some","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"few","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"everyone","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'None - not one or no one; fits the context of zero people knowing.

Why not others:

Some, Few: imply at least some knew, which is incorrect.

Everyone: opposite meaning, all knew.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.120Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
