D: dissent - express disagreement in debate.', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/english-2025-05-20-shift-2/q50-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 50', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.130Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/english-2025-05-20-shift-2/q50-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 50","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (414, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Which one of the following gland is responsible for the secretion of growth hormones?', NULL, '[{"text":"Pineal Gland","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pituitary Gland","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thyroid Gland","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Adrenal Gland","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The growth hormone (GH) is secreted by the pituitary gland (specifically the anterior pituitary). Correct answer: 2. Pituitary Gland', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.133Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (415, 18, NULL, NULL, 'In an A.P. if $ m^{th} $ term is n and the $ n^{th} $ term is m, where $ m \neq n $, find the $ p^{th} $ term.', NULL, '[{"text":"$ n + m + p $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"m - p","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ n + m - 1 $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ n + m - p $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Given:

$$ T_{m}=a+(m-1)d=n\quad\ldots(1) $$

$$ T_{n}=a+(n-1)d=m\quad\ldots(2) $$

Subtract (2) from (1):

$$ (a+(m-1)d)-(a+(n-1)d)=n-m $$

$$ (m-n)d=n-m $$

$$ d=-1 $$

Substitute $d = -1$ in (1):

$$ a+(m-1)(-1)=n $$

a - m + 1 = n

$$ a=n+m-1 $$

Now find $ T_{p} $:

$$ \begin{aligned}&T_{p}=a+(p-1)d\\=(n+m-1)+(p-1)(-1)\\&=n+m-1-p+1\\&=n+m-p\end{aligned} $$

✓ Final Answer:

4. $ n + m - p $', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.133Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (416, 18, NULL, NULL, 'The base radius of a cone is 21 cm and the height is 28 cm, then, which of the following is/ are correct?

(A) Slant height = 35 cm

(B) Slant height = 33 cm

(C) Volume = 12936 cm^{3}

(D) Curved Surface Area = 2310 cm $ ^{2} $', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (D) and (A) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D), (A) and (B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Given:

r = 21 cm, h = 28 cm
1. Slant height:

$$ l=\sqrt{r^{2}+h^{2}}=\sqrt{21^{2}+28^{2}}=\sqrt{1225}=35 $$

(A) correct

(B) wrong

2. Volume:

$$ \begin{aligned}V=\frac{1}{3}\pi r^{2}h=\frac{1}{3}\pi\cdot441\cdot28&=4116\pi\\ &=4116\times\frac{22}{7}=12936\end{aligned} $$

(C) correct

3. Curved Surface Area:

$$ \begin{aligned}CSA&=\pi rl=\pi\cdot21\cdot35=735\pi\\&=735\times\frac{22}{7}=2310\end{aligned} $$

(D) correct
Final Answer:

Option 3 $ \rightarrow $ (C), (D) and (A) only', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.134Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (417, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Who among the following is best known as the Chief Architect of the Indian Atomic Energy Program?', NULL, '[{"text":"C.V. Raman","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Homi Jehangir Bhabha","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Meghnad N. Saha","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Vikram Sarabhai","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The title "Chief Architect of the Indian Atomic Energy Program" is associated with:

Homi Jehangir Bhabha

He is regarded as the father of India''s nuclear program.

Correct answer:

2. Homi Jehangir Bhabha', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.134Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (418, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Select the figure from the options, which when placed in the blank space would complete the given pattern.', NULL, '[{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q05-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 5', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.134Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q05-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 5","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q05-options.jpg","alt":"Printed answer choices for question 5","kind":"options"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (419, 18, NULL, NULL, 'The angle of elevation of the top of an unfinished tower at a distance of 75m from its base is $ 30^{\circ} $. How much higher must the tower be raised so that the angle of elevation of its top at the same point may be $ 60^{\circ} $?', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 20\\sqrt{3} $ m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 50\\sqrt{3} $ m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"30 m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"60 m","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Initial height:

$$ \tan30^{\circ}=\frac{h_{1}}{75}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} $$

$$ h_{1}=\frac{75}{\sqrt{3}}=25\sqrt{3} $$

Final height:

$$ \tan60^{\circ}=\frac{h_{2}}{75}=\sqrt{3} $$

$$ h_{2}=75\sqrt{3} $$

Increase in height:

$$ h_{2}-h_{1}=75\sqrt{3}-25\sqrt{3}=50\sqrt{3} $$

✓ Final Answer: 2.50√3 m', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.135Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (420, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Consider the compound interest of the following

(A) The compound interest on Rs 16000 at 20% per annum for 9 months, compounded quarterly is: Rs 2522

(B) The compound interest on Rs 2800 at 10% per annum for 18 months, compounded annually is: Rs 434.

Choose the correct statement(s):', NULL, '[{"text":"Only (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Only (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Both (A) and (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Neither (A) nor (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '(A)

Principal = 16000

Rate = 20% p.a. → quarterly ⇒ 5% per quarter

Time = 9 months = 3 quarters

$$ A=16000(1.05)^{3}=16000\times1.157625=18522 $$

$$ CI=18522-16000=2522 $$

(A) is correct

(B)

Principal = 2800

Rate = 10% p.a.

Time = 18 months = 1 year + 6 months

Compounded annually:

Step 1 (1 year):

$$ 2800\times1.1=3080 $$

Step 2 (next 6 months → simple interest on 3080):

$$ SI=3080\times10\%\times\frac{1}{2}=154 $$

$$ Amount=3080+154=3234 $$

CI = 3234 - 2800 = 434

(B) is correct

✓ Final Answer:

3. Both (A) and (B)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.135Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (421, 18, NULL, NULL, 'How many triangles are there in the following figure?', NULL, '[{"text":"18","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"16","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"12","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"20","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Step 1: Small triangles

Count all smallest unit triangles:

• Top row: 4

• Bottom row: 4

Total small = 8
Step 2: Medium triangles

Formed by combining 2 small triangles:

• Top: 3

• Bottom: 3

Total = 6

Step 3: Larger triangles

• Across full width (top): 2

• Across full width (bottom): 2

Total = 4

Step 4: Total triangles:

Final Answer: 1.18', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q08-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 8', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.136Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q08-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 8","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (422, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Sonam ranks 18th from the top and 15th from the bottom in certain examinations. Determine how many students appeared for the examinations?', NULL, '[{"text":"33","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"34","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"32","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"31","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Use the formula:

Total students = (Rank from top) + (Rank from bottom) - 1

= 18 + 15 - 1 = 32

Final Answer: 3.32', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.136Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (423, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Which one among the following is a major relief feature in the Ocean floor?', NULL, '[{"text":"Mid-Oceanic Ridges","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Deep Sea Plain","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Seamount","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Submarine Canyons","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Hence, Deep Sea Plain They are the largest and most extensive topographic features on Earth, covering more area than any other ocean floor feature and representing the true ocean basin floor correct', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.136Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (424, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Who among the following awardees of the Ramon Magsaysay Award 2024 is a scholar who bridges tradition and modernity by promoting education, social entrepreneurship and culture preservation?', NULL, '[{"text":"Farhan, Farwiza","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Phuntsho, Karma","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Miyazaki Hayao","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nguyen Thi Ngoc Phuong","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The correct answer is:
2. Karma Phuntsho

He is a Bhutanese scholar and founder of the Loden Foundation, known for promoting education, social entrepreneurship, and preservation of Bhutanese culture, effectively bridging tradition and modernity.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.137Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (425, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Put the following religious teachers in chronological order beginning from the earliest to the latest:

(A) Thondaradippodi Azhwar in Tamil Nadu

(B) Nizamuddin Auliya in Delhi

(C) Basavanna in Karnataka

(D) Sri Chaitanya in Bengal', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (C), (B), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (C), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (B), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'To arrange them chronologically, note their approximate time periods:

• (A) Thondaradippodi Alvar - 8th-9th century CE

• (C) Basavanna - 12th century CE

• (B) Nizamuddin Auliya - 13th-14th century CE

• (D) Chaitanya Mahaprabhu - 15th-16th century CE

Correct chronological order (earliest $ \rightarrow $ latest):

(A) $ \rightarrow $ (C) $ \rightarrow $ (B) $ \rightarrow $ (D)

Correct answer: Option 1', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.137Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (426, 18, NULL, NULL, 'A and B can do a piece of work in 12 days. B and C together can do it in 15 days. If A is twice as good a workman as C, find the number of days in which B alone can do the work?', NULL, '[{"text":"10 days","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"20 days","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"5 days","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"12 days","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Let the daily work rates of A, B, and C be a, b, and c.

From the question:

$$ \bullet \quad a+b=\tfrac{1}{12} $$

$$ \bullet \quad b+c=\frac{1}{15} $$

$ \bullet $ a = 2c

Step 1: Substitute $ a = 2c $ into first equation

$$ 2c+b=\frac{1}{12} $$

Step 2: Use second equation

$$ b+c=\frac{1}{15} $$

Step 3: Subtract equations

$$ (2c+b)-(b+c)=\frac{1}{12}-\frac{1}{15} $$

$$ c=\frac{5-4}{60}=\frac{1}{60} $$

Step 4: Find b

$$ b+\frac{1}{60}=\frac{1}{15}=\frac{4}{60} $$

$$ b=\frac{3}{60}=\frac{1}{20} $$

Step 5: Time taken by B alone

$$ \mathrm{Time}=\frac{1}{b}=20\mathrm{days} $$

Correct answer: 20 days (Option 2)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.137Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (427, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Find out which of the answer figure completes the given matrix and will come in place of '' ? ''', NULL, '[{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q14-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 14', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.137Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q14-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 14","kind":"table"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q14-options.jpg","alt":"Printed answer choices for question 14","kind":"options"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (428, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (IV), (C) - (II), (D) - (I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (IV), (C) - (III), (D) - (I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (I), (C) - (IV), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The correct matches are:

• (A) World Trade Organization → (II) Geneva

• (B) International Finance Corporation → (IV) Washington D.C.

• (C) United Nations Development Programme → (I) New York

• (D) International Civil Aviation Organisation $ \rightarrow $ (III) Montreal

So the correct option is:

1. (A) - (II), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (III)', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q15-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 15', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.138Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q15-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 15","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (429, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the Odd One Out :', NULL, '[{"text":"Hypertension","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ulcer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Kidney","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Anaemia","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The odd one out is:

3. Kidney

Explanation:

• Hypertension, Ulcer, and Anaemia are diseases/medical conditions.

• Kidney is an organ, not a disease.

Hence, Kidney is the odd one out.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.138Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (430, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Rohit walks 30 m straight from his school towards the North, Then he turns left and walks 20 m. He turns left again and walks 10 m. Finally, he turns left and walks 20 m to reach point A. What is the shortest distance between his school and point A.', NULL, '[{"text":"10 m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"20 m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"30 m","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"5 m","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Let''s track Rohit''s movement step by step:

1. Starts at school → walks 30 m North

2. Turns left → walks 20 m West

3. Turns left → walks 10 m South

4. Turns left → walks 20 m East → reaches point A

Net displacement:

- North-South: 30 - 10 = 20 m North

- East-West: 20 m West and 20 m East cancel out → 0

So, Rohit is 20 m North of the starting point.

Shortest distance:

Straight-line distance = 20 m

Correct answer: 20 m (Option 2)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.138Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (431, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Which one among the following schemes was introduced by the Government of India with the objective of universal access to banking facilities, for all households across the country, through a bank branch, or a fixed point business correspondent within a reasonable distance?', NULL, '[{"text":"Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pradhan Mantri Vyay Vandana Yojana","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The correct answer is 4. Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana.

It was launched to provide universal access to banking facilities for households, including access through bank branches and business correspondents.

The others are for different purposes:

• Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana - loans for small businesses

• Pradhan Mantri Vaya Vandana Yojana - pension scheme for senior citizens

Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana - accident insurance

Answer: Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.139Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (432, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following States of India share land border with Bhutan?', NULL, '[{"text":"Tripura, Manipur and Mizoram","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Mizoram","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sikkim, Assam, Manipur","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sikkim, Assam, Arunachal Pradesh","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The correct answer is 4. Sikkim, Assam, Arunachal Pradesh.

India shares its border with Bhutan through these states:

• Sikkim

• West Bengal

• Assam

• Arunachal Pradesh

Among the given options, only Option 4 contains only states that border Bhutan. Answer: 4. Sikkim, Assam, Arunachal Pradesh', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.139Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (433, 18, NULL, NULL, 'If ROBUST is coded as QNATRS in a certain language, which word will be coded as ZXCMP?', NULL, '[{"text":"BZEOR","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"AYDNQ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"YWBLO","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"AWDLQ","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Observe the pattern:

ROBUST → QNATRS

Compare each letter:

- R → Q (-1)

- O → N (-1)

- B → A (-1)

- U → T (-1)

- S → R (-1)

- T → S (-1)

So, each letter is shifted one step backward in the alphabet.

Now reverse this logic for the question:

We need a word whose letters, when shifted -1, give ZXCMP.

So shift each letter of ZXCMP +1:

- Z → A

- X → Y

- C → D

- M → N

- P → Q

Thus, the original word is AYDNQ.

Correct answer: 2. AYDNQ', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.139Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (434, 18, NULL, NULL, 'If 3rd December 2000 was Sunday, what day was 3rd January 2001?', NULL, '[{"text":"Tuesday","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Monday","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Wednesday","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sunday","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'We are given:

• 3 December 2000 = Sunday

• Find the day on 3 January 2001

Step 1: Count days between the two dates

From Dec 3, 2000 → Jan 3, 2001 = 31 days

Step 2: Convert days into weeks

31 ÷ 7 = 4 weeks + 3 extra days

Step 3: Add 3 days to Sunday

• Sunday → Monday (1)

• Tuesday (2)

• Wednesday (3)

Final Answer:

Wednesday (Option 3)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.139Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (435, 18, NULL, NULL, 'The Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, which provided for reorganization of the erstwhile State of Jammu and Kashmir into two Union Territories - Jammu and Kashmir, and Ladakh was enacted in which year?', NULL, '[{"text":"2018","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2019","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2020","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2021","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The correct answer is 2. 2019.

The Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Act, 2019 was enacted in 2019, and it reorganized the former state into the two Union Territories of:

• Jammu and Kashmir

• Ladakh

Answer: 2019', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.140Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (436, 18, NULL, NULL, 'How many times in a continuous period of 24 hours, are the 2 hands of an ordinary clock at a right angle ?', NULL, '[{"text":"25 times","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"12 times","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"44 times","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"48 times","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Answer: C

In a 12-hour period, the hour and minute hands form a right angle 22 times.

So, in 24 hours:

$ 22 \times 2 = 44 $ times

Final Answer:

44 times (Option 3)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.140Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (437, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Amit and Pankaj are brothers. Rekha is the daughter of Kapil and sister of Amit. How is Pankaj''s mother related to Kapil.', NULL, '[{"text":"Sister","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Wife","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sister-in-law","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mother","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Let''s break it down:

• Amit and Pankaj are brothers $ \rightarrow $ they share the same parents.

• Rekha is daughter of Kapil and sister of Amit → so Amit is also Kapil''s child.

So, Kapil is the father of Pankaj.

• Since Pankaj is Amit''s brother → Pankaj is also Kapil''s son.

Therefore, Pankaj''s mother must be Kapil''s wife.

Final Answer: 2. Wife', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.140Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (438, 18, NULL, NULL, 'What is the period of rise of the Chalukyas in Karnataka and of the Pallavas in Tamil Nadu?', NULL, '[{"text":"500-600 CE","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"500-600 BCE","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"100-200 CE","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"100-200 BCE","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The correct answer is 1. 500-600 CE.

The Chalukyas in Karnataka and the Pallavas in Tamil Nadu rose to prominence in the early medieval period, around the 6th century CE.

Answer: 500-600 CE', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.141Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (439, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (I), (C) - (IV), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (I), (C) - (IV), (D) - (II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (I), (B) - (III), (C) - (IV), (D) - (II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Let''s match them correctly:

• (A) Ramsar Site → (III) Renuka Lake (a well-known Ramsar wetland)

• (B) Biosphere Reserve → (I) Manas (Manas Biosphere Reserve)

• (C) Elephant Reserve → (IV) Wayanad (part of Nilgiri Elephant Reserve region)

• (D) Tiger Reserve → (II) Orang (Orang National Park is a Tiger Reserve)

Correct matching:

(A) - (III), (B) - (I), (C) - (IV), (D) - (II)

Correct answer: Option 2', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q27-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 27', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.141Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q27-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 27","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (440, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Put the following Viceroys of India in chronological order beginning from the earliest to the latest?

(A) Lord Minto II

(B) Sir John Lawrence

(C) Lord Wavell

(D) Lord Linlithgow', NULL, '[{"text":"(B), (C), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (B), (A), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Let''s arrange them by their tenure as Viceroy of India:

(B) John Lawrence - 1864-1869

