Correct answer: Option 3', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q48-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 48', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.155Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-1/q48-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 48","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (461, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the odd one out :', NULL, '[{"text":"Jayanta Talukdar","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Aman Saini","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Anshu Malik","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dola Banerjee","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Hence, Option 3: Anshu Malik Jayanta Talukdar, Aman Saini, and Dola Banerjee are all associated with archery, while Anshu Malik is a wrestler, making her the odd one out correct', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.155Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (462, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Banda, a major city in Uttar Pradesh, is located on the banks of which one of the following rivers?', NULL, '[{"text":"Betwa","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ken","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Son","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Tapti","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The correct answer is 2. Ken.

Banda in Uttar Pradesh is situated on the banks of the Ken River.

Answer: Ken', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.156Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (463, 18, NULL, 60, '(A) and (D) are incorrect but (B) and (C) are correct', NULL, '[{"text":"1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Given:

• B is the son of C, but C is not the mother → C is father → C = male

• A and C are married $ \rightarrow $ A = female

• E is the brother of C $ \rightarrow $ E = male

• D is the daughter of A $ \rightarrow $ D = female

• F is the brother of B $ \rightarrow $ F = male

Children of A and C:

B(son)

• D (daughter)

• F (son)

So, A has 3 children.

Now evaluate statements:

(A) There are only three male members

Males: C, E, B, F $ \rightarrow $ 4 males ✗ (False)

(B) A has only three children

B, D, F $ \rightarrow $ 3 children ✓ (True)

(C) A and D are both females

A (wife), D (daughter) $ \rightarrow $ True ✓

(D) D is a female but A is not a female

A is female $ \rightarrow $ False ✗

Final Answer:

4. (A) and (D) are incorrect but (B) and (C)

4. (A) and (D) are incorrect but (B) and (C) are correct', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.159Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (464, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) - (I), (B) - (II), (C) - (III), (D) - (IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (III), (C) - (IV), (D) - (I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (IV), (B) - (I), (C) - (II), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '(A) $ \frac{1}{6!} + \frac{1}{7!} = \frac{x}{8!} $

$$ \frac{1}{6!}=\frac{1}{720},\quad\frac{1}{7!}=\frac{1}{5040} $$

$$ LCM=5040\Rightarrow\frac{7+1}{5040}=\frac{8}{5040}=\frac{1}{630} $$

Now,

$$ \frac{x}{8!}=\frac{x}{40320}=\frac{1}{630}\Rightarrow x=\frac{40320}{630}=64 $$

(A) $ \rightarrow $ (III) 64

(B) $ \frac{n!}{(n-r)!} $, n = 6, r = 2

$$ \frac{6!}{4!}=6\times5=30 $$

(B) $ \rightarrow $ (IV) 30

(C) $ \mathrm{f}f^{n}C_{9}=^{n}C_{8} $

Property:

$$ {}^{n}C_{r}={}^{n}C_{n-r} $$

So,

$$ 9=n-8\Rightarrow n=17 $$

$$ ^{17}C_{17}=1 $$

(C) $ \rightarrow(1) $ 1

(D) $ ^{6}P_{3}-^{5}P_{2} $

$$ ^{6}P_{3}=6\times5\times4=120 $$

$$ ^{5}P_{2}=5\times4=20 $$

$$ 120-20=100 $$

(D) $ \rightarrow $ (II) 100

Final Matching:

(A) $ \rightarrow $ (III)

(B) $ \rightarrow $ (IV)

(C) $ \rightarrow $ (I)

(D) $ \rightarrow $ (II)

Correct Answer: 3. (A) - (III), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (II)', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-2/q01-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 1', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.159Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-2/q01-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 1","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (465, 18, NULL, NULL, 'If HOME is coded as 815135. How can ROAD be written as?', NULL, '[{"text":"810034","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"181514","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"351518","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"510035","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given: HOME → 815135

Break it letter-wise using positions in the alphabet:

- $ H = 8 $

- $ O = 15 $

- $ M = 13 $

- $ E = 5 $

So, HOME = 8 15 13 5 → 815135

Now apply the same rule to ROAD:

- R = 18

- O = 15

- A = 1

- D = 4

So, ROAD = 18 15 14 → 181514

Correct Answer: 2.181514', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.161Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (466, 18, NULL, NULL, 'If J is the sister of K. K is the sister of L. L is the sister of M. M is the brother of N. Then which of the following statements is not necessary true?

(A) K and L are sisters.

(B) M and N are brothers.

(C) L is sister of N.

(D) J, K, L are females and M is male.', NULL, '[{"text":"(B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given:

• J is sister of K → J = female

• K is sister of L → K = female → L can be male or female

• L is sister of M → L = female → M can be male or female

• M is brother of $ N \to M = \text{male} \to N $ can be male or female

Now check statements:

(A) K and L are sisters

• K = female, L = female

✓ True (necessary)

(B) M and N are brothers

- M is male, but N''s gender is not given

✗ Not necessarily true

(C) L is sister of N

- L is sister of M, and M is brother of N → they are siblings

- L is female $ \rightarrow $ sister of N

✓ True (necessary)

(D) J, K, L are females and M is male

J, K, L = females ✓

• M = male ✓

✓ True (necessary)

Final Answer:

Only (B) is not necessarily true.

Correct Answer: 2. (B) only', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.162Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (467, 18, NULL, NULL, 'If day before yesterday was Friday, then what will be the Tuesday?', NULL, '[{"text":"A day after tomorrow","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"tomorrow","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"today","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 3^{rd} $ day after today","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Let''s solve step by step:

- Day before yesterday = Friday

- So, yesterday = Saturday

• Therefore, today = Sunday

Now find Tuesday relative to today (Sunday):

• Monday → 1 day after today

Tuesday → 2 days after today

This is same as "day after tomorrow"

Correct Answer: 1. A day after tomorrow', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.163Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (468, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Six friends, A, B, C, D, E and F are sitting in a row facing towards East. E and F are in the center, and A and B are at the ends. C is sitting on the left of A. Then match List-I with List-II', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) - (IV), (B) - (II), (C) - (I), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (II), (C) - (I), (D) - (IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (III), (B) - (I), (C) - (II), (D) - (IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) - (IV), (B) - (I), (C) - (II), (D) - (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given:

• 6 people: A, B, C, D, E, F

• Facing East (so right = forward direction → your right side is actual right)

• E and F are in the center → positions 3 & 4

• A and B are at the ends → positions 1 & 6

- C is on the left of A

Step 1: Place A and B

Positions: _ Ends → A and B

If A is at position 1, then C cannot be left of A $ \times $ So, A must be at position 6, and B at position 1

Step 2: Place C

C is to the left of A (pos 6) $ \rightarrow $ so C is at pos 5

Step 3: Place E and F (center)

Positions 3 & 4 $ \rightarrow $ E and F

Step 4: Remaining position

Only position 2 left $ \rightarrow $ D

Final arrangement:

B D E/F F/E C A

Now answer:

(A) People to the right of D (pos 2)

→ positions 3,4,5,6 → 4 people → (III)

(B) Who is on the right of B (pos 1)

→ position 2 → D → (II)

(C) Immediate left of C (pos 5)

→ position 4 $ \rightarrow $ F $ \rightarrow $ (I)

(D) People to the left of E (pos 3 or 4)

• If E at 3 → left = 2 people

• If E at $4 \rightarrow$ left = 3 people

But only matching option is $2 \rightarrow$ (IV)

Final Matching:

(A) $ \rightarrow $ (III)

(B) $ \rightarrow $ (II)

(C) $ \rightarrow $(I)

(D) $ \rightarrow $ (IV)

Correct Answer: 2. (A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)', NULL, NULL, 2025, '/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-2/q08-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 8', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.164Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/general-test-2025-05-20-shift-2/q08-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 8","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (469, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following major advances in Indian Epigraphy in chronological order, beginning with the earliest to the most recent.

(A) Alexander Cunningham published a set of Ashokan inscriptions

(B) James Pinsep decipherers Ashokan Brahmi

(C) First issue of Epigraphia Indica

(D) First issue of Epigraphia Carnatica', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B), (C), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (C), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (A), (D), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Key years:

Key words:
• (B) James Prinsep deciphered Brahmi $ \rightarrow $ 1837
• (A) Cunningham published Ashokan inscriptions $ \rightarrow $ 1870s
• (C) First issue of Epigraphia Indica $ \rightarrow $ 1888
• (D) First issue of Epigraphia Carnatica $ \rightarrow $ 1894
Chronological order:
(B) $ \rightarrow $ (A) $ \rightarrow $ (C) $ \rightarrow $ (D)
Correct Answer: 3. (B), (A), (C), (D)', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.165Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (470, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Which one of the following is $ \underline{\text{NOT}} $ an example of "In Situ" biodiversity conservation efforts in India?', NULL, '[{"text":"Botanical Garden","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"National Park","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Wildlife Sanctuaries","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Biosphere Reserve","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '1. Botanical Garden

Why:

• In situ conservation = protecting species in their natural habitat

Examples: National Park, Wildlife Sanctuary, Biosphere Reserve

• Botanical Garden is ex situ conservation, because plants are conserved outside their natural habitat.

Correct Answer: 1. Botanical Garden', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.166Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (471, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Point A (4, 2) divides segment BC in the ratio 2:5. Coordinates of B and C are (2,6), (9,y) respectively. Find the value of y.', NULL, '[{"text":"6","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"6","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"8","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"8","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Use section formula (internal division):

$$ A=\left(\frac{2x_{2}+5x_{1}}{2+5},\frac{2y_{2}+5y_{1}}{2+5}\right) $$

Here,

$ B(2,6) = (x_1, y_1) $

$ C(9,y)=(x_2,y_2) $

Ratio = 2:5

$ A = (4, 2) $

For x-coordinate:

$$ 4=\frac{2(9)+5(2)}{7}=\frac{18+10}{7}=\frac{28}{7}=4\checkmark $$

For y-coordinate:

$$ 2=\frac{2(y)+5(6)}{7} $$

$$ 2=\frac{2y+30}{7} $$

14=2y+30

2y = -16 $ \Rightarrow $ y = -8

Correct Answer: 4. -8', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.167Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (472, 18, NULL, NULL, 'Megha is fifth from the left end and Priya is tenth from the right end in a row of girls. If there are nine girls between

Megha and Priya, how many girls are there in the rows?', NULL, '[{"text":"26","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"25","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"24","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"23","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Let total girls = N

- Priya is 10th from right → position from left = N - 9

Given: 9 girls between them

N-14=10\Rightarrow N=24

Correct Answer: 3.24', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.168Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
