(C) The population is either stable or grows slowly

(D) The net addition to the population is high.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Fertility remains high in the beginning of second stage but it declines with time. This is accompanied by reduced mortality rate. Improvements in sanitation and health conditions lead to decline in mortality. Because of this gap the net addition to population is high.', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.260Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
