the x-axis and the lines x = 2 and x = 4 is

$$ 2^{\frac{3}{2}} $$', NULL, '[{"text":"1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.412Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (849, 3, NULL, NULL, 'In a college, 30% students fail in Physics, 25% fail in Mathematics and 10% fail in both.

One student is chosen at random. The probability that she fails in Physics if she has failed in Mathematics is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{2}{5} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{5} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{9}{10} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{3}{10} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Conditional Probability

Let P be the event that a student fails in Physics, and M be the event that a student fails in Mathematics.

1. Given Probabilities

$$ P(P)=30\%=0.30 $$

$$ P(M)=25\%=0.25 $$

$$ P(P\cap M)=10\%=0.10\quad(\mathrm{F a i l i n g~i n~b o t h}) $$
2. Conditional Probability Formula

We need to find the probability that she fails in Physics given she has failed in Mathematics, which is $ P(P|M) $.

$$ P(P|M)=\frac{P(P\cap M)}{P(M)} $$

3. Calculation

Substitute the given values:

$$ P(P|M)=\frac{0.10}{0.25}=\frac{10}{25} $$

Simplify the fraction:

$$ P(P|M)=\frac{2}{5} $$

[The correct option is 1.]', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.413Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (850, 3, NULL, NULL, 'An urn contains 5 red and 5 black balls. A ball is drawn at random, its color is noted and is returned to Moreover, 2 additional balls of the same color are put in the urn and then a ball is drawn at random.

The probability that the second drawn ball is red, is:

$$ \begin{aligned}&1.\frac{5}{12}\\ &2.\frac{1}{2}\\ &3.\frac{1}{3}\\ &4.\frac{1}{4}\\ \end{aligned} $$', NULL, '[{"text":"1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.414Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (851, 3, NULL, NULL, 'If A(3, 2), B(1, -1) and C(2, 1) are three vertices of a parallelogram ABCD, then its area (in sq. units) i

1. 1

2. $ \frac{1}{2} $

3. 5

4. $ \frac{5}{2} $', NULL, '[{"text":"(B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) and (B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Urn Problem: Probability of Second Ball being Red

Let $ R_{1} $ be the event that the first ball drawn is red, and $ B_{1} $ be the event that the first ball drawn is black.

$$ R_{2} $$

We want to find $P(R_{2})$.

1. Initial Probabilities and Conditions

Initial Urn: 5 Red (R), 5 Black (B). Total = 10 balls.

$$ P(R_{1})=\frac{5}{10}=\frac{1}{2} $$

$$ P(B_{1})=\frac{5}{10}=\frac{1}{2} $$

The ball is returned, and 2 additional balls of the same color are added.

2. Conditional Probabilities fo

We use the Law of Total Probability: $ P(R_2) = P(R_2|R_1)P(R_1) + P(R_2|B_1)P(B_1) $

Case 1: $ R_{1} $ occurs (First ball is Red)

The red ball is returned, and 2 additional red balls are added.

New Urn: $ 5+2=7 $ R, 5 B. Total = 12 balls.

$$ P(R_{2}|R_{1})=\frac{7}{12} $$

Case 2: $ B_{1} $ occurs (First ball is Black)

The black ball is returned, and 2 additional black balls are added.

New Urn: 5 R, $ 5 + 2 = 7 $ B. Total = 12 balls.

$$ P(R_{2}|B_{1})=\frac{5}{12} $$

3. Calculate $ P(R_{2}) $

$$ P(R_{2})=P(R_{2}|R_{1})P(R_{1})+P(R_{2}|B_{1})P(B_{1}) $$

$$ P(R_{2})=\left(\frac{7}{12}\right)\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)+\left(\frac{5}{12}\right)\left(\frac{1}{2}\right) $$

$$ P(R_{2})=\frac{1}{2}\bigg(\frac{7}{12}+\frac{5}{12}\bigg) $$

$$ P(R_{2})=\frac{1}{2}\bigg(\frac{12}{12}\bigg) $$

$$ P(R_{2})=\frac{1}{2}(1) $$

$$ P(R_{2})=\frac{1}{2} $$

[The correct option is 2.]

Which of the following statements are true?

(A) If $ \vec{r} = x\vec{i} + y\vec{j} + z\vec{k} $, then $ x, y, z $ are called direction ratios of $ \vec{r} $.

(B) For any two vectors $ \vec{a} $ and $ \vec{b} $, $ \vec{a} + \vec{b} = \vec{b} + \vec{a} $.

(C) $ \vec{a} \perp \vec{b} $ if and only if $ \vec{a} \times \vec{b} = \vec{0} $.

(D) Projection of $ \vec{b} $ on $ \vec{a} $ is $ \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{a}|^2} $.

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:

1. (B) and (C) only

2. (B), (C) and (D) only

3. (C) and (D) only

4. (A) and (B) only
Options:

A. 1

B. 2

C. 3

D. 4
Solution:

True Statements about Vectors

1. Analysis of Statements

(A) If $ \vec{r} - x\vec{i} + y\vec{j} + z\vec{k} $, then x, y, z are called direction ratios of $ \vec{r} $.

This is TRUE. The components of a vector are its direction ratios.

(B) For any two vectors $ \vec{a} $ and $ \vec{b} $, $ \vec{a} + \vec{b} - \vec{b} + \vec{a} $.

This is TRUE. Vector addition is commutative.

(C) $ \vec{a} \perp \vec{b} $ if and only if $ \vec{a} \times \vec{b} - \vec{0} $.

This is FALSE.

$ \vec{a} \perp \vec{b} $ if and only if $ \vec{a} \cdot \vec{b} = 0 $.

$ \vec{a} \times \vec{b} - \vec{0} $ if and only if $ \vec{a} $ and $ \vec{b} $ are parallel ( $ \vec{a} \parallel \vec{b} $).

(D) Projection of $ \vec{b} $ on $ \vec{a} $ is $ \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{a}|^2} $.

This is FALSE.

The scalar projection (component) of $ \vec{b} $ on $ \vec{a} $ is $ \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{a}|} $.

The vector projection of $ \vec{b} $ on $ \vec{a} $ is $ \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{a}|^2} $.

2. Conclusion

The only correct statements are (A) and (B).

[The correct option is 4.]', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.415Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (852, 3, NULL, NULL, 'If $ A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 3 & 1 \end{bmatrix} $ and $ A^{4} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ k & 1 \end{bmatrix} $, then the value of k is:', NULL, '[{"text":"81","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"27","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"12","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"36","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'We are given a matrix A and its fourth power $ A^{4} $:

$$ A=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 3&1\end{pmatrix}\quad and\quad A^{4}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ k&1\end{pmatrix} $$

The task is to find the value of the constant k.

Matrix Powers Calculation

We calculate the powers of A to identify a pattern for $ A^{n} $.

Calculate $ A^{2} $

$$ \boldsymbol{A}^{2}=\boldsymbol{A}\cdot\boldsymbol{A}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 3&1\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 3&1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1\cdot1+0\cdot3&1\cdot0+0\cdot1\\ 3\cdot1+1\cdot3&3\cdot0+1\cdot1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 6&1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 2\cdot3&1\end{pmatrix} $$

Calculate $ A^{3} $

$$ \boldsymbol{A}^{3}=\boldsymbol{A}^{2}\cdot\boldsymbol{A}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 6&1\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 3&1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1\cdot1+0\cdot3&1\cdot0+0\cdot1\\ 6\cdot1+1\cdot3&6\cdot0+1\cdot1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 9&1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 3\cdot3&1\end{pmatrix} $$

General Pattern

Observing the results, we deduce the general form for the n-th power of A:

$$ \boldsymbol{A}^{n}=\begin{pmatrix}{{{1}}}&{{{0}}} \\{{{n\cdot3}}}&{{{1}}}\end{pmatrix} $$

Finding the Value of k

Using the pattern for n = 4:

$$ \boldsymbol{A}^{4}=\begin{pmatrix}{{{1}}}&{{{0}}} \\{{{4\cdot3}}}&{{{1}}}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}{{{1}}}&{{{0}}} \\{{{12}}}&{{{1}}}\end{pmatrix} $$

Comparing this result with the given expression for $ A^{4} $:

$$ \begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ 12&1\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\ k&1\end{pmatrix} $$

By matrix equality, the corresponding elements must be equal:

k=12

Conclusion

[The correct option is 3.]', NULL, NULL, 2025, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:38.416Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
