The embryo sac is also known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"megaspore","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"female gametophyte","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"megasporophyll","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"megagamete","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Embryo sac is also known as the female gametophyte or megagametophyte.

Sol. There are two layers in the seed coat - (i) outer layer (testa) that is usually hard and develops from the outer integument and (ii) the inner layer (tegmen) which forms from the inner integument when it becomes thin and papery.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q43-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 43', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.650Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q43-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2136, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Answer the question from the diagram of typical anatropous ovule

Testa of a seed is produced from:', NULL, '[{"text":"ovary wall","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"hilum","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"outer integument of ovule","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"funicle","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The pollen tube enters the embryo sac through micropylar end.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 44', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.651Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2137, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Answer the question from the diagram of typical anatropous ovule

Identify the diploid cells present in the ovule:

(A) Outer integument

(B) Antipodal

(C) Nucellus

(D) Synergids', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B), only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C), only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (D), only Direction for the question 46 to 50: Read the given paragraph and answer the given question. Nearly all plants cannot maintain a constant internal environment. Their body temperature changes with the ambient temperature. In aquatic animals, the osmotic concentration of the body fluids changes with that of the ambient air, water osmotic concentration. These animals and plants are simply conformers. Considering the benefits of a constant internal environment to the organism, we must ask why these conformers had not evolved to become regulators. Recall the human analogy we used above; much as they like, how many people can really afford an air conditioner? Many simply ''sweat it out'' and resign themselves to suboptimal performance in hot summer months. Very small animals are rarely found in polar regions. During the course of evolution, the costs and benefits of maintaining a constant internal environment are taken into consideration. Some species have evolved the ability to regulate, but only over a limited range of environmental conditions, beyond which they simply conform. If the stressful external conditions are localised or remain only for a short duration, the organism has other alternatives for survival.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Nucellus forms a major part of the ovule and consists of a diploid layer of cells that surrounds the embryo sac. It provides nutrition to the embryo. The nucellus is part of the sporophyte and the ploidy is 2n. The ploidy of outer integument is 2n.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q45-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 45', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.651Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q45-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 45","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2138, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Conformers are the animals whose:', NULL, '[{"text":"Body temperature remains constant.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Body temperature is higher than the ambient temperature.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Body temperature is lower than the ambient temperature.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Body temperature changes with the ambient temperature.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Conformers are animals are also known as ectotherms, as they cannot regulate their own internal temperature. It adapts its behaviour to the surroundings or migrates to environments with optimal temperatures. Conformers are referred to as cold-blooded animals. Examples of this class are amphibians, reptiles, insects etc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.652Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2139, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the conformer from the following:', NULL, '[{"text":"Elephant","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Shrew","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Human","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dog","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Small animals like shrews and hummingbirds are conformers and are not able to maintain a constant internal environment. This is because they have a large surface area compared to their volume and loss or gain of heat is a function of the surface area of an organism.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.652Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2140, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Very small animals are rarely found in polar regions because they:', NULL, '[{"text":"Cannot tolerate very low temperature.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lose body heat very fast because of a larger surface area relative to their volume.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lose body heat slowly because of a larger surface area relative to their volume.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lose body heat very fast because of a smaller surface area relative to their volume.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Since small animals have a larger surface area relative to their volume, they tend to lose body heat very fast when it is cold outside; then they have to expend much energy to generate body heat through metabolism. This is the main reason why very small animals are rarely found in polar regions.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.653Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2141, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the animals for which thermoregulation is comparatively an energetically expensive process:', NULL, '[{"text":"Humming birds and fishes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Shrews and frogs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Frogs and fishes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Humming birds and shrews","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Thermoregulation is energetically expensive for many organisms particularly small animals like shrews and humming birds.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.653Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2142, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Why is it that most of the animals (99%) evolved are not able to maintain their body temperature?', NULL, '[{"text":"Thermoregulation is a useless process","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thermoregulation is a useful process","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thermoregulation is energetically expensive process","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thermoregulation is energetically frugal process.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Majority of animals cannot maintain a constant internal temperature. Their body temperature changes with ambient temperature. Thermoregulation is energetically expensive for many organisms.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.654Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2143, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The probability of having a haemophilia carrier daughter by a haemophilia carrier mother and a normal father is:', NULL, '[{"text":"100%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"50%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"25%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"75%","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The haemophilia is a sex-linked recessive disease which shows its transmission from an unaffected female carrier to some of the male progeny. In this disease, a single protein that is a part of the cascade of proteins involved in the coagulation of blood is affected. As a result of this, in an infected individual, a simple cut will result in non-stop bleeding. The heterozygous female carrier for haemophilia may transfer the disease to sons. The probability of the female becoming haemophilic is very rare because the mother of such a female has to be at least a carrier while the father should be haemophilic. It is an inherited genetic disorder which results in the deterioration of the formation of a blood clot. In a condition, where the father is normal and the mother is the carrier of haemophilia disease, then the female offspring that are produced may be normal or the carrier of the disease.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.655Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2144, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the stages of oogenesis in order of their occurrence.

(A) Formation of ovum & II $ ^{nd} $ polar body

(B) Meiosis II begins but held at Metaphase II

(C) Meiosis I started but held at Prophase I

(D) Formation of primary oocyte from oogonia

(E) Completion of Meiosis-I and formation of secondary oocyte and first polar body', NULL, '[{"text":"(D), (C), (B), (E), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (E), (D), (A), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D), (C), (E), (B), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D), (C), (A), (E), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Oogonia cells start division and enter into prophase-I of the meiotic division and get temporarily arrested at that stage, called primary oocytes. Each primary oocyte then gets surrounded by a layer of granulosa cells and is called the primary follicle. A large number of these follicles degenerate during the phase from birth to puberty. Therefore, at puberty only 60,000-80,000 primary follicles are left in each ovary. The primary follicles get surrounded by more layers of granulosa cells and a new theca and are called secondary follicles. The secondary follicle soon transforms into a tertiary follicle which is characterised by a fluid filled cavity called antrum. The theca layer is organised into an inner theca interna and an outer theca externa. It is important to draw your attention that it is at this stage that the primary oocyte within the tertiary follicle grows in size and completes its first meiotic division. It is an unequal division resulting in the formation of a large haploid secondary oocyte and a tiny first polar body. During fertilization, the secretions of the acrosome help the sperm enter into the cytoplasm of the ovum through the zona pellucida and the plasma membrane. This induces the completion of the meiotic division of the secondary oocyte. The second meiotic division is also unequal and results in the formation of a second polar body and a haploid ovum (ootid).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.655Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2145, 6, NULL, NULL, 'A mature embryo sac of an angiosperm is:', NULL, '[{"text":"7 nucleate, 7 celled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"8 nucleate, 7 celled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"6 nucleate; 7 celled","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4 nucleate, 7 celled","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'a typical angiosperm embryo sac, at maturity, though 8-nucleate is 7-celled.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.656Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2146, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Who proposed the concept ''saltation'' in evolution?', NULL, '[{"text":"Thomas Malthus","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Charles Darwin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hugo deVries","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ernst Haeckel","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Evolution for Darwin was gradual while deVries believed mutation caused speciation and hence called it saltation (single step large mutation).

Sol. Primary treatment of sewage involves filtration and sedimentation. All solids that settle form the primary sludge, and the supernatant forms the effluent. The effluent from the primary settling tank is taken for secondary treatment. The primary effluent is passed into large aeration tanks where it is constantly agitated mechanically and air is pumped into it. This allows vigorous growth of useful aerobic microbes into flocs. Once the BOD of sewage or waste water is reduced significantly, the effluent is then passed into a settling tank where the bacterial ''flocs'' are allowed to sediment. This sediment is called activated sludge.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.656Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2147, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following steps of sewage treatment in a sequential order.

(A) Primary effluent passed in aeration tank

(B) Activated sludge is formed

(C) Filtration and sedimentation of sewage

(D) Aerobic microbes grow into flocs', NULL, '[{"text":"(D), (C), (A), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (D), (C), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (A), (D), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (D), (B), (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.657Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2148, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The finches found on Galapagos Islands were originally _.', NULL, '[{"text":"Insectivores","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Fruit eaters","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Fish eaters","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Seed eaters","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'During his journey Darwin went to Galapagos Islands. There he observed an amazing diversity of creatures. Of particular interest, small black birds later called Darwin''s Finches amazed him. He realised that there were many varieties of finches in the same island. All the varieties, he conjectured, evolved on the island itself. From the original seed-eating features, many other forms with altered beaks arose, enabling them to become insectivorous and vegetarian finches.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.657Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2149, 6, NULL, NULL, '''Hisardale'' a new breed of sheep developed in Punjab by:', NULL, '[{"text":"In-breeding","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Out-crossing","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cross-breeding","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Out-breeding","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Hisardale is a new breed of sheep developed in Punjab by crossing Bikaneri ewes and Marino rams.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.657Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2150, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is an example of auto-immune disease?', NULL, '[{"text":"Rheumatoid arthritis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Malaria","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Elephantiasis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amoebiasis","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Rheumatoid arthritis which affects many people in our society is an auto-immune disease.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.658Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2151, 6, NULL, NULL, 'If the solar energy available to a particular ecosystem is 1,000,000 J. What will be the energy available at $ 2^{nd} $ trophic level in the food chain?', NULL, '[{"text":"100 kJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"10 kJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1 kJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.1 kJ","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In a food chain of an ecosystem, 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level which is also called the 10% rule of energy transfer. So, if there is 1000000 J of sunlight then the first trophic level will be having 100000 J and the second trophic level will have 10000 J, that is 10 kJ of energy.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.658Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2152, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The Verhulst - Pearl Logistic Growth of population is characterised by:', NULL, '[{"text":"Straight line curve","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sigmoid curve","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"J-shaped curve","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"L-shaped curve","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Logistic growth is the population growth curve represented by the equation $ dN/dt = rN $ (1 - N/K), it is sigmoid.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.658Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2153, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The method of producing thousands of plants through tissue culture is called micro-propagation. Each of these plants will be genetically identical to the original plant from which they were grown, i.e., they are somaclones. Even if the plant is infected with a virus, the meristem (apical and axillary) is free of virus. Pomato is a somatic hybrid. The capacity to generate a whole plant from any cell/explant is called totipotency.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q11-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 11', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.659Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q11-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 11","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2154, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The ligation of alien DNA in pBR322 is carried out at a restriction site present in one of the two antibiotic resistance genes (amp $ ^{R} $ and tet $ ^{R} $). The tumor inducing (Ti) plasmid of Agrobacterium tumifaciens has now been modified into a cloning vector which is no more pathogenic to the plants but is still able to use the mechanisms to deliver genes of our interest into a variety of plants. Nowadays the most commonly used matrix is agarose which is a natural polymer extracted from sea weeds.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q12-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 12', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.659Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q12-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 12","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2155, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Use of biofertilizers as a nutrient source is a practised in _.', NULL, '[{"text":"Inorganic farming","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Animal husbandry","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Organic farming","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Crop rotation","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Natural manures, compost, and bio-fertilizers are used in organic farming by farmers.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.660Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2156, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Examples of Ex-situ conservation are:

(A) Botanical gardens

(B) Sacred grooves

(C) Hot spots

(D) Zoological parks', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) and (B) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Botanical gardens, zoological parks, seed banks, cryopreservation, field gene banks are ex-situ methods of conserving biodiversity. Hot spots and sacred grooves are in-situ methods.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.661Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2157, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The gene controlling the ABO blood groups in humans is:', NULL, '[{"text":"A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"O","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'ABO blood groups are controlled by the gene I gene in humans.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.662Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2158, 6, NULL, NULL, '''Barnacles'' growing on the back of whale is a classical example of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Mutualism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Predation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amensalism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Commensalism","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Commensalism is the interaction in which one species benefits and the other is neither harmed nor benefited. An orchid growing as an epiphyte on a mango branch, and barnacles growing on the back of a whale benefit while neither the mango tree nor the whale derives any apparent benefit.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.663Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2159, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the statements which hold true for transgenic animals.

(A) Transgenic animals can be used to study vaccine safety.

(B) Over 95% of transgenic animals are mice

(C) Transgenic animals cannot be used to study human diseases

(D) Transgenic animal possesses and express foreign gene', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Many transgenic animals are designed to increase our understanding of how genes contribute to the development of disease. These are specially made to serve as models for human diseases so that investigation of new treatments for diseases is made possible. Today transgenic models exist for many human diseases such as cancer, cystic fibrosis, rheumatoid arthritis and Alzheimer''s.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.664Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2160, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Select the properties of cancer cell

(A) Forms benign tumors

(B) Causes very little damage to the surrounding tissues

(C) Can show Metastasis

(D) Lacks contact inhibition', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'In our body, cell growth and differentiation is highly controlled and regulated. In cancer cells, there is breakdown of these regulatory mechanisms. Normal cells show a property called contact inhibition by virtue of which contact with other cells inhibits their uncontrolled growth. Cancer cells appears to have lost this property. Tumors are of two types, namely the Benign tumors that normally remain confined to their original location and do not spread to other parts of the body and cause little damage and malignant tumors that show metastasis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.665Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2161, 6, NULL, NULL, 'In plants, continued self-pollination results in', NULL, '[{"text":"Outcrossing","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Inbreeding depression","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Self-incompatibility","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Male sterility","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Continued self-pollination result in inbreeding depression. So flowering plants developed following devices to discourage self-pollination and to encourage cross-pollination.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.665Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2162, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The first clinical gene therapy was given to treat:', NULL, '[{"text":"Thalassemia","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Haemophilia","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Adenosine deaminase deficiency","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Turner''s Syndrome","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl with adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.666Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2163, 6, NULL, NULL, 'In biolistic method, the cells are bombarded with high velocity microparticles of:', NULL, '[{"text":"DNA coated with gold or tungsten","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gold or tungsten coated with DNA","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Platinum or copper coated with DNA","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Copper or iron coated with DNA","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In another method, suitable for plants, cells are bombarded with high velocity micro-particles of gold or tungsten coated with DNA in a method known as biolistics or gene gun', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.667Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2164, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following does not show parthenogenesis?', NULL, '[{"text":"Honeybees","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Turkey","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rotifers","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Snakes","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'some organisms like rotifers, honeybees and even some lizards and birds (turkey), the female gamete undergoes development to form new organisms without fertilisation. This phenomenon is called parthenogenesis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.668Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2165, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Wings of an insect and wings of a bird are:', NULL, '[{"text":"Homologous organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Analogous organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Vestigial organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Over specialised organs","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The wings of a bird and insects are analogous structures, they represent convergent evolution.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.668Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2166, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Snow-blindness happens when a person is exposed to _.', NULL, '[{"text":"Extreme cold","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Snow blizzard","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"High UV-B dose","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"X-rays","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'In human eye, cornea absorbs UV-B radiation, and a high dose of UV-B causes inflammation of cornea, called snow-blindness, cataract, etc. Such exposure may permanently damage the cornea.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.669Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2167, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Down''s Syndrome is due to the presence of an additional copy of the chromosome number 21 (trisomy of 21). Turner''s Syndrome is caused due to the absence of one of the X chromosomes, i.e., 45 with X0. Phenylketonuria is an in-born error of metabolism. Thalassemia is an autosome-linked recessive blood disease transmitted from parents to the offspring when both the partners are unaffected carrier for the gene.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q25-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 25', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.670Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q25-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 25","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2168, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'adventitious buds arise from the notches present at margins of leaves of Bryophyllum. This ability is fully exploited by gardeners and farmers for commercial propagation of plants, ginger propagates through rhizome, water hyacinth by offset and agave by bulbuls.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q26-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 26', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.671Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q26-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 26","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2169, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which enzyme is used as a clot buster''?', NULL, '[{"text":"Staphylokinase","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Glucokinase","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Streptokinase","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Protease","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Streptokinase produced by the bacterium Streptococcus and modified by genetic engineering is used as a ''clot buster'' for removing clots from the blood vessels of patients who have undergone myocardial infarction leading to heart attack.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.672Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2170, 6, NULL, NULL, 'A double stranded DNA fragment has 500 Adenine bases. If total number of base pairs in this fragment is 2500, then what will be the number of guanine bases?', NULL, '[{"text":"500","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"750","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1000","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2000","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'According to Chargaff''s law, Adenine = 500 bases,

$ A + T = G + C $

$ A + T = 500 + 500 = 1000 $

Guanine bases = 2500 - 1000 = 1500, G = C = 750', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.672Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2171, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following steps of rDNA technology in correct sequence.

(A) Amplification of gene by PCR

(B) Insertion of rDNA into host cell using vector

(C) Isolation of the genetic material from the cell

(D) Cutting the DNA at specific location', NULL, '[{"text":"(C), (D), (B), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (D), (A), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D), (C), (A), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C), (D), (B)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'DNA containing the gene of interest is identified and isolated from the organism.

The gene of interest is inserted into the plasmid which is a vector which is used to deliver and maintain the DNA in the host organism. This is known as recombinant DNA or rDNA.

The rDNA is now introduced into the host and the process is known as transformation.

The host cells that have taken up the rDNA are known as transformed cells. These cells need to be differentiated from the other cells that have not taken up the rDNA. Here, growing the mixture of cells in an antibiotic-containing medium helps in the selection and identification of the transformants from the non-transformants. The various selectable markers also play an important role in identifying the recombinants from the non-recombinants.

The rDNA containing the gene of interest expresses itself by producing a protein and this is known as the expression of the introduced gene', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.673Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2172, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Some of the fresh water fishes commonly found in India are:

(A) Hilsa

(B) Pomfrets

(C) Catla

(D) Rohu

(E) Common carp', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B), (C) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (D) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Some of the freshwater fishes which are very common include Catla, Rohu and common carp. Some of the marine fishes that are eaten include - Hilsa, Sardines, Mackerel and Pomfrets.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.674Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2173, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following hormone is generally not produced by the placenta?', NULL, '[{"text":"hCG","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"hPL","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thyroxin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Estrogen","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Placenta also acts as an endocrine tissue and produces several hormones like human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), human placental lactogen (hPL), estrogens, progestogens, etc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.674Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2174, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Read the following and select the set of correct statements.

(A) Euchromatin is transcriptionally inactive

(B) Heterochromatin is more densely packed

(C) Heterochromatin is loosely packed

(D) Euchromatin is transcriptionally active

(E) Euchromatin stains lighter', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) and (B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (D) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'In a typical nucleus, some region of chromatin are loosely packed (and stains light) and are referred to as euchromatin. The chromatin that is more densely packed and stains dark are called as Heterochromatin. Euchromatin is said to be transcriptionally active chromatin, whereas heterochromatin is inactive.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.675Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2175, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Ascaris, the common round worm and Wuchereria, the filarial worm, are some of the helminths which are known to be pathogenic to man. Ascaris, an intestinal parasite causes ascariasis. Wuchereria the filarial worms cause filariasis. Many fungi belonging to the genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and Epidermophyton are responsible for ringworms which is one of the most common infectious diseases in man. Entamoeba histolytica is a protozoan parasite in the large intestine of human which causes amoebiasis (amoebic dysentery).', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 33', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.676Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 33","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2176, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The association of Glomus with roots of higher plants is known as _.', NULL, '[{"text":"Mycorrhiza","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rhizobium","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Azotobacter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Oscillatoria","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.679Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2177, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Fungi are also known to form symbiotic associations with plants (mycorrhiza). Many members of the genus Glomus form mycorrhiza.

Sol. ovum and sperms are prevented from physically meeting with the help of barrier contraceptives, IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the Cu ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilising capacity of sperms, Saheli is an oral contraceptive, surgical methods, also called sterilisation, are generally advised for the male/female partner as a terminal method to prevent any more pregnancies.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q35-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 35', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.681Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q35-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 35","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2178, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Haemophilia is a', NULL, '[{"text":"Sex linked dominant disorder","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sex linked recessive disorder","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Autosome linked dominant disorder","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Autosome recessive disorder","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Haemophilia is a sex-linked recessive disease, which shows its transmission from unaffected carrier female to some of the male progeny.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.682Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2179, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is NOT a sexually transmitted disease?', NULL, '[{"text":"Syphilis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"AIDS","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Filariasis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gonorrhoea","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Wuchereria (W. bancrofti and W. malayi), the filarial worms cause filariasis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.683Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2180, 6, NULL, NULL, '''Polyblend'' is a product made by Ahmed Khan. It is a:', NULL, '[{"text":"Herbal pesticide","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Biodegradable plastic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Fine powder of recycled modified plastic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A type of biofuel","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Polyblend, a fine powder of recycled modified plastic, was developed then by his company.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.684Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2181, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Secondary productivity is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Measured by organic matter produced.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rate of formation of new organic matter by producers.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rate of formation of new organic matter by consumers.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Always greater than primary productivity.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Secondary productivity is defined as the rate of formation of new organic matter by consumers.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.685Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2182, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Some examples of recent extinctions include the dodo (Mauritius), quagga (Africa), thylacine (Australia), Steller''s Sea Cow (Russia) and three subspecies (Bali, Javan, Caspian) of tiger.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q40-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 40', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.686Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q40-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 40","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
