Identify the labels A, B and C in the given figure', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) HI (B) DNA (C) Histone histone octamer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) DNA (B) HI (C) Histone histone octamer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) Histone (B) DNA (C) HIO octamer histone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) DNA (B) Histone (C) HI octamer histone","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A is DNA, B is H1 histone and C is histone octamer.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 44', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.689Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2186, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Core of histone molecules

Figure showing packaging of DNA Helix. Observe the figure and answer the following questions.

The region in prokaryotic cell whose DNA is organised in large loops held by proteins is called:', NULL, '[{"text":"Nuclein","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nucleic region","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nucleus","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nucleoid","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'In prokaryotes, such as, E. coli, though they do not have a defined nucleus, the DNA is not scattered throughout the cell. DNA (being negatively charged) is held with some proteins (that have positive charges) in a region termed as ''nucleoid''. The DNA in nucleoid is organised in large loops held by proteins', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q45-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 45', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.689Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q45-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 45","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2187, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question.

The function of filiform apparatus is to:', NULL, '[{"text":"Help in germination of pollen grains","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Guide the entry of pollen tube into ovule","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Help in the development of embryo","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Formation of male gametes","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The function of the filiform apparatus is to guide the pollen tube into the synergids.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q46-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 46', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.690Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q46-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 46","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2188, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question.

The ploidy of parts (D) and (E) are:', NULL, '[{"text":"(D)-n (E)-2n","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D)-2n (E)-n","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D)-n (E)-n","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D)-n (E)-3n The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question. (a) Pollen tube and synergids respectively Identify the part (A) and (B). (b) Synergids and female gamete respectively (d) Pollen tube and female gamete respectively","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'D is egg cell and is haploid and, E is synergists and is also haploid.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q47-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 47', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.690Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q47-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 47","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2189, 6, NULL, NULL, '(c) Pollen tube and antipodal cells respectively

The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question.

The site of germination of pollen grains is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Stigma","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ovary","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Style","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Embryo sac","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The site of germination of pollen grains is stigma.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q49-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 49', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.690Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q49-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 49","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2190, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question.

Triple fusion takes place when:', NULL, '[{"text":"One male gamete fuses with the one female gamete","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Two male gametes with the egg nucleus","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"One female gamete fuses with the polar nuclei","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"One male gamete fuses with the polar nuclei","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'One of the male gametes moves towards the egg cell and fuses with its nucleus thus completing the syngamy. This results in the formation of a diploid cell, the zygote. The other male gamete moves towards the two polar nuclei located in the central cell and fuses with them to produce a triploid primary endosperm nucleus (PEN). As this involves the fusion of three haploid nuclei it is termed triple fusion.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q50-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 50', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.691Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q50-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 50","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2191, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Select the statements which hold true for immune system:

A. Innate immunity or nonspecific immunity is present at the time of birth

B. Acquired immunity is never pathogen specific

C. Cytokine barriers are a part of innate immunity

D. Rheumatoid arthritis is an auto-immune disease', NULL, '[{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Acquired immunity, on the other hand is pathogen specific.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.693Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2192, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q02-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 2', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.700Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q02-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 2","kind":"table"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2193, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Bacillus thuringiensis produces Bt toxin crystals it does not kill the bacterium itself as the toxin is in the _ in bacteria.', NULL, '[{"text":"Harmless form","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Inactive form","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Premature stage","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Insoluble stage","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Crystals of Bt toxin produced by some bacteria is inactive form which gets activated in alkaline conditions of the gut of the worms.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.701Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2194, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Asexual reproductive structure of sponge is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Conidia","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Offset","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gemmule","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Zoospore","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Some common asexual reproductive structures are conidia (Penicillium), buds (Hydra) and gemmules (sponge).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.701Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2195, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Net primary productivity is the:', NULL, '[{"text":"Difference between the productivity of two different ecosystems","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Difference between the productivity of an area before and after succession","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rate of production of organic matter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rate of production of organic matter after considering respiration loss","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Gross primary productivity of an ecosystem is the rate of production of organic matter during photosynthesis. Gross primary productivity minus respiration losses (R), is the net primary productivity (NPP).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.702Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2196, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Two nucleotides linked together to form a dinucleotide though:', NULL, '[{"text":"3′ - 5′ phosphodiester linkage","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2′ - 5′ phosphodiester linkage","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1′ - 5′ phosphodiester linkage","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"N-glycosidic linkage","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A dinucleotide is obtained by the joining of two nucleotides by a $ 3'' $-5'' phosphodiester linkage.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.703Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2197, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Colour-blindness is due to mutation in certain genes present in the X chromosome. Down''s Syndrome is due to the presence of an additional copy of the chromosome number 21 (trisomy of 21). Klinefelter''s Syndrome is caused due to the presence of an additional copy of X-chromosome and Turner''s Syndrome is caused due to the absence of one of the X chromosomes.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q07-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 7', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.704Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q07-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 7","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2198, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The processing of pro-insulin involves:', NULL, '[{"text":"Attachment of C-peptide","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Modification of C-peptide","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Maturation of C-peptide","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Removal of C-peptide","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'This C peptide is not present in the mature insulin and is removed during maturation into insulin.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.704Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2199, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which is the biofortified variety of wheat with high protein content?', NULL, '[{"text":"Kalyan Sona","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sonalika","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Atlas - 66","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Himgiri","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Atlas 66, has a high protein content and has been used as a donor for improving cultivated wheat.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.705Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2200, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which is not a type of sexually transmitted infections?', NULL, '[{"text":"Genital warts","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cancer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gonorrhoea","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Syphilis","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Cancer is not a STD.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.706Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2201, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following steps of sewage treatment in correct sequence:

A. Flocs consume organic matter and reduces the BOD.

B. Removal of floating debris and grit.

C. Bacterial flocs allowed to sediment.

D. Primary effluent passed into aeration tank and agitated mechanically.

E. Effluent after secondary treatment is released into water bodies.', NULL, '[{"text":"B-D-A-C-E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B-C-A-D-E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-D-E-B-C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-C-D-E-B","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Primary treatment steps basically involve physical removal of particles - large and small - from the sewage through filtration and sedimentation. The primary effluent is passed into large aeration tanks (Figure 10.6) where it is constantly agitated mechanically and air is pumped into it. This allows vigorous growth of useful aerobic microbes into flocs. Once the BOD of sewage or waste water is reduced significantly, the effluent is then passed into a settling tank where the bacterial ''flocs'' are allowed to sediment. d into a settling tank where the bacterial ''flocs'' are allowed to sediment. This sediment is called activated sludge. A small part of the activated sludge is pumped back into the aeration tank to serve as the inoculum. The remaining major part of the sludge is pumped into large tanks called anaerobic sludge digesters. Here, other kinds of bacteria, which grow anaerobically, digest the bacteria and the fungi in the sludge. The effluent from the secondary treatment plant is generally released into natural water bodies like rivers and streams.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.706Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2202, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Select the high yielding and disease resistant variety(ies) of rice from the following:

A. Sonalika

B. Jaya

C. Kalyan Sona

D. Ratna', NULL, '[{"text":"B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Sonalika and Kalyan sona are high-yielding and disease resistant varieties.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.707Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2203, 6, NULL, NULL, 'ABO blood groups are controlled by _.', NULL, '[{"text":"Gene A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gene B","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gene I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gene O","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'ABO blood group in humans is controlled by gene I.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.707Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2204, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is not made by fermentation?', NULL, '[{"text":"Dosa batter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Bread","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Toddy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Aerated drinks","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Aerated drinks is not made by fermentation.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.708Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2205, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following hormone is secreted by the ovary in the later phase of pregnancy?', NULL, '[{"text":"Lactogen","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Relaxin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Estrogen","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In the later phase of pregnancy, a hormone called relaxin is also secreted by the ovary.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.709Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2206, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the correct sequence of events for the process of oogenesis:

A. The tertiary follicle changes into Graafian follicle

B. Formation of oogonia in fetal ovary.

C. Completion of first meiotic division by primary oocyte within the tertiary follicle.

D. Release of secondary oocyte from the ovary', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, C, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, C, A, B","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, A, D, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C, A, D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The process of formation of a mature female gamete is called oogenesis. Oogenesis is initiated during the embryonic development stage when a couple of million gamete mother cells. These cells start division and enter into prophase-I of the meiotic division and get temporarily arrested at that stage, called primary oocytes. Each primary oocyte then gets surrounded by a layer of granulosa cells and is called the primary follicle. The primary oocyte within the tertiary follicle grows in size and completes its first meiotic division. The tertiary follicle further changes into the mature follicle or Graafian follicle.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.709Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2207, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Human activities have accelerated rate of species extinction in the world. The major cause for it are:

A. Habitat loss and defragmentation

B. Habitat loss and fragmentation

C. Over-exploitation

D. Alien species invasions', NULL, '[{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The accelerated rates of species extinctions that the world is facing now are largely due to human activities. Habitat loss and fragmentation, alien species invasion, over-exploitation are responsible for species extinctions.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.711Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2208, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Surgical methods, also called sterilisation, are generally advised for the male/female partner as a terminal method to prevent any more pregnancy. Saheli is an oral contraceptive developed by CDRI. Condom is a barrier contraceptive for males, lactational amenorrhea (absence of menstruation) method is based on the fact that ovulation and therefore the cycle do not occur during the period of intense lactation following parturition.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q18-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 18', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.714Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q18-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 18","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2209, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Solid wastes generated from hospitals are generally disposed of by:', NULL, '[{"text":"Recycling","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Reusing","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Throwing it in landfills","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Using incinerators","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Incineration is a process that involves burning of solid waste in a furnace until the waste are converted into ashes.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.715Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2210, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is not a cannabinoid?', NULL, '[{"text":"Marijuana","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hashish","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ganja","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Heroin","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Heroin, commonly called smack is chemically diacetylmorphine which is a white, odourless, bitter crystalline compound. It is an opioid.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.716Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2211, 6, NULL, NULL, 'A double stranded DNA has 30% Of Thymine. The percentage Of Guanine in it would be:', NULL, '[{"text":"70%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"20%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"40%","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"30%","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'As per Chargaff''s law: A + T = G + C

Thymine = 30%

Adenine = 30%

Cytosine = 20%

Guanine = 20%', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.717Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2212, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Organs which differ in their origin and development but perform similar function are known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Homologous organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Analogous organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Vestigial organs","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Atavistic organs","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Analogous organs are those organs that have some superficial resemblance, perform similar functions and yet, have different evolutionary origins and hence, different anatomical structures.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.718Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2213, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'the most commonly used matrix is agarose which is a natural polymer extracted from sea weeds that is used in electrophoresis. In PCR, repeated amplification is achieved by the use of a thermostable DNA polymerase (isolated from a bacterium, Thermus aquaticus), which remain active during the high temperature induced denaturation of double stranded DNA. In micro-injection, recombinant DNA is directly injected into the nucleus of an animal cell. In rDNA technology, selectable marker helps in identifying and eliminating non-transformants and selectively permitting the growth of the transformants.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q23-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 23', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.719Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q23-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 23","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2214, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Select the brain capacity of Homo erectus from the following:', NULL, '[{"text":"900 cc","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"800 cc","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1400 cc","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"500 cc","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Homo erectus had a large brain around 900cc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.720Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2215, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Sickle-cell anaemia is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Autosome linked dominant trait","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sex linked dominant trait","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sex linked recessive trait","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Autosome linked recessive trait","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Sickle-cell anaemia is an autosome linked recessive trait that can be transmitted from parents to the offspring when both the partners are carried for the gene.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.721Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2216, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The enzyme that can recognise the following palindromic sequence

5-GAATTC-3

3-CTTAAG-5'' is _:', NULL, '[{"text":"Hind II","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"EcoR I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hind III","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Bam HI","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'EcoRI cuts the DNA between the bases G and A only when the sequence GAATTC is present in DNA.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.721Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2217, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Bacteria like Streptococcus pneumoniae and Haemophilus influenzae are responsible for the disease pneumonia. Rhino viruses represent one such group of viruses which cause one of the most infectious human ailments - the common cold. Many fungi belonging to the genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and Epidermophyton are responsible for ringworms which is one of the most common infectious diseases in man. Wuchereria causes elephantiasis or filariasis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q27-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 27', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.722Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q27-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 27","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2218, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Pollen grains are protected from high temperature and strong acids due to the presence of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Sporopollenin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Collagen","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pectin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cellulose","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Pollen grains are well-preserved as fossils because of the presence of sporopollenin.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.723Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2219, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In diploid organisms, specialised cells called meiocytes (gamete mother cell) undergo meiosis. At the end of meiosis, only one set of chromosomes gets incorporated into each gamete.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q29-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 29', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.723Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q29-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 29","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2220, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following stages of primary succession in water in correct sequence.

A. Rooted submerged plants

B. Marsh meadows

C. Phytoplanktons

D. Scrubs followed by trees

E. Free floating plants', NULL, '[{"text":"A→C→B→E→D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"E→D→A→C→B","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D→B→A→C→E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C→A→E→B→D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'In primary succession in water, the pioneers are the small phytoplanktons, which are replaced with time by rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms followed by free-floating plants, then reed-swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub and finally the trees. The climax again would be a forest', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.724Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2221, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Some examples of recent extinctions include the dodo (Mauritius), quagga (Africa), thylacine (Australia), Steller''s Sea Cow (Russia) and three subspecies (Bali, Javan, Caspian) of tiger.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q31-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 31', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.725Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q31-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 31","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2222, 6, NULL, NULL, '''r'' in exponential growth equation implies:', NULL, '[{"text":"Difference between the total number of births and deaths","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Extrinsic rate of natural increase","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Population density","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Intrinsic rate of natural increase","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '''r'' in exponential growth represents ''intrinsic rate of natural increase''.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.725Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2223, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following steps of Polymerase Chain Reaction in correct sequence.

A. Annealing of Primer

B. Denaturation of dsDNA

C. Extension of Primer

D. Amplification', NULL, '[{"text":"A-B-C-D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B-A-C-D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D-B-C-A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C-A-B-D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The steps of PCR include denaturation, annealing, extension and amplification.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.726Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2224, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the gas which was not used by Miller''s in his classic experiment:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ CH_{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ O_{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ H_{2}O $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ NH_{3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In 1953, S.L. Miller, an American scientist created similar conditions in a laboratory scale. He created electric discharge in a closed flask containing $ CH_{4} $, $ NH_{3} $ and water vapour at 8000°C. He observed formation of amino acids.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.729Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2225, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the statements relevant to Genetically Modified (GM) crops:

A. They have better pest resistance.

B. They have increased nutritional value.

C. They are more reliant on chemical fertilizers.

D. They have less post harvest losses.', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Genetic modification has: (i) made crops more tolerant to abiotic stresses (cold, drought, salt, heat). (ii) reduced reliance on chemical pesticides (pest-resistant crops). (iii) helped to reduce post harvest losses. (iv) increased efficiency of mineral usage by plants (this prevents early exhaustion of fertility of soil). (v) enhanced nutritional value of food, e.g., golden rice, i.e., Vitamin ''A'' enriched rice.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.732Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2226, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Zooplanktons species suspended their development during unfavourable conditions. This phenomenon is known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Hibernation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dormancy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Aestivation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Diapause","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Under unfavourable conditions many zooplankton species in lakes and ponds are known to enter diapause, a stage of suspended development.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.733Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2227, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the statements which are true with respect to Euchromatin

A. Loosely packed

B. Densely packed

C. Stains light

D. Transcriptionally active', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C, and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In a typical nucleus, some region of chromatin are loosely packed (and stains light) and are referred to as euchromatin. The chromatin that is more densely packed and stains dark are called as Heterochromatin. Euchromatin is said to be transcriptionally active chromatin, whereas heterochromatin is inactive.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.734Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2228, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the floral reward offered to insects for pollination

A. Pollen grains

B. Nectar

C. Fragrance

D. Safe place to lay eggs', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'To sustain animal visits, the flowers have to provide rewards to the animals. Nectar and pollen grains are the usual floral rewards. In some species floral rewards are in providing safe places to lay eggs.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.735Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2229, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Select the statements(s) which is/are true for Baculoviruses:

A. They belong to genus Nucleopolytetra viruses.

B. They are species specific in their action.

C. They have narrow spectrum insecticidal application.

D. They don''t have any negative impact on non-target insects.', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Baculoviruses are pathogens that attack insects and other arthropods. The majority of baculoviruses used as biological control agents are in the genus Nucleopolyhedrovirus. These viruses are excellent candidates for species-specific, narrow spectrum insecticidal applications. They have been shown to have no negative impacts on plants, mammals, birds, fish or even on non-target insects.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.736Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2230, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Joint Forest Management (JFM) was introduced to promote:', NULL, '[{"text":"Chipko Movement","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Jhum Cultivation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Slash and bum agriculture","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Local community in protecting forests","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Realising the significance of participation by local communities, the Government of India in 1980s has introduced the concept of Joint Forest Management (JFM) so as to work closely with the local communities for protecting and managing forests.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.737Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2231, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the question

(Stages in embryo development in a dicot)

Why is it that most zygotes divide only after certain amount of endosperm is formed?', NULL, '[{"text":"It assures nutrition to the developing embryo.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It assures nutrition to the developing cotyledons.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It ensures that endosperm is completely consumed.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It ensures that endosperm persists in the mature seed.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Embryo develops at the micropylar end of the embryo sac where the zygote is situated. Most zygotes divide only after certain amount of endosperm is formed. This is an adaptation to provide assured nutrition to the developing embryo.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q41-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 41', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.738Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q41-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 41","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2232, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the question

(Stages in embryo development in a dicot)

Identify the parts of the embryonal axis of a $ \underline{\text{dicot}} $ embryo:

A. Epicotyle

B. Plumule

C. Radicle

D. Scutellum', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A typical dicotyledonous embryo, consists of an embryonal axis and two cotyledons. The portion of embryonal axis above the level of cotyledons is the epicotyl, which terminates with the plumule or stem tip. The cylindrical portion below the level of cotyledons is hypocotyl that terminates at its lower end in the radicle or root tip. The root tip is covered with a root cap.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q42-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 42', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.738Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q42-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 42","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2233, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the question.

(Stages in embryo development in a dicot)

Coleoptile and Coleorrhiza in the embryo of grasses are:', NULL, '[{"text":"Part of the embryonal axis with hypocotyl","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"part of the embryonal axis with epicotyl","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hollow foliar structure enclosing shoot apex, leaf primordia AND sheath enclosing radicle and root cap, respectively","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sheath enclosing root can and hollow foliar (d) Sheath enclosing root cap and hollow foliar structure enclosing leaf primordia respectively","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Epicotyl has a shoot apex and a few leaf primordia enclosed in a hollow foliar structure, the coleoptile.

Sol. The embryonal axis has the radical and root cap enclosed in an undifferentiated sheath called coleorrhiza. The portion of the embryonal axis above the level of attachment of scutellum is the epicotyl.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q43-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 43', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.739Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q43-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2234, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the question

(Stages in embryo development in a dicot)

The correct sequence for parts labelled (i), (ii), (iii) and (iv) in the figure is:

A. Plumule

B. Suspensor

C. Cotyledons

D. Radicle', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, D, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C, A, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, D, B, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, D, C, A","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A typical dicotyledonous embryo, consists of an embryonal axis and two cotyledons. The portion of embryonal axis above the level of cotyledons is the epicotyl, which terminates with the plumule or stem tip. The cylindrical portion below the level of cotyledons is hypocotyl that terminates at its lower end in the radicle or root tip. The root tip is covered with a root cap.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q44-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 44', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.741Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q44-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2235, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the question

(Stages in embryo development in a dicot)

Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III),(B)-(IV),(C)-(II),(D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Embryogeny is similar in both monocotyledons and dicotyledons. The zygote gives rise to the proembryo and subsequently to the globular, heart-shaped and mature embryo.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q45-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 45', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.741Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q45-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 45","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q45-table-2.jpg","alt":"Table for question 45","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2236, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the following question

Domestic sewage primarily contains:', NULL, '[{"text":"Inorganic matter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Organic matter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Heavy-metals","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Electronic wastes","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Domestic sewage primarily contains biodegradable organic matter, which readily decomposes - thanks to bacteria and other micro-organisms, which can multiply using these organic substances as substrates and hence utilise some of the components of sewage.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q46-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 46', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.743Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q46-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 46","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q46-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 46","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2237, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the following question.

Indirectly, BOD is a measure of:

(a) Inorganic matter present in water

(b) Carbon dioxide in water

(c) Organic matter present in water

(d) Sand in water

Q48. Observe the figures and answer the following question.

BOD of water decreases significantly and the clean water organisms appears, in the water because', NULL, '[{"text":"Microorganism have consumed all inorganic matter present in water","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Microorganisms have consumed most of the biodegradable organic matter present in Water","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dissolved Oxygen is totally consumed","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Level of Carbon dioxide is significantly increased","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'indirectly, BOD is a measure of the organic matter present in the water.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q47-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 47', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.745Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q47-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 47","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q47-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 47","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q47-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 47","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q47-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 47","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2238, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Observe the figures and answer the following question

At the point of sewage discharge, the mortality of fish and Other aquatic creatures increases because:

(a) Dissolved oxygen becomes low

(b) Dissolved oxygen becomes high

(c) Dissolved Carbon dioxide becomes low

(d) Dissolved Nitrogen concentration becomes high

Q50. Observe the figures and answer the following question

The pollutants present in sewage which are relatively easy to remove are:', NULL, '[{"text":"Dissolved salts","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Metal ions","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dissolved organic compounds","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Floating debris","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Micro-organisms involved in biodegradation of organic matter in the receiving water body consume a lot of oxygen, and as a result there is a sharp decline in dissolved oxygen downstream from the point of sewage discharge. This causes mortality of fish and other aquatic creatures.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q49-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 49', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.746Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q49-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 49","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q49-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 49","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q49-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 49","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-1/q49-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 49","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2239, 6, NULL, NULL, 'What amount of energy would be at the producer level if it is 50 KJ at third trophic level?', NULL, '[{"text":"5 KJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"50 KJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"500 KJ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"5000 KJ","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The energy at the producer level is 5000 kJ, because only 10% of energy is transferred to next higher trophic level, above producers.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.750Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2240, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'In plants, the units of vegetative propagation such as runner, rhizome (ginger), sucker, tuber, offset (water hyacinth), bulbil (Agave) are all capable of giving rise to new offspring.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 2', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.750Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 2","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2241, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Copying genetic information from one strand of DNA into mRNA is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Transcription","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Translation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Transformation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Replication","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The process of copying genetic information from one strand of DNA into mRNA is termed as transcription.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.751Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2242, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Transfer of pollen grains from anther of one flower to the stigma of a flower of different plant is called as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Fertilisation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Geitonogamy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Xenogamy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cleistogamy","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Transfer of pollen grains from anther to the stigma of a different plant is called xenogamy. This is the only type of pollination which during pollination brings genetically different types of pollen grains to the stigma.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.751Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2243, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Hisardale is a cross-breed of sheep developed in Punjab by crossing Bikaneri ewes and Marino rams. Out-breeding is the breeding of the unrelated animals, which may be between individuals of the same breed but having no common ancestors for 4-6 generations (out-crossing) or between different breeds (cross-breeding) or different species (inter-specific hybridisation). A single outcross often helps to overcome inbreeding depression. Inbreeding is necessary if we want to evolve a pure line in any animal.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q05-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 5', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.752Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q05-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 5","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2244, 6, NULL, NULL, 'How many episodes of mass extinctions of species have occurred on earth since the origin and diversification of life?', NULL, '[{"text":"Two","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Three","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Five","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"SIX","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'During the long period (> 3 billion years) since the origin and diversification of life on earth there were five episodes of mass extinction of species.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.753Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2245, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the steps of Polymerase chain reaction in proper sequence-

A. Selection of desired fragment of DNA

B. Annealing

C. Amplification

D. Extension

E. Denaturation', NULL, '[{"text":"A, E, B, D, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B, C, E, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, D, B, C, E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"E, A, B, C, D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Correct sequence of steps in a PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) are denaturation, annealing and extension.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.754Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2246, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The process of evolution of different species in a given geographical area starting from a point and dispersing to other areas is called as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Natural Selection","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Adaptive radiations","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Disruptive selection","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Convergent evolution","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The process of evolution of different species in a given geographical area starting from a point and literally radiating to other areas of geography (habitats) is called adaptive radiation. Darwin''s finches represent one of the best examples of this phenomenon.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.754Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2247, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the mammals which live wholly in water:

A. Dolphins

B. Seals

C. Sea Horse

D Sea cow', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Dolphins, seals and sea cow are mammals that live in water, sea horse that is Hippocampus is not a mammal.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.755Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2248, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Human protein $ \alpha $-1 antitrypsin is used to treat', NULL, '[{"text":"Phenylketonuria","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Emphysema","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Haemophilia A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hepatitis B","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Transgenic animals that produce useful biological products can be created by the introduction of the portion of DNA (or genes) which codes for a particular product such as human protein ( $ \alpha $-1-antitrypsin) used to treat emphysema.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.755Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2249, 6, NULL, NULL, 'In a laboratory population of 80 fruit flies, 8 died in a week, then the death rate of fruit flies is:', NULL, '[{"text":"0.3 individuals per fruit fly per week","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.2 individuals per fruit fly per week","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.1 individuals per fruit fly per week","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.01 individuals per fruit fly per week","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'If 8 individuals in a laboratory population of 80 fruitflies died during a week, then death rate in the population during that period is $ \frac{8}{80} = 0.1 $ individuals per fruitfly per week.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.755Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2250, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The A and B polypeptides chains in insulin are linked together by which bond?', NULL, '[{"text":"Diester","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Disulphide","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hydrogen","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Peptide","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Insulin composed of two peptide chains namely the A chain and B chain that are linked together by two disulfide bonds.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.756Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2251, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The karyotype in Klinefelter''s syndrome is:', NULL, '[{"text":"2.44 + XO","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"44 + XXX","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"44 + XXY","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"44 + YO","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Klinefelter''s Syndrome is a genetic disorder caused due to the presence of an additional copy of X-chromosome resulting into a karyotype of 47, XXY.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.756Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2252, 6, NULL, NULL, 'In some species of Asteraceae and grasses, seeds are produced without fertilisation. This phenomenon is known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Apomixis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Parthenogenesis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Embryogenesis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gametogenesis","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Some seeds, in general are the products of fertilisation, a few flowering plants such as some species of Asteraceae and grasses, have evolved a special mechanism, to produce seeds without fertilisation, called apomixis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.756Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2253, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Fine powder of recycled modified plastics is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Polythene","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Polybag","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Polyblend","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Polystyrene","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Polyblend is a fine powder of recycled modified plastic. It was developed by the company of Ahmed Khan who was a plastic sack manufacturer in Bangalore.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.757Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2254, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following steps for replication of HIV in a correct sequence:

A. Production of new viral RNA by infected cell

B. Infection of normal cell by virus

C. Production of viral DNA

D. Production of new viruses', NULL, '[{"text":"B, C, D, A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B, C, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, C, B, A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C, A, D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Replication of Retrovirus', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.757Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2255, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the free-living nitrogen fixing bacteria

A. Rhizobium

B. Mycorrhiza

C. Azospirillum

D. Azotobacter', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Some bacteria can fix atmospheric nitrogen while free-living in the soil (examples Azospirillum and Azotobacter), thus enriching the nitrogen content of the soil.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.758Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2256, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The backbone of a polynucleotide chain is formed by:', NULL, '[{"text":"Sugar and nitrogenous base","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nitrogenous base and phosphates","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sugar and phosphates","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sugar: nitrogenous base and phosphates","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'DNA is made of two polynucleotide chains, where the backbone is constituted by sugar-phosphate, and the bases project inside.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.758Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2257, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Chromosomes in meiocytes of butterfly are:', NULL, '[{"text":"00","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"208","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"308","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"380","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Chromosomes in meiocytes of butterfly is 380.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.758Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2258, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The enzyme which is used to remove nucleotides from the ends of DNA fragment is-', NULL, '[{"text":"DNA ligase","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Restriction endonuclease","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Restriction exonuclease","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"DNA Polymerase","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Exonucleases are the enzymes that cut the double stranded or single stranded DNA and remove the nucleotides from the 5'' or 3'' ends.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.759Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2259, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Spermiogenesis is the process of formation of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Sperms from spermatids","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Spermatids from secondary spermatocytes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Secondary from primary spermatocytes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Primary spermatocytes from spermatogonia","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The spermatids are transformed into spermatozoa (sperms) by the process called spermiogenesis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.760Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2260, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Bacteria like Streptococcus pneumoniae and Haemophilus influenzae are responsible for the disease pneumonia in humans which infects the alveoli (air filled sacs) of the lungs. Rhino viruses represent one such group of viruses which cause one of the most infectious human ailments - the common cold. Salmonella typhi is a pathogenic bacterium which causes typhoid fever in human beings.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q22-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 22', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.761Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q22-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 22","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2261, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Colostrum secreted by mother is rich in:', NULL, '[{"text":"Ig D antibodies","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ig E antibodies","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ig A antibodies","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ig M antibodies","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Colostrum is very essential for a newborn as it supplies plentiful immunoglobulin A (IgA) that provides immunity.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.762Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2262, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the common Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs):', NULL, '[{"text":"Chlamydiasis, Trichomoniasis, Influenza","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Elephantiasis, Chlamydiasis, Syphilis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Trichomoniasis, Elephantiasis, Ascariasis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Chlamydiasis: Trichomoniasis, Syphilis","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Gonorrhoea, syphilis, genital herpes, chlamydiasis, genital warts, trichomoniasis, hepatitis-B are common STDs.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.764Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2263, 6, NULL, NULL, 'What kind of IUD is Lippes loop?

A. Non-medicated

B. Copper releasing

C. Zinc releasing

D. Hormone releasing

E. Medicated IUDs', NULL, '[{"text":"A only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Intra Uterine Devices are presently available as the non-medicated IUDs (e.g., Lippes''s loop), copper releasing IUDs (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375) and the hormone releasing IUDs (Progestasert, LNG-20).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.764Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2264, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Signals of parturition originate from which of the following?

A. Human Placental Lactogen

B. Parturition hormone

C. Fully developed foetus

D. Placenta', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The signals for parturition originate from the fully developed foetus and the placenta which induce mild uterine contractions called foetal ejection reflex.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.765Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2265, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Haemophilia is sex linked recessive disease, when a single gene can exhibit multiple phenotypic expression. Such a gene is called a pleiotropic gene. E.g. phenylketonuria. 9:3:3:1 is a ratio obtained in dihybrid cross. The inheritance of flower colour in the dog flower (snapdragon or Antirrhinum sp.) is a good example to understand incomplete dominance.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q27-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 27', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.766Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q27-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 27","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2266, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is NOT a technique of genetic engineering?', NULL, '[{"text":"Creation of recombinant DNA","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Use of gene cloning","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gene transfer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Grafting","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Grafting is a method of asexual plant propagation that joins plant parts from different plants together so they will heal and grow as one plant.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.766Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2267, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The yellow mosaic virus resistant variety Parbhani Kranti is the new variety of _', NULL, '[{"text":"Okra","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Flat bean","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Chilli","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cowpea","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Resistance to yellow mosaic virus in bhindi (Abelmoschus esculentus) was transferred from a wild species and resulted in a new variety of $ A.\ esculentus $ called Parbhani kranti.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.767Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2268, 6, NULL, NULL, 'In which ecosystem, a large fraction of energy flows more through DFC than through GFC?', NULL, '[{"text":"Pond Ecosystem","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"River Ecosystem","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Estuary Ecosystem","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Forest Ecosystem","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'in a terrestrial ecosystem, a much larger fraction of energy flows through the detritus food chain than through the GFC.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.767Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2269, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Diseases caused by fungi are:

A. Tobacco mosaic

B. Brown rust of wheat

C. Black rot of crucifers

D. Red rot of sugarcane

E. Late blight of potato', NULL, '[{"text":"A, C and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, D and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Some of the diseases caused by fungi are rusts, e.g., brown rust of wheat, red rot of sugarcane and late blight of potato; by bacteria - black rot of crucifers; and by viruses - tobacco mosaic, turnip mosaic, etc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.768Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2270, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) and Enzyme Linked Immuno-sorbent Assay (ELISA) are some of the techniques that serve the purpose of early diagnosis. Transgenic animals that produce useful biological products can be created by the introduction of the portion of DNA (or genes) which codes for a particular product such as human protein ( $ \alpha $-1-antitrypsin) used to treat emphysema. In 1997, the first transgenic cow, Rosie, produced human protein-enriched milk (2.4 grams per litre). The milk contained the human alpha-lactalbumin and was nutritionally a more balanced product for human babies than natural cow-milk.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q32-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 32', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.768Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q32-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 32","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2271, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'in 1953 that James Watson and Francis Crick, based on the X-ray diffraction data produced by Maurice Wilkins and Rosalind Franklin, proposed a very simple but famous Double Helix model for the structure of DNA. One of the hallmarks of their proposition was base pairing between the two strands of polynucleotide chains. However, this proposition was also based on the observation of Erwin Chargaff that for a double stranded DNA, the ratios between Adenine and Thymine and Guanine and Cytosine are constant and equals one. DNA Fingerprinting was initially developed by Alec Jeffreys. The elucidation of the lac operon was also a result of a close association between a geneticist, Francois Jacob and a biochemist, Jacque Monod.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 33', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.769Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 33","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2272, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Bone structure of forelimbs of vertebrates like whale, bat, cheetah and human is evidence of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Convergent evolution","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Divergent evolution","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Disruptive selection","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Directional selection","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Whales, bats, Cheetah and human (all mammals) share similarities in the pattern of bones of forelimbs. Though these forelimbs perform different functions in these animals, they have similar anatomical structure - all of them have humerus, radius, ulna, carpals, metacarpals and phalanges in their forelimbs. Hence, in these animals, the same structure developed along different directions due to adaptations to different needs. This is divergent evolution and these structures are homologous.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.769Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2273, 6, NULL, NULL, 'What of the following team refers to the confinement of the species to a specific area and also the same species are not found anywhere', NULL, '[{"text":"Pandemism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Endemism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Epidemic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Botanical Garden","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Endemism is the state of being a species found in a single defined geographic location, such as an island, state, nation, country or other defined zone; organisms that are indigenous to a place are not endemic to it if they are also found elsewhere.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.770Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2274, 6, NULL, NULL, '"Jhum cultivation" in the north-eastern states of India has contributed to:', NULL, '[{"text":"Reforestation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Plantation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Deforestation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Habitat Construction","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Slash and burn agriculture, commonly called as Jhum cultivation in the north-eastern states of India, has also contributed to deforestation. In slash and burn agriculture, the farmers cut down the trees of the forest and burn the plant remains. The ash is used as a fertiliser and the land is then used for farming or cattle grazing. After cultivation, the area is left for several years so as to allow its recovery. The farmers then move on to other areas and repeat this process.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.771Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2275, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II:

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:

(a) (A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)

(b) (A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)

(c) (A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)

(d) (A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)

38. Which of statements are correct about Thalassemia?

A. In $ \beta $ Thalassemia, production of $ \alpha $ globulin chain is affected and in $ \alpha $ Thalassemia production of $ \beta $ globulin chain is affected.

B. $ \alpha $ Thalassemia is controlled by two closely linked genes HBA1 and HBA2

C. The genes HBA1 and HBA2 are located on chromosome 11 of each parent.

D. $ \beta $ Thalassemia is controlled by a single gene HBB

E. The gene HBB is located on chromosome 16 of each parent.', NULL, '[{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'During primary treatment, the grit (soil and small pebbles) are removed by sedimentation. All solids that settle form the primary sludge, and the supernatant forms the effluent. During secondary treatment, the primary effluent is passed into large aeration tanks where it is constantly agitated mechanically and air is pumped into it. This allows vigorous growth of useful aerobic microbes into flocs. While growing, these microbes consume the major part of the organic matter in the effluent. This significantly reduces the BOD (biochemical oxygen demand) of the effluent. Once the BOD of sewage or waste water is reduced significantly, the effluent is then passed into a settling tank where the bacterial ''flocs'' are allowed to sediment. This sediment is called activated sludge. A small part of the activated sludge is pumped back into the aeration tank to serve as the inoculum. The remaining major part of the sludge is pumped into large tanks called anaerobic sludge digesters. Here, other kinds of bacteria, which grow anaerobically, digest the bacteria and the fungi in the sludge. During this digestion, bacteria produce a mixture of gases such as methane, hydrogen sulphide, and carbon dioxide. These gases form biogas.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q37-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 37', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.771Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-10-shift-3/q37-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 37","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2276, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The organism responsible for large holes in 1Swiss cheese'' is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Saccharomyces cerevisiae","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lactobacillus lactobacter","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Trichoderma polysporum","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Propionibacterium sharmanii","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'the large holes in ''Swiss cheese'' are due to production of a large amount of CO2 by a bacterium named Propionibacterium sharmanii.

suffer), predation and parasitism (one benefits and the other suffers), commensalism (one benefits and the other is unaffected), amensalism (one is harmed, other unaffected) and mutualism (both species benefit).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.771Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2277, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The interaction between two species where one species is benefitted and the other is neither benefitted nor harmed is known as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Commensalism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amensalism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Predation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Parasitism Direction for the question 41 to 45: Read the passage carefully. Attempt the questions. In our body, cell growth and differentiation is highly controlled and regulated. In cancer cells, there is breakdown of these regulatory mechanisms. Cancerous cells just continue to divide giving rise to masses of cells called tumors. Benign tumors normally remain confined to their original location. The malignant tumors, on the other hand are a mass of proliferating cells. These cells actively divide and starve the normal cells by competing for vital nutrients. Cells sloughed from such tumors reach distant sites through blood and wherever they get lodged in the body. They start a new tumor there. This property is called metastasis. Transformation of normal cells into cancerous cells may be induced by physical, chemical or biological agents called carcinogens.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Depending on the outcome, interactions between two species are classified as competition (both species', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.772Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'banner', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2278, 6, NULL, NULL, 'The statement which is correct for cancer cells:', NULL, '[{"text":"These cells grow very slowly invade and damage the blood cells","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"These cells grow very rapidly. invade and damage the normal tissue","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"These cells grow very slow, invade and manufacture the plasma cells","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"These cells grow very rapidly invade and damage the liver cells only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In our body, cell growth and differentiation is highly controlled and regulated. In cancer cells, there is breakdown of these regulatory mechanisms. These cells grow very rapidly, invading and damaging the surrounding normal tissues. As these cells actively divide and grow they also starve the normal cells by competing for vital nutrients.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.772Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2279, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Cancer is caused by:

A. Carcinogens

B. Protein rich foods

C. Primary lymphocytes

D. Oncogenes', NULL, '[{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Transformation of normal cells into cancerous neoplastic cells may be induced by physical, chemical or biological agents. These agents are called carcinogens. Cancer causing viruses called oncogenic viruses have genes called viral oncogenes. Furthermore, several genes called cellular oncogenes (c-onc) or proto-oncogenes have been identified in normal cells which, when activated under certain conditions, could lead to oncogenic transformation of the cells.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.772Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2280, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Normal cells show a property that does not allow their uncontrolled growth. This property is known as:

(a) Contact inhibition

(b) Contact selection

(c) Metastasis

(d) Contact promotion

44. Benign tumors are normally remain confined to:', NULL, '[{"text":"Blood and later spread to other pans of body.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Original location and do not spread to other parts of the body.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Original location and later spread to all the body parts.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Original location and cause heavy damage to the body parts.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.773Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2281, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Tobacco smoke been identified as a major cause of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Skin Cancer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Blood Cancer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lung Cancer","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Brain Cancer Direction for the question 46 to 50: Read the passage carefully. Attempt the questions. An overwhelming majority (99 per cent) of animals and nearly all plants cannot maintain a constant internal environment. Their body temperature changes with the ambient temperature. In aquatic animals, the osmotic concentration of the body fluids changes with that of the ambient air and water osmotic concentration. These animals and plants are simply conformers. Considering the benefits of a constant internal environment to the organism, we must ask why these conformers had not evolved to become regulators. Recall the human analogy we used above; much as they like, how many people can really afford an air conditioner? Many simply ''sweat it out'' and resign themselves to suboptimal performance in hot summer months. Very small animals are rarely found in polar regions. During the course of evolution, the costs and benefits of maintaining internal environment are taken into consideration. Some species have evolved the ability to regulate, but only over a limited range of environmental conditions, beyond which they simply conform. If the stressful external conditions are localised or remain only for a short duration, the organism has five other alternatives for survival.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Smoking is associated with increased incidence of cancers of lung, urinary bladder and throat, bronchitis, emphysema, coronary heart disease, gastric ulcer, etc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.773Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2282, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Conformers have not evolved to become regulators because:', NULL, '[{"text":"Conformers are generally small sized organisms.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cost of becoming a regulator is very low.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Their anatomical structure is simple.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cost of becoming a regulation is very high.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Small animals have a large surface area to volume ratio, so a lot of energy has to be spent to regulate temperature. To conserve energy conformers have not evolved into regulators.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.774Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2283, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the animal which is NOT a conformer.', NULL, '[{"text":"Humming bird","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Shrew","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Polar Bear","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lizard","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Polar bear is not a conformer.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.774Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2284, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Conformers are the animals whose body temperature:', NULL, '[{"text":"Remain constant","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Change with the surrounding temperature.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Remain quite lower than the surrounding temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Remain quite higher than the surrounding temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Conformers have little homeostasis and are ectothermic, their body temperature changes according to their environment.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.774Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2285, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the set of aquatic animals whose osmotic concentration is not constant.', NULL, '[{"text":"Whale and Fish","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amoeba and Paramecium","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Whale and Dolphin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dolphin and Fish","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In Amoeba and paramecium, the osmoregulation occurs through Contractile vacuole.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.775Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2286, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the statements which support the reason why small animals are rarely found in polar regions.

A. Small animals have larger surface area relative to their volume

B. Small animals have larger volume relative to their surface area

C. Shrews and humming birds are not found in polar region

D. Small animals have smaller surface area relative to their volume', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Small animals have larger surface area relative to their volume, they tend to lose body heat very fast when it is cold outside; therefore they have to expend much energy to generate body heat through metabolism. This is the reason why polar regions are not a suitable habitat for $ \underline{\text{tiny humming birds.}} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T20:59:54.775Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2287, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the incorrect statement

A. Bakelite and urea-formaldehyde resins are elastomers

B. Polyamides like nylon 6, nylon 6,6 are the examples of fibers.

C. Polystyrene polyvinylchloride and polythene are thermoplastic polymers.

D. Thermoplastic polymers have intermolecular force between elastomers and fibers.', NULL, '[{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D and A only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Bakelite and urea-formaldehyde resins are the example of thermosetting polymers. These are not elastomers.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.089Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2288, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Option (A)

Mg is a metal that has free electrons. So, it conducts electricity in the solid state and is known as an electronic conductor.

Hence, (A) → (iv)

Option (B)

MgCl₂ shows electrolytic conductivity in the molten state due to its behaviour as an electrolyte ( i.e., mobile ions Mg²⁺ and Cl⁻ ions help in the flow of current). Thus, MgCl₂ is an electrolytic conductor.

Hence, (B) → (iii)

Option (C)

When silicon (group 14) is doped with phosphorus (group 15), which contains five valence electrons, four out of the five valence electrons form covalent bonds with the four neighbouring silicon atoms. The fifth electron is extra and is delocalized. These delocalized electrons increase the conductivity due to the negatively charged electrons. Hence silicon doped with phosphorus (electron-rich impurity) is called an n-type semiconductor.

Hence, (C) → (ii)

Option (D)

When germanium (group 14) is doped with boron (group 13), which contains three valence electrons, the three valence electrons form covalent bonds with the four neighbouring silicon atoms. The place where the fourth valence electron is missing is called the electron-hole or electron vacancy. An electron from the nearby atom can occupy the vacancy, but in doing so, it would leave a vacancy in its original position.

Thus, it would seem as if the electron-hole is moving in the direction opposite to the electron that first occupied the vacant site. Under the influence of an electric field, the electrons move towards the positively charged plate whilst the electron-hole moves towards the negatively charged plate, as if the electron-hole were positive. Hence germanium doped with boron (electron-deficient impurity) is called a p-type semiconductor.

Hence,

(D) → (i)', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 2', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.090Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 2","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2289, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Chlorine containing antibiotic by soil microorganisms which is effective for the treatment of typhoid fever is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Chloroquine","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Chloramphenicol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Halothane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Tetra chloromethane","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Chloramphenicol: $ C_{11}H_{12}Cl_{2}N_{2}O_{5} $

The antibiotic used for the treatment of typhoid is Chloramphenicol.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.090Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2290, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following statements are not correct?

A. Phenol is used to prepare analgesic drugs.

B. Solubility of phenol in water is more than that of chlorobenzene.

C. Phenol is neutralised by sodium carbonate.

D. Boiling point of o-nitrophenol is lower than that of p-nitrophenol.', NULL, '[{"text":"A & B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B & D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C & D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Phenol is a weak acid and cannot be neutralized by sodium carbonate.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.090Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2291, 5, NULL, NULL, 'According to the Raoult''s law, vapour pressure of a solution is directly proportional to:', NULL, '[{"text":"Mole fraction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Part per million","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mass percentage","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Molality","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'According to Raoult''s law the partial vapors pressure of each component in the solution is directly proportional to its mole fraction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.091Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2292, 5, NULL, NULL, '20 g of binary electrolyte (Molecular mass = 100) are dissolved in 500 g of water. The freezing point of the solution is -0.74°C and $k_{f}$ is 1.86 K kg mol$^{-1}$. The degree of ionisation of electrolyte is:', NULL, '[{"text":"0.5","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.75","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1.0","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.0","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '$ \Delta T_{f} = k_{f} \times m \times i $

m (Molality) = n_{B}/W_{A}(kg) = (20/100)/(500/1000) = 2/5 = 0.4

$ \Delta T_{f} = 0 - (-0.744) = 0.744 $ OC

Kf = 1.86 km^{-1}

= 0.744 = 1.86 $ \times $ 0.4 $ \times $ i

i = 1, for dissociation, $ \alpha = 1 - 1/n - 1 $

= 1 - 1/2 - 1 = 0', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.091Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2293, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The edge lengths of the unit cells in terms of the radius of spheres constituting fcc, bcc & simple cubic unit cells respectively are:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 2\\sqrt{2}r, \\frac{4r}{\\sqrt{3}}, 2r $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{4r}{\\sqrt{3}}, 2\\sqrt{2}r, 2r $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2r, $ 2\\sqrt{2}r $, $ \\frac{4r}{\\sqrt{3}} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 2r, \\frac{4r}{\\sqrt{3}}, 2\\sqrt{2}r $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'As atoms in FCC lattice touch each other along the face diagonal

$ \Rightarrow r + 2r + r = \text{length of face diagonal} $

$ \Rightarrow a \sqrt{2} = 4r $

$ \Rightarrow a = 2\sqrt{2}r $

As atoms in BCC lattice touch each other along the body diagonal

$ \Rightarrow r + 2r + r = \text{length of body diagonal} $

$ \Rightarrow a \sqrt{3} = 4r $

$ \Rightarrow a = 4r/\sqrt{3} $

As atoms in simple cubic lattice touch each other along the edge

$ \Rightarrow r + r = \text{length of edge} $

$ \Rightarrow a = 2r $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.091Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2294, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which among the following is not a broad spectrum antibiotic?', NULL, '[{"text":"Ofloxacin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Vancomycin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Penicillin","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Chloramphenicol","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Antibiotics which kill or inhibit a wide range of gram positive and gram-negative bacteria are called broad spectrum antibiotics. Among the given options, penicillin is not a broad-spectrum antibiotic. It is a narrow spectrum antibiotic i.e., it is effective mainly against specific families of bacteria.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.092Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2295, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Part (A)

Soda water contains dissolved carbon dioxide in water. Thus, soda water is a solution of gas in liquid. Hence, (A) $ \rightarrow $ (iv)

Part (B)

Sugar solution contains dissolved sugar particles in water. Thus, sugar solution is a solution of solid in liquid. Hence, (B) $ \rightarrow $ (iii)

Part (C)

German silver is an alloy of Cu, Zn and Ni. Thus, German silver is a solution of solid in solid. Hence, (C) $ \rightarrow $ (ii)

Part (D)

Air is a mixture of nitrogen gas, oxygen gas and some other gases. Thus, air is a solution of gas in gas. Hence, (D) $ \rightarrow $ (i)', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q09-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 9', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.092Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q09-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 9","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2296, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Predict P, Q, R, S and T in a correct sequence:

A.

E.', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, C, D, E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, A, C, D, E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"E, A, C, B, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C, D, B, E","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '(P)

(T)', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 10', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.095Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q10-figure-5.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2297, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Given reaction is the example of -', NULL, '[{"text":"Kolbe''s reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Reimer-Tiemann reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Williamson Synthesis","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Friedel Craft reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Kolbe''s reaction: When phenol reacts with sodium hydroxide, reactive phenoxide ion is formed. So, electrophilic aromatic substitution takes place with CO2 under a pressure of 4-7 atm followed by acidification and ortho hydroxybenzoic acid (Salicylic acid) is formed. This is called Kolbe''s reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q11-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 11', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.097Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q11-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 11","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2298, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Fog is a colloidal solution of', NULL, '[{"text":"Solid in gas","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gas in gas","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Liquid in gas","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gas in liquid","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Fog is an example of a colloid in which the dispersed phase is a liquid and the dispersion medium is a gas. Fog has tiny water droplets suspended in air. These kind of colloids are also called aerosols.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.097Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2299, 5, NULL, NULL, '[Cu(en) $ _2 $] $ ^{2+} $ is more stable than [Cu(NH $ _3 $) $ _4 $] $ ^{2+} $', NULL, '[{"text":"It is a heteroleptic complex","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethylene diamine has an alkyl group","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Copper in +2 oxidation state is more stable","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ligand is didentate and form chelate complex","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '[Co(en) $ _3 $] $ ^{3+} $ is more stable than [Co(NH $ _3 $) $ _6 $] $ ^{3+} $ as [Co(en) $ _3 $] $ ^{3+} $ is a metal chelate due to presence of bidentate ligand ethylene diamine ligand. Metal chelates are more stable than complexes containing only monodentate ligands.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.098Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2300, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Artificial sweetener: A sugar substitute is an ingredient added to food that has a similar sweet flavour to sugar but much fewer calories than sugar-based sweeteners, making it a zero-calorie or low-calorie sweetener. Alitame is an artificial sweetener.

B. Antihistamines interfere with the natural action of histamine by competing with histamine for binding sites of receptor where histamine exerts its effect. Synthetic drugs, brompheniramine (Dimetapp) and terfenadine (Seldane), act as antihistamines.

C. Non-narcotic (non-addictive) analgesics

Aspirin and paracetamol are the most common drugs in this case.

D. Antiseptics are the chemical drugs which either kill or prevent the growth of microorganisms. They are applied selectively to living tissues such as wounds, cuts, ulcers, and diseased skin surfaces. Examples are: -Furacin and soframycin are antiseptics.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q14-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 14', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.098Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q14-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 14","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2301, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the incorrect statement.', NULL, '[{"text":"In endothermic reaction reactant molecules have lower energy than product molecules","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Energy of activated complex is higher than the energy of reactants","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Energy of activation of a reaction is different from energy of activation with catalyst for the same reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Rate of reaction decreases with rise in temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'An increase temperature increases the reaction rate. When temperature is increased, the kinetic energy of the molecules also increases. Because of higher kinetic energy, the number of particles that possess the minimum energy also increases thereby more particles will collide and react.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.098Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2302, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In the following sequence of reaction:

$ \mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{Br} \xrightarrow{\mathrm{KCN}} \mathrm{A} \xrightarrow{\mathrm{H}_{3}\mathrm{O}^{+}} \mathrm{B} \xrightarrow[\text{ether}]{\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}} \mathrm{C} $

The end product (C) is', NULL, '[{"text":"Acetone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Methane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Acetaldehyde","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethyl alcohol","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Methyl bromide reacts with KCN to form acetonitrile. Br atom is replaced with CN group. Hydrolysis of cyano group gives carboxylic group. Reduction of carboxylic group gives hydroxyl group.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.099Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2303, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Select the incorrect statement(s)

A. Surface active agents like soaps and synthetic detergents form micelles in water.

B. Soaps are emulsifying agents.

C. $ C_{17}H_{35} $ (hydrocarbon) and -COO $ ^{-} $(Carboxylate) part of stearate ion ( $ C_{17}H_{35}COO^{-} $) both are hydrophobic.

D. Surfactants are basic in nature.', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and A only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Option (b) is incorrect because $ C_{17}H_{35} $ is hydrophobic, whereas COO $ ^- $ of stearate ion ( $ C_{17}H_{35}COO^- $) is hydrophilic. This owes to the polarity of ions and hydrocarbons.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.099Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2304, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Process of zone refining is used in the purification of', NULL, '[{"text":"Al","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cu","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ge","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ag","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Zone refining process is used in the purification of germanium.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.099Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2305, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Reaction occurring at cathode is $ \ce{HgO + H_{2}O + 2e^{-} -> Hg(l) + 2OH^{-}} $

Above reaction is found in:', NULL, '[{"text":"Leclanche cell","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mercury cell","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Fuel cell","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ni-Cd-cell","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Mercury cell: It consists of zinc mercury amalgam as anode, a paste of HgO and Carbon black is used as cathode. The electrolyte is a paste of KOH and ZnO. At anode: Zn (amalgam) + 2OH⁻ → ZnO(s) + HO(l) + 2e⁻ At cathode: HgO(s) + H₂O + 2e⁻ → Hg(l) + 2OH⁻', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.100Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2306, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The pair in which both the species have the same magnetic moment (spin only value) is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $, $ [\\mathrm{CoCl}_{4}]^{2-} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $, $ [\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Mn}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $, $ [\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{CoCl}_{4}]^{2-}, [\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ [\mathrm{Cr}(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $ and $ [\mathrm{Fe}(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})_{6}]^{2+} $ have same magnetic moment as both $ \mathrm{Cr}^{2+} $ and $ \mathrm{Fe}^{2+} $ have same number of unpaired electrons.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.100Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2307, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Mohr''s salt is _ is colour', NULL, '[{"text":"Yellow","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Blue","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Green","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Colourless","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Ferrous Ammonium Sulphate is also called Mohr''s salt a light green color sand like crystalline solid', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.101Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2308, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Insulin is the example of', NULL, '[{"text":"Peptide Hormones","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amino acid derived hormones","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Steroidal hormones","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Adrenal Cortical hormones","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Insulin is a peptide hormone (51 amino acids arranged in two peptide chains linked by two disulphide bonds, molecular weight 5807Da), which is secreted by the $ \beta $-Cells of the islets of Langerhans in the pancreas.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.101Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2309, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. For the electronic configuration of the Cr^{3+} ion, we

will remove three electrons from the Cr (one from the 4s1 and two from the 3d5), leaving us with $ 1s^{2}2s^{2}2p^{6}3s^{2}3p^{6}3d^{3} $ or $ [Ar]3d^{3} $.

B. The manganese (IV) oxide is the second most strongly attracted compound, and is paramagnetic.

C. $ Cu^{+1} $ compound are diamagnetic in nature. the outer configuration is $ 3d^{10} $ and therefore it has all paired electrons in $ Cu^{+1} $ oxidation state.

D. Electronic configuration of .22Ti^{4+} is [Ar] $ ^{18} $3d^{0}4s^{0}. So all electrons are paired and thus its all complexes are diamagnetic.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q23-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 23', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.101Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q23-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 23","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2310, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Alum helps in purifying water by:

A. Coagulation of mud particles

B. Sedimentation of mud particles.

C. Dialysis

D. Forming true solution with water', NULL, '[{"text":"A & C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A & D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B & C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A & B only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Alum, also known as aluminium sulfate is added to water in order to destabilize the mud particles suspended in it. This process is known as coagulation. Alum helps in purifying water by aluminium which coagulates the mud particles. Because of the high charge on the aluminium ion ( $ Al^{+3} $), it helps the small particles of suspended solids to group together until they are of such size that they sink and can be removed.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.102Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2311, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Correct sequence of conversion of 4-nitrotoluene to 2-bromobenzoic acid is

A.

B.

C.

D.

E.', NULL, '[{"text":"C→B→D→E→A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B→C→D→E→A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A→B→C→D→E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C→D→E→B→A","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q25-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 25', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.102Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q25-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 25","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q25-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 25","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q25-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 25","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q25-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 25","kind":"figure"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2312, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. In compounds, lanthanum exhibits only one oxidation state, +3.

B. Like most rare-earth elements, praseodymium most readily forms the +3 oxidation state, which is the only stable state in aqueous solution, although the +4 oxidation state is known in some solid compounds

C. We know that, +3 oxidation is common in all series. Stable of +3 O.S. depends upon high hydration energy, high lactic energy and high I.P.

Nd^{2+} has configuration 4f^{4}

Nd^{4+} has configuration 4f^{2}

Hence +2, +4 oxidation states are unstable in Nd in aqueous solution.

D. Samarium is a chemical element with symbol Sm and atomic number 62. It is a moderately hard silvery metal that slowly oxidizes in air. Being a typical member of the lanthanide series, samarium usually has the oxidation state +3.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q26-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 26', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.102Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q26-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 26","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2313, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The electrochemical cells

Zn|Zn²⁺||Cu²⁺|Cu and Fe|Fe²⁺||Cu²⁺| Cu are

connected in series, What will be the net emf of the

cell at 25°C?

Given: E° of Zn²⁺|Zn = −0.76V

E° of Cu²⁺|Cu = +0.34V

E° of Fe²⁺|Fe = −0.41V', NULL, '[{"text":"+1.85 V","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"−1.85 V","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"+0.83 V","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"−0.83 V","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Emf of the cell, Zn(s)|Zn²⁺(aq)||Cu²⁺(aq)|Cu(s) is:

$ \mathrm{E^{0}_{Cu2+}/Cu} - \mathrm{E^{0}_{Zn2+}/Zn} = +0.34 - (-0.76) $

= 1.10V

Emf of the cell, Fe(s)|Fe²⁺(aq)||Cu²⁺(aq)|Cu(s) is:

$ \mathrm{E^{0}_{Cu2+}/Cu} - \mathrm{E^{0}_{Fe2+}/Fe} = +0.34 - (0.41) = 0.75 \, \mathrm{V} $

Since the two electrodes are connected in series, the net emf of the cell is:

$ =1.10+0.75=\underline{1.85}V $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.103Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2314, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In a thermite process, the reducing agent is', NULL, '[{"text":"C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Zn","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Na","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Al","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'The Thermite Process or Goldschmidt Process is the method of obtaining liquid metal by reduction of the oxide with aluminium powder, when ignited with magnesium ribbon it reacts by producing iron and aluminium oxide at an intensely high temperature approaching 3000° C. The reducing agent is aluminium.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.103Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2315, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following compounds can be used as antifreeze in automobile radiators?', NULL, '[{"text":"Methyl Alcohol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Glycol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nitrophenol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethyl Alcohol","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Due to its high boiling point and miscibility with $ H_{2}O $, glycol is used as an antifreeze in automobile radiators.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.103Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2316, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The isotope $ ^{19}\text{K}^{42} $ has a half life of about 12 hours. What fraction of the initial concentration of $ ^{19}\text{K}^{42} $ remains after 48 hours.', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{8} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{12} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{16} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Half-life period is 12 hours. Hence, the amount of $ ^{19}\text{K}^{42} $ becomes half in $ t_{1/2} $. After 48 h, it becomes 1/16th.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.104Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2317, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Yellow colour in NaCl is due to', NULL, '[{"text":"Schottky defect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Metal excess defect due to anionic vacancies","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Frenkel defect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Metal deficiency defect","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In metal excess defect due to anion vacancies, negative ion is missing from its site by leaving a negative hole and this is occupied by electron. The anionic site occupied by electron is called F- centre. This imparts yellow colour to the NaCl while heating.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.104Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2318, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Butanone is less reactive than propanal towards nucleophilic addition reaction because:', NULL, '[{"text":"more + I effect found in butanone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"less + I effect found in butanone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"more + I effect found in propanal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"less +ve charge found on carbonyl group of propanal","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The electron density at the carbonyl carbon increases with the increase in the +1 effect. As a result, the chances of attack by a nucleophile decrease. Hence, the increasing order of the reactivities of the given carbonyl compounds in nucleophilic addition reactions is: Butanone < Propanal', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.104Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2319, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. Xerophthalmia is a serious eye disorder associated with vitamin A deficiency.

B. Vitamin C deficiency, also known as scurvy, is a disease primarily associated with socioeconomic status and access to food.

C. Beriberi is a disease in which the body does not have enough thiamine (vitamin B $ _{1} $).

D. Severe vitamin D deficiency can also lead to other diseases: In children, it can cause rickets. Rickets is a rare disease that causes the bones to become soft and bend.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 33', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.104Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q33-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 33","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2320, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following in decreasing order of their boiling point

(Ⅰ)

(II)

(a) I > II > III

(b) II. > III > I

(III)

(c) III > I > II

(d) II > I > III

p-Hydroxyazobenzene is also called as', NULL, '[{"text":"Yellow dye","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Red dye","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Orange dye","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Violet dye","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'As the intermolecular force increases, boiling point increases. Strength of intermolecular force is as follows:

H-bonding > dipole-dipole > Dispersion force

Alcohol has the highest boiling point due to more extensive intermolecular H-bonding

Aldehyde is more polar than ether. So, ethanol has higher boiling point than methoxy methane.

Alkane has the lowest boiling point due to complete non-polar nature (it has only London dispersion force).

Hence, increasing order of boiling points of compounds is given below-

$ CH_3CH_2CH_3 < CH_3OCH_3 < CH_3CH_2OH $', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q34-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 34', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.105Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q34-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 34","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q34-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 34","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q34-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 34","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2321, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which is not the limitation of valence bond theory involving coordination compound.', NULL, '[{"text":"It involves a number of assumptions","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It does not give quantitative interpretation of magnetic data","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It does not distinguish between weak & strong ligands","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"It does not explain the formation of coordination compounds","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Limitations of Valence bond theory:

It does not give explain magnetic properties/data.

It does not explain the color indicated by coordination compounds.

It does not give an explanation of the thermodynamic/kinetic stabilities of coordination complexes.

It does not differentiate between weak/strong ligands.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.105Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2322, 5, NULL, NULL, 'A solution of CuSO₄ is electrolysed for 10 minutes using a current of 1.5 amperes. (1 mol of Cu = 63 g). How much copper is deposited at cathode. 1F = 96487 Cmol⁻¹', NULL, '[{"text":"0.2938 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2.938 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"29.38 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.02938 g (d) 0.02938 g","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The reaction is, \mathrm{Cu^{2+}+2e^{-}\rightarrow Cu}

I = 1.5 ampere

t = 10 $ \times $ 60

= 600s

Q = It

= 1.5 $ \times $ 600 = 900 L

The reaction states that, 2 $ \times $ 96500 C required to deposit 63.5 g Cu at cathode

900 C will deposit,

= 63.5 $ \times $ 900/(2 $ \times $ 96500) $ \times $ 900 = 0.296 g Cy at cathode.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.105Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2323, 5, NULL, NULL, 'What is the order of hydrolysis of methyl acetate in acidic medium?', NULL, '[{"text":"Zero order","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pseudo First order","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"First order","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Second order","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ \text{CH}_3\text{COOCH}_3 + \text{H}_2\text{O} $ (excess) $ \rightarrow $ $ \text{CH}_3\text{COOH} + \text{CH}_3\text{OH} $

In this reaction, $ \text{H}_2\text{O} $ taken in excess therefore is known as first order pseudo reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.106Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2324, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following compounds undergo predominantly S $ _{N} $2 reaction with NaOH in a polar aprotic solvent?

(a)

(b)

(c)

Choose the most most appropriate answer from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Rate of $ S_{N}2 $ reaction $ \propto -M, -1 $ power.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q39-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 39', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.106Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q39-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 39","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q39-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 39","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q39-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 39","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-02-shift-3/q39-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 39","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2325, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following ion is colourless?', NULL, '[{"text":"Zn^{2+}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ti^{3+}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mn^{3+}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ Cr^{3+} $ Answer the question on the basis of passage given below: (Q41 to Q45) There are some deposits of nitrates and phosphates in the earth''s crust. Nitrates are more soluble in water. Nitrates are difficult to reduce under laboratory conditions, but microbes do it easily. Ammonia, forms a large number of complexes with transition metals. Hybridisation easily explains the ease of sigma donation capability of $ NH_{3} $ and $ PH_{3} $. Phosphine is an inflammable gas, it is prepared from white phosphorus.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The ion will show colour if it has unpaired electrons in its electronic configuration, In $ Zn^{+2} $ there are no unpaired electrons due to fully filled d orbital. Hence, will be colourless.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.106Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2326, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is the correct statement?', NULL, '[{"text":"Phosphates have no biological significance in humans.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Between nitrates and phosphates, phosphates are less abundant in the earth''s crust.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Between nitrates and phosphates, nitrates are less abundant in the earth''s crust","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Oxidation of nitrates is possible in soil.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Due to greater solubility and nature to be prone to microbial action, nitrates are less abundant in earth''s crust.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.106Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2327, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Among the following the correct statement is

A. Between NH₃ and PH₃, NH₃ is a better electron donor because the lone pair of electrons occupy spherical ''s'' orbital and is less directional.

B. Between NH₃ and PH₃, NH₃ is a better electron donor because the lone pair of electrons occupies sp³ orbital and is more directional.

C. Between NH₃&PH₃,PH₃ is a better electron donor because the lone pair of electrons occupies sp³ orbital and is more directional.

D. Between NH₃ & PH₃, PH₃ is a better electron donor because the lone pair of electrons occupies ''s'' orbital and is less directional.', NULL, '[{"text":"A only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'In NH₃ lone pair on N is present in sp³ hybridized orbital and hence is more directional.

Whereas in PH₃ lone pair is present mainly in 3s orbital also the bond angle in PH₃ is almost 90° and such compounds are regarded as drago compounds.

So NH₃ is more basic than PH₃', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.107Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2328, 5, NULL, NULL, 'White phosphorus on reacting with NaOH gives NaH_{2}PO_{2} and PH_{3} as products. This is an example of.

(a) Dimerisation reaction

(b) Disproportionation reaction

(c) Condensation reaction

(d) Precipitation reaction

4. PH₃ is a better reducing agent than NH₃ because', NULL, '[{"text":"PH₃ can give its lone pair of electron easily","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Bond dissociation enthalpy of P-H is low","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Bond dissociation enthalpy of P-H is high","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"PH₃ is tetrahedral is shape","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Here Phosphorus atom changes its ON from 0 to +1 in $ NaH_{2}PO_{2} $ and 0 to -3 in $ PH_{3} $

$$ \begin{aligned}&P_{4}+3NaOH+3H_{2}O\longrightarrow&PH_{3}\quad+&3NaH_{2}PO_{2}\\&&Phosphine\quad&Sodium hypophosphite\end{aligned} $$', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.107Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2329, 5, NULL, NULL, '$ NH_{3} $ is a stronger base than $ PH_{3} $', NULL, '[{"text":"Phosphorus is smaller in size than nitrogen","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Nitrogen is smaller in size than phosphorus","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"PH $ _{3} $ does not have lone pair of electron","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"NH_{3} does not have lone pair of electron Answer the question on the basis of passage given below: (Q46 to Q50) Aldehydes and ketones are two important classes of organic compounds which are widely used in the synthesis of a variety of other organic compounds. Due to the polarity of the carbonyl group, they undergo nucleophilic addition reactions. Broadly speaking, these addition reactions are of two types-one in which simply the addition of the nucleophilic reagent occurs across $ \\geq C=O $ bond and the other in which addition is followed by the elimination of a molecule of water. A number of ammonia derivatives such as hydroxylamine, hydrazine, phenylhydrazine, 2, 4-dinitrophenylhydrazine and semicarbazide belong to the second category of reactions. These derivatives are used for identification and characterization of aldehydes/ketones. Both types of nucleophilic addition reactions are influenced by steric and electronic factors. In general, aliphatic aldehydes are more reactive than aromatic aldehydes. The aliphatic aldehydes reduce both Fehling''s solution and Tollen''s reagent but aromatic aldehydes reduce only Tollen''s reagent. Like aldehydes, aromatic ketones are less reactive than aliphatic ketones towards nucleophilic addition reactions. Phenols and carboxylic acids are acidic in nature. Both dissolve in NaOH solution and turn blue litmus red. However carboxylic acids are much stronger acids than phenols and decompose NaHCO₃ with the evolution of CO₂ but phenols do not. Both electron-donating and electron-withdrawing substituents influence the acid strength of aliphatic as well as aromatic acids. Unlike all other aliphatic acids, formic acid has reducing properties and also does not show reactions of the alkyl group.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ NH_{3} $ is a stronger base than $ PH_{3} $. This is because the lone pair of electrons on N atom in $ NH_{3} $ is directed and not diffused as it is in $ PH_{3} $ due to large size of phosphorus and hence more available for donation.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.107Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2330, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following statement/s is/ are correct?

A. Aldeydes give positive test with Tollen''s reagent.

B. Ketones give positive test with Fehling''s solution

C. Ketones do not react with Fehling''s solution.

D. Aldehydes with Schiff''s reagent restore pink colou

E. Ketones with Schiff''s reagent restore pink colour.', NULL, '[{"text":"A, C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C, D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C, B only (a)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. Tollen''s test gives positive results in the presence of aldehyde and $ \alpha $-hydroxyketone.

C. Aldehydes result in a positive Tollen''s test, but ketones do not, because of their structure, ketones do not react with Fehling''s or Tollens'' reagents. The H atom is not directly linked to the carbonyl group in a ketone. Thus, ketones are not readily oxidized whereas aldehydes are.

D. Schiff''s reagent gives pink colour with formic acid and aldehydes such as acetaldehyde. It does not give pink colour with other carboxylic acids, esters and ketones.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.108Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2331, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Carboxylic acid do not give the characteristic reaction of carbonyl group because:', NULL, '[{"text":"the oxygen atom of the OH group does not contain lone pair of electrons","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"carbonyl carbon of carboxyl group is more electrophilic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"carbonyl carbon of carboxyl group is more nucleophilic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"carbonyl carbon of carboxyl group is less electrophilic","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Carboxylic acids do not give characteristic reaction of carbonyl group. This is because the lone pairs on oxygen atom attached to hydrogen atom in the -COOH group are involved in resonance thereby making the carbon atom less electrophilic. Hence, carboxylic acids do not give characteristic reaction of carbonyl group.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.108Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2332, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Fehling Solution A and B respectively, are:', NULL, '[{"text":"Alkaline solution of sodium potassium tartrate and alcoholic copper sulphate","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Aqueous copper sulphate and alkaline solution off Rochelle salt","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Alkaline potassium citrate and aqueous solution of copper sulphate","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Alkaline solution of Rochelle salt and aqueous copper sulphate","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Solution A: CuSO_{4} solution.

Solution B: Rochelle salt (sodium potassium tartrate)

+ sodium hydroxide', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.108Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2333, 5, NULL, NULL, 'How much calcium will be obtained when 4 Faradays of electricity is passed through molten CaCl_{2}.', NULL, '[{"text":"20 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"40 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"80 g","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"160 g","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'We know that, 1 Faraday charge liberates one gram-equivalent of a metal, hence 4 F charge will liberate = 4 x 40 = 160 g of Calcium', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.111Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2334, 5, NULL, NULL, '0.01 M aqueous solutions of following salts were prepared. Their conductivity values were measured at $ 25^{\circ} $C. Which of the following will possess highest conductivity at $ 25^{\circ} $C?', NULL, '[{"text":"LiCl","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"RbCl","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"NaCl","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"CsCl","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Note that anion $ \text{Cl}^{c-} $ is the same in all the given compounds. So, the conductance value will only depend on the size of cation in aqueous solution.

Since $ \Lambda_{mCs\oplus} > \Lambda_{mRb\oplus} > \Lambda_{mNa\oplus} > \Lambda_{mLi\oplus} $

Hence, $ \Lambda_{mCsCl} > \Lambda_{mRbCl} > \Lambda_{mNaCl} > \Lambda_{mLiCl} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.112Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2335, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following amines can be prepared by Gabriel synthesis?

(A) Isobutyl amine

(B) 2-Phenyl ethylamine

(C) N-Methyl benzyl amine

(D) Aniline', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Only primary aliphatic amines such as $ (CH_{3})_{2}CH_{2}CH_{2}NH_{2} $ (a) and $ C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}CH_{2}NH_{2} $ (b) can be prepared by Gabriel synthesis, 2° amines, i.e., $ C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}NHCH_{3} $ (c) and aromatic 1° amines, i.e., $ C_{6}H_{5}NH_{2} $ (d), however, cannot be prepared.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.113Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2336, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The decomposition of $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ in alkaline medium, in presence of $\mathrm{I}^{-}$ ions occurs as follows:

$2\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\xrightarrow{\mathrm{I}^{-},~alkaline~medium}2\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}+\mathrm{O}_{2}$

If the reaction occurs in the following two steps:

Step 1: $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}+\mathrm{I}^{-}\xrightarrow{\mathrm{Slow}}\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}+\mathrm{IO}^{-}$

Step 2: $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}+\mathrm{IO}^{-}\xrightarrow[\mathrm{Fast}]{\mathrm{Slow}}\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}+\mathrm{I}^{-}+\mathrm{O}_{2}$

The correct rate law expression for the reaction is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$\\mathrm{r}=k[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2}]^{2}[\\mathrm{I}^{-}]$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{r}=k[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2}][\\mathrm{I}^{-}]$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{r}=k[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2}][\\mathrm{IO}^{-}]$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{r}=k[\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\mathrm{O}_{2}]^{2}[\\mathrm{I}^{-}][\\mathrm{OH}^{-}]$","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'As step (1) is slow, it is the rate-determining step as it dictates the overall pace of the reaction, hence its Rate =k[H_{2}O_{2}][I^{-}]', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.114Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2337, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the given name reaction:

$ \text{R} - \text{NH}_2 + \text{CHCl}_3 + 3\text{KOH} \xrightarrow{\text{Heat}} \text{R} - \text{NC} + 3\text{KCl} + 3\text{H}_2\text{O} $', NULL, '[{"text":"Sandmeyer''s reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Carbylamine reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hoffman''s bromamide reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hinsberg''s reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ \text{RNH}_2 + \text{CHCl}_3 + 3\text{KOH} \rightarrow \text{RNC} + 3\text{KCl} + 3\text{H}_2\text{O} $

This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.114Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2338, 5, NULL, NULL, 'A compound is formed by 2 elements P and Q. Atoms of element Q (as anions) makes ccp and those of P (as cations) fill all tetrahedral voids and also occupy half of the octahedral voids. What is the correct formula of this compound?', NULL, '[{"text":"P₂Q₅","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"P₅Q₂","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"P₂Q₃","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"P₃Q₂","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given, the compound is formed by two elements p and q. Atom Q is in CCP arrangement we know, Number of atoms in CCP (N) = 4 Atom P occupy tetrahedral void and half octahedral void

Number of tetrahedral void = 2N = 2 $ \times $ 4 = 8

Number of octahedral voids = N = 4

Thus, atom P = 8 + 4/2 = 10

$ P_{10}Q_{4} $

Thus formula of the compound is $ P_{5}Q_{2} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.114Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2339, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following compounds in the order of their increasing boiling point:

Pentan-1-ol, n-butane, pentanal, ethoxy ethane', NULL, '[{"text":"n-butane < ethoxy ethane < pentanal < pentan-1-ol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"n-butane < pentanal < ethoxy ethane < pentan-1-ol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"n-butane < pentanal-1-ol < ethoxy ethane < pentanal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"pentan-1-ol < ethoxy ethane < pentanal < n-butane","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Factors affecting boiling point

1. Number of carbon atoms:

As the number of carbon atoms increases in alcohol molecule, the boiling point of alcohol also increases as the molecular mass increases which increases the molecular attraction between molecules.

2. Branching in molecules:

As the number of branching increases, the boiling point of alcohol decreases because branching in molecules decreases the surface area thereby decreasing the attractive forces between individual molecules.

As the extent of hydrogen bonding increases, the boiling point also increases due to increase in the attractive forces between individual molecules. Boiling point order
Pentan-1-ol

n-butane

If pentan-1-ol and pentanal are compared, both compounds have almost same molecular mass so, similar London forces. Moreover, dipole-dipole interactions are also similar in both the compounds only hydrogen bonding is making a difference as extent of intermolecular hydrogen bonding is greater in case of pentan-1-ol than pentanal. Hence, boiling point of pentan-1-ol is greater than pentanal. Hence considering all factors, increasing order of boiling point will be:', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.115Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2340, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The rate law for a reaction between substance P & Q is given by $ \mathrm{Rate} = k[\mathrm{P}]^{\mathrm{x}}[\mathrm{Q}]^{\mathrm{y}} $

If concentration of P is doubled and concentration of Q is halved, the ratio of the new rate to the earlier rate of reaction will be:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ x + y $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"x - y","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 2^{x} - y $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{2^{x-y}} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'rate = k[A]^x[B]^y

On doubling the concentration of A and making the

volume of B half, the new rate becomes $ 2^x \times (1/2)^y = 2 $-times the earlier rate.

So Ratio is $ 2^{x-y} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.115Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2341, 5, NULL, NULL, 'For the reactions $5\mathrm{Br}^-(aq) + \mathrm{BrO}_3^-(aq) + 6\mathrm{H}^+ (aq) \rightarrow 3\mathrm{Br}_2(aq) + 3\mathrm{H}_2\mathrm{O}(1)$

The rate of the reaction is:', NULL, '[{"text":"one-fifth of rate of disappearance of $\\mathrm{Br}^-$- ions","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"one-fifth of rate of formation of $\\mathrm{Br}_2$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"one-third of rate of disappearance of $\\mathrm{BrO}_3^","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ ions (d) one-fourth of rate of formation of $\\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{O}$","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'For the given reaction,

$ \mathrm{BrO_3^- + 5Br^-(aq) + 6H^+ \rightarrow 3Br_2(l), + 3H_2O(l)} $

Rate of reaction in terms of $ \mathrm{Br}_2 $ and $ \mathrm{Br}^- $ is,

$ \mathrm{Rate} = 1/3[\mathrm{d}[\mathrm{Br}_2]/\mathrm{dt} = -1/5\mathrm{d}[\mathrm{Br}^-]/\mathrm{dt} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.115Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2342, 5, NULL, NULL, 'We have four aqueous solution labelled as:

(A) 0.1 M NaCl

(B) 0.01 M NaCl

(C) 0.01 M BaCl_{2}

(D) 0.01 M Sucrose

Choose the correct increasing order of Van''t Hoff factor from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ i_{C} < i_{A} < i_{B} < i_{D} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ i_{D} < i_{C} < i_{B} < i_{A} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ i_{D} < i_{A} = i_{B} < i_{C} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ i_{C} < i_{A} = i_{B} < i_{D} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The extent to which a substance associates or dissociates in a solution is described by the Van''t Hoff factor.

i = Total number of moles of particles after association/dissociation / Number of moles of particles before association/dissociation

Both NaCl and BaCl₂ are strong electrolytes and completely dissociate in aqueous solution.

NaCl→Na⁺+Cl⁻

i=2/1=2

Thus, value of Van''t Hoff factor for NaCl solution with concentrations 0.1M, 0.01M and 0.001M will be same because these concentrations represent dilute solutions.

BaCl₂→Ba²⁺+ 2Cl⁻

i=3/1=3

Sucrose is neither weak nor strong electrolyte. It''s not an electrolyte, it doesn''t dissociate or associate in its aqueous solution. But simply dissolve in water.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.116Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2343, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IIV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A. A mixture containing two enantiomers in equal proportions will have zero optical rotation, such as a mixture is known as racemic mixture. The process of conversion of enantiomers into a racemic mixture is known as racemization. If an alkyl

halide follows AN1 mechanism then racemization takes place, while if it

B. In vicinal dihalides, halogens atoms are present on the adjacent carbon atom, bromination of alkenes will give vicinal dihalides.

C. Alkylidene halides are named as Gem-dihalides. In gem-dihalides halogen atoms are present on same carbon atom.

D. Saytzeff''s rule

In dehydrohalogenation reactions, the preferred product is that alkene which has a greater number of alkyl groups attached to the doubly bonded carbon atoms. Saytzeff''s rule helps to determine the formation of the major alkene in a dehydrohalogenation reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q11-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 11', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.116Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q11-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 11","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2344, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following statements about gold (Au) element are correct?

(A) Gold occurs in nature in native state.

(B) Gold dissolves in aqua-regia.

(C) Gold is extracted by leaching the metal with dilute NaCN.

(D) Leaching is followed by replacement reaction.', NULL, '[{"text":"(B), (C), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) and (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Correct statements:

[A] Gold doesn''t react with very many other elements, hence it is often found in its native form in the Earth''s crust

[B] Gold is soluble in aqua-regia.

[C] Extraction of gold from its native ore involves leaching the metal ore with dilute solution of NaCN in presence of air.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.116Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2345, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Methyl bromide reacts with silver nitrite to form:', NULL, '[{"text":"Nitromethane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Methylnitrite","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethanenitrite","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Grignard reagent","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '$$ CH_{2}Br\xrightarrow{AgNO_{2}}CH_{2}NO_{2}+AgBr $$', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.117Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2346, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The volume of mixing ( $ \Delta V $) is not zero for which of the following solutions?', NULL, '[{"text":"Chloroethane and Bromoethane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Benzene and Toluene","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethanol and Acetone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"n-Hexane and n-Heptane","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.117Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2347, 5, NULL, NULL, 'When dilute hydrochloric acid is added to sodium chromate solution the colour changes to:', NULL, '[{"text":"yellow","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"colourless","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"green","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"organge","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A solution of acetone in ethanol deviates from Raoult''s law in a positive way. This is due to the fact that ethanol molecules are strongly hydrogen-bonded. When acetone is added, the hydrogen bonds are broken and ethanol becomes more volatile. As a result, its vapour pressure rises.

Sol. When dilute hydrochloric acid (Yellow colour) is added to yellow coloured sodium chromate solution then the colour of the solution will change to orange.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.117Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2348, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The complex having lowest $ \Delta_0 $ value among the given complexes is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{NH}_3)_6]^{3+} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{O})_6]^{3+} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{CN})_6]^{3-} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ [\\mathrm{CrCl}_6]^{3-} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'CFSE depends on number of d-electron in metal ion.

Cr - 1s² 2s² 2p6 3s² 3p6 3d⁴, so d orbital contains 4

electrons

Co - 1s² 2s² 2p6 3s² 3p6 3d⁷ 4s²

CFSE is higher when the complex contains strong field

ligand. Thus, crystal field splitting energy increases in

the order

Because according to spectrochemical series the

order of field strength is

Cl- < H2O < NH3 < CN-', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.118Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2349, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The actual density of a crystal of NaCl is observed to be lower than the expected value. It is caused due to the presence of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Interstitial Defect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Frenkel Defect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Schottky Defect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Impurity Defect","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Schottky defect causes decrease in the density of a crystal. In this defect, equal number of cations and anions are missing from their position in the crystal lattice.

Frenkel defect does not alter the density of a crystal. In this defect, cation or anion occupies an interstitial position.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.118Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2350, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The pair(s) of co-ordination complexes/ions exhibiting the same kind of isomerism is / are:

(A) [Cr(NH₃)₅Cl]Cl₂ and [Cr(NH₃)₄Cl₂]Cl

(B) [Co(NH₃)₄Cl₂]⁺ and [Pt(NH₃)₂(H₂O)Cl]⁺

(C) [CoBr₂Cl₂]⁻² and [PtBr₂Cl₂]²⁻

(D) [Pt(NH₃)₃(NO₃)]Cl and [Pt(NH₃)₃Cl]Br', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The pairs of coordination complexes/ions exhibiting the same kind of isomerism are: Octahedral $ [Co(NH_3)_4Cl_2]^+ $ and square planar $ [Pt(NH_3)_2(H_2O)Cl]^+ $ which shows geometrical (cis-trans) isomerism. Square planar $ [Pt(NH_3)_3(NO_3)] $Cl and square planar $ [Pt(NH_3)_3Cl] $Br shows ionization isomerism. The pairs of coordination complexes/ions NOT exhibiting the same kind of isomerism are: $ [Cr(NH_3)_5Cl]Cl_2 $ neither shows structural nor stereoisomerism. $ [Cr(NH_3)_4Cl_2] $Cl shows geometrical (cis trans) isomerism Tetrahedral $ [CoBr_2Cl_2]^{2-} $ and square planar $ [PtBr_2Cl_2]^{2-} $ do not show same type of isomerism.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.119Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2351, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. PVC is produced from its monomer, vinyl chloride.

poly(vinyl chloride)

B. It is urea formaldehyde polymer and it''s monomers are urea and formaldehyde.

C. The structure of Glyptal is made up of two monomers Ethylene glycol and Phthalic acid

D. Bakelite is a polymer made up of the monomers phenol and formaldehyde.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q20-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 20', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.119Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q20-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 20","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2352, 5, NULL, NULL, '0.01 molal aqueous solutions of strong electrolytes NaCl, KCl, MgSO_{4} and K_{2}SO_{4} are prepared. Which of the following statements is correct regarding their osmotic pressure? (Assume complete dissociation of solute particles)', NULL, '[{"text":"All of them exhibit equal osmotic pressure","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Osmotic pressure of all of them are different","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"MgSO_{4} has highest osmotic pressure","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"K_{2}SO_{4} has highest osmotic pressure","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'osmotic pressure ( $ \pi $) = MRTi

$ \pi = 0.01 RT $ i

Only Van''t Hoff factor varies for each compound given in the options i.e., $ \pi \alpha $ i

For option (d) only, $ \mathrm{K}_{2}\mathrm{SO}_{4} \rightarrow 2\mathrm{K}^{+} + \mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-} $

i = 3/1 = 3', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.120Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2353, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In the extraction of metallic Zn from calamine ore (ZnCO_{3}) following steps are involved:

(A) Distillation of impure Zn

(B) Calcination of the ore

(C) Hydraulic washing of ore

(D) Reduction of ZnO using coke

Choose the correct order of steps from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"(C), (D), (B), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (B), (D), (A)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C), (B), (D)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A. Distillation is used for low boiling metals like zinc. The impure metal is evaporated under low pressure to obtain the pure metal as distillate.

C. The powdered ore is washed using an upward stream of flowing water. The heavier ore particles are left after the lighter gangue particles are washed away.

B. Calcination is defined as the process of converting ore into an oxide by heating it strongly. The ore is heated below its melting point either in absence of air or in limited supply.

D. The reaction is as follows: $ \mathrm{ZnO(s)} + \mathrm{C(g)} = 1400\mathrm{O_2} $

$ \mathrm{Zn(s)} + \mathrm{CO(g)} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.120Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2354, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:

(a) (A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)

(b) (A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(II)

(c) (A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)

(d) (A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)

24. Which property is observed in an emulsion?', NULL, '[{"text":"Tyndall effect","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Brownian motion","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Tyndall effect and Brownian motion","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Stable in nature","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. Glycosidic linkage: Joint monosaccharide units.

B. Peptide linkage: Joint amino acid units.

C. Each nucleotide consists of a heterocyclic base, a pentose sugar (2''-deoxy-d-ribofuranose), and a phosphate group. There are four heterocyclic bases in DNA: adenine (A), guanine (G), cytosine (C) and thymine (T).

D. Nucleosides are monomers of nucleic acids, DNA and RNA.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q23-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 23', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.120Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q23-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 23","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2355, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which phenomenon occurs when an electric field is applied to a colloidal solution and electrophoresis is prevented?

(A) Reverse osmosis takes place

(B) Electroosmosis takes place

(C) Dispersion medium begins to move in an electric field

(D) Dispersion medium becomes stationary', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'When electrophoresis, i.e., movement of particles is prevented by some suitable means, it is observed that the dispersion medium begins to move in an electric field. This phenomenon is termed electroosmosis.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.121Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2356, 5, NULL, NULL, 'When electric current is passed through acidified water, 448 mL of hydrogen gas at STP is collected at the cathode in 965 seconds. The current passed in amperes is:', NULL, '[{"text":"1.0","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2.5","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3.0","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4.0","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Step 1: Calculation weight of hydrogen in given volume

At STP, volume of one mole of hydrogen gas is 22.4 L = 22400 mL

Weight of one mole of of H₂ = 2 g

22400 mL of H₂ = 2 g

448 mL of H₂ = 2 x 448/22400 = 0.04 g

Step 2: Calculation for amount of current

2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → H₂

According to Faraday''s law,

nF = 1 mole

where, F = Faraday''s constant = 96500 C

n = number of electrons = 2

∴Charge required to deposit 2g of hydrogen = 2 × 96500

∴Charge required to deposit 0.01g of hydrogen = 2 × 96500 × 0.04/2 = 1102.8 C

Current = Charge/time

Current = 1102.8/965

Current = 1.14 ≈ 1', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.121Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2357, 5, NULL, NULL, 'A square planar complex is formed by hybridization:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ s $, $ p_x $, $ p_y $, $ p_z $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ s $, $ p_x $, $ p_y $, $ d_z $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ s $, $ p_y $, $ p_z $, $ d_{xy} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ s $, $ p_x $, $ p_y $, $ d_{x^2-y^2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A square planar complex is formed by hybridization of s, p_x, p_y, d_{x2-y2} atomic orbitals. All these orbitals lie in the xy plane. Four ligands also lie in the xy plane. This results in maximum overlap.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.122Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2358, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The hormone responsible for preparing the uterus for implantation of fertilised egg is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Progesterone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Testosterone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Epinephrine","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Norepinephrine","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Progesterone''s presence is critical in maintaining the lining of the endometrium, which is necessary for the implantation and growth of the embryo.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.122Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2359, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following statement is incorrect?', NULL, '[{"text":"Brownian movement stabilises sol.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Both emulsifier and peptising agents stabilises colloids but their actions are different.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mixing two oppositely charged sols neutralizes their charges and stabilises the colloid.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"The stability of lyophobic colloidal particles is due to preferential adsorption of ions on their surface from the solution.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'When dispersed phase is added in excess, it forms a separate layer and thus the emulsion gets destabilized.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.123Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2360, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following process is responsible for the formation of delta at a place where rivers meet the sea?', NULL, '[{"text":"Emulsification","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Colloid formation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Coagulation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Peptization","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'River water is a colloidal solution containing many solid particles like sand, clay etc.

Sea water contains electrolyte NaCl.

Electrolytes present in sea water coagulate the colloidal solution of the river water.

The place where river meets with sea formation of Delta takes place due to coagulation process in which sea water helps river water to coagulate.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.124Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2361, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:

(a) (A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)

(b) (A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)

(c) (A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)

(d) (A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)

2. o-Nitrophenol is less soluble in water than p-nitrophenol because:', NULL, '[{"text":"o-Nitrophenol is more steam volatile than p-nitrophenol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"o-Nitrophenol shows intramolecular H-bonding","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"o-Nitrophenol shows intermolecular H-bonding","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Melting point of o-Nitrophenol is lower than p-nitrophenol","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'A. A reaction with sodium metal can be used to differentiate between ethanol and diethyl ether. While ether does not react with sodium metal, ethanol will react and release H $ _{2} $ gas.

B. Methanol and ethanol are distinguished by a type of test known as iodoform when ethanol is warmed with iodine in the presence of NaOH, it forms a yellow coloured precipitate but methanol do not react positively to iodoform test.

C. Tert. butyl alcohol reacts immediately with $ (ZnCl_{2}+HCl) $ Lucas reagent to form cloudiness, secondary butyl alcohol reacts within 5 minutes while n-butyl alcohol does not react at all room temperature.

D. Phenol gives violet colour with FeCl_{3} solution but cyclohexanol does not.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q31-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 31', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.124Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q31-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 31","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2362, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In the 3d series of transition elements, the element more likely to exhibit +1 oxidation state is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Fe","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mn","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cu","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ag","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Copper metal (with electronic configuration $ [Ar]3d^{10} $ $ 4s^{1} $) in the first series of transition metals exhibits +1 oxidation state most frequently as it readily loses one electron (present in 4s orbital) to give stable 3d10 electronic configuration.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.125Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2363, 5, NULL, NULL, 'An aromatic compound ''A'' of molecular formula $ \ce{C7H7ON} $ undergoes a series of reaction as:

$ \ce{C7H7ON ->[Br2/KOH][A] B ->[NaNO2 + HCl][A] C ->[CH3CH2OH][A]} $

Identify compound D:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\ce{C7H5N} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{C6H6O} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{C6H7N} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{C6H6} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.127Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2364, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The magnetic moment of Cu $ ^{2+} $ ion (Z = 29) is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\sqrt{3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\sqrt{8} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\sqrt{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\sqrt{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Cu^{2+} has 1 unpaired electron

$ \mu=\sqrt{n(n+2)} $BM

$ \mu=\sqrt{1(1+2)}=\sqrt{3} $BM', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.128Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2365, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The correct statements about Cr^{2+} and Mn^{3+} are:

(atomic number of Cr = 24 and Mn = 25)

(A) Cr^{2+} is a reducing agent

(B) Mn^{3+} is an oxidising agent

(C) Both Cr^{2+} and Mn^{3+} exhibit d^{4} electronic configuration

(D) When Cr^{2+} is used as reducing agent chromium ion attains d^{5} electronic configuration', NULL, '[{"text":"(B), (D) and (A) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B), (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C), (D), (A) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D), (A) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '(A) $ Cr^{2+} $ is a reducing agent. It itself loses electrons (and hence acts as a reducing agent) and forms higher oxidation states. In fact, +6 oxidation states of Cr is very stable. Hence the option (A) is correct.

(B) Mn^{3+} is an oxidizing agent. It itself gains electrons (and hence acts as an oxidizing agent) to form Mn^{2+} with 3d^{5} electronic configuration which is stable as it is half-filled.

Hence, the option (B) is correct.

(C) Cr and Mn have outer ionic configurations of $ 3d^{5}4s^{1} $ and $ 3d^{5}4s^{2} $ respectively.

Hence, both Cr^{2+} and Mn^{3+} exhibit d4 electronic configuration.

Hence, the option (C) is correct.

(D) When Cr^{2+} is used as a reducing agent, the chromium ion attains d3 (as in Cr^{3+}) electronic configuration.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.130Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2366, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The formation of micelle takes place only:

(A) above a particular temperature called kraft temperature

(B) above a particular concentration called critical micelle concentration

(C) when catalyst is added', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (C)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Associated colloids are substances which at low concentrations behave as normal strong electrolytes, but at higher concentrations exhibit colloidal behaviour due to the formation of aggregates. The aggregated particles thus formed are called micelles.

The formation of micelles takes place only above a particular temperature called Kraft temperature (Tk) and above a particular concentration called critical micelle concentration (CMC).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.131Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2367, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Antiseptics and disinfectants either kill or prevent growth of micro-organism. Identify which of the following statements is not true?

(A) Disinfectants harm the living tissues.

(B) A 0.2% solution of phenol is an antiseptic while 1% solution acts as disinfectant.

(C) Chlorine and Iodine are used as strong disinfectants.

(D) Dilute solution of boric acid and hydrogen peroxide are antiseptics.

(E) Iodoform is also used as an antiseptic for wounds. Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"(C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) and (B) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A 0.2% solution of phenol is an antiseptic while 1% solution acts as a disinfectant.

Chlorine and Iodine are used as strong disinfectants. Dilute solution of boric acid is an antiseptic used to wash eyes and hydrogen peroxide is disinfectant. Disinfectants harm the living tissues.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.132Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2368, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In the following sequence of reactions:

$ \ce{CH3-CH-CH3 ->[HNO2][NH2] [A] ->[\text{Oxidation}][\text{B}] \ce{CH3MgBr ->[H+] /H2O}} $

The compound [C] is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Butan-l-ol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Butan-2-ol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1,1-Dimethyl ethanol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2-methyl propan-2-ol","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The end product (C) is 1,1-dimethylethanol.

Isopropyl amine reacts with nitrous acid to form isopropyl alcohol. On oxidation acetone is obtained which then reacts with methyl magnesium iodide (a Grignard reagent) followed by acid hydrolysis to give 1,1-dimethylethanol.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.133Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2369, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Identify Compound [A]', NULL, '[{"text":"Butan-2-one","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3-methyl Pentan-2-one","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Propanone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Acetophenone","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A Ketone A( $ C_{4}H_{8}O $) undergoes haloform reaction, So the Ketone should have -C=O-CH3 group. So the structure of A is $ CH_{3}-CH_{2}-C-CH_{3} $.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.134Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2370, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The compound [B] formed can be prepared from reaction of aq.KOH. with:', NULL, '[{"text":"$\\mathrm{CH_{3}CH_{2}CH_{2}-Cl}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{CH_{3}-\\overset{\\mathrm{Cl}}{\\underset{\\mathrm{Cl}}{C}}}-\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH_{3}}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{CH_{3}-\\overset{\\mathrm{Cl}}{\\underset{\\mathrm{Cl}}{C}}}-\\mathrm{CH_{2}-CH_{3}}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{CH_{3}-\\overset{\\mathrm{CH_{3}}}{\\underset{\\mathrm{Cl}}{\\mathrm{C}}}-\\mathrm{CH_{3}}}$","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '$ \begin{array}{c} \mathrm{CH}_{3}-\underset{\mathrm{Cl}}{\mathrm{CH}}-\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\ \mathrm{CH}_{3} \end{array} \xrightarrow{\mathrm{Aq.KOH}} \begin{array}{c} \mathrm{CH}_{3}-\underset{\mathrm{OH}}{\mathrm{CH}}-\mathrm{CH}_{2}- \\ \mathrm{OH} \end{array} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.135Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2371, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Compound [E] in presence of dil NaOH gives:', NULL, '[{"text":"But-2-enal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Methanol","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2-Methyl but-2-enal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pent-2-enal","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '$ \text{CH}_3\text{CHO} \xrightarrow{\text{OH}^-} \text{CH}_3\text{-CH=CH-CHO} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.135Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2372, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Compound F on treatment with chlorine, in the presence of small amount of red phosphorus, gives:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ CH_{3}CH_{2}-Cl $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ CH_{3}COCl $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ ClCH_{2}COOH $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ ClCH_{2}CH_{2}-Cl $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '$ \text{CH}_3\text{COOH} + \text{Cl}_2 \xrightarrow{\text{Red Phosphorus}} \text{Cl} - \text{CH}_2\text{COOH} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.136Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2373, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The boiling point of [A] observed is exceptionally high because of:

(a) Intermolecular-H-bond

(b) Intramolecular-H-bond

(c) Like interaction

(d) Dipole-Dipole interaction
Direction (Q46-Q50) Answer the questions on basis of passage given below:

The noble gases He to Rn have close shell configuration and are monoatomic gases under normal conditions. Though mostly unreactive, but direct reaction of Xe with $ F_{2} $ leads to a series of compounds with Xe oxidation numbers +2, +4 and +6. When certain compounds like phenol and quinol are crystallised in the presence of noble gas such as Ar, Kr and Xe a category of compound called clathrates are formed. In these the noble gas atoms are trapped in the cavities of the crystal lattices. The compounds which crystallise are known as hosts (H) while the noble gas atoms are called guests (G). The general formula of a clathrate compound is $ nHmG $, where n is the number of host molecules and m is the number of atoms a molecule of guest.

In what molar ratio must Xe and F_{2} be taken to give XeF_{4}?', NULL, '[{"text":"1:1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1:2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2:1","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1:5","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Boiling points of aldehydes and ketone depend on intermolecular dipole-dipole attraction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.137Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2374, 5, NULL, NULL, 'XeF $ _{4} $ and XeF $ _{6} $ are:', NULL, '[{"text":"reducing agent","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"oxidising agent","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"unreactive","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"strongly basic","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ 6\text{XeF}_4 + 12\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow 4\text{Xe} + 2\text{XeO}_3 + 24\text{HF} + 3\text{O}_2 $

$ \text{XeF}_6 + 3\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{XeO}_3 + 6\text{HF} $

$ \text{XeF}_4 $ and $ \text{XeF}_6 $ are expected to be oxidizing because in both the reactions $ \text{XeF}_4 $ and $ \text{XeF}_6 $ both caused the oxidation.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.138Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2375, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which force is responsible for holding Ar in its clathrate compound with quinol?', NULL, '[{"text":"Van der Waal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hydrogen bond","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ionic bond","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Covalent bond","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Unlike hydrates, inorganic clathrates have a covalently bonded framework of inorganic atoms with guests typically consisting of alkali or alkaline earth metals.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.139Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2376, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. $ SF_{4} $ molecular geometry is see-saw with one pair of valence electrons. The nature of the molecule is polar.

See-saw shape

B. $ BrF_{3} $ molecular geometry is said to be T-shaped or Trigonal Bipyramidal

C. Overall, the shape and expected hybridization of $\mathrm{BrO}_{3}^{-}$ is trigonal pyramidal

D. Xenon oxyfluoride (Xe OF₄) molecular geometry is square pyramidal.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q49-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 49', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.140Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-05-shift-1/q49-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 49","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2377, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which factors are responsible for making fluorine the strongest oxidising agent?

(A) Highest electronegativity

(B) High electron gain enthalpy

(C) High bond dissociation enthalpy

(D) Small size of flourine', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (C) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Fluorine is a much stronger oxidizing agent than chlorine. The oxidizing power depends on three factors.

1. Bond dissociation energy

2. Electron gain enthalpy

3. Hydration enthalpy

The electron gain enthalpy of chlorine is more negative than that of fluorine. However, the bond dissociation energy of fluorine is much lesser than that of chlorine. Also, because of its small size, the hydration energy of fluorine is much higher than that of chlorine. Therefore, the latter two factors more than compensate for the less negative electron gain enthalpy of fluorine. Thus, fluorine is a much stronger oxidizing agent than chlorine.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.141Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2378, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Tetracarbonylnickel (O) - Ni(CO)₄

B. Tetraammineaquachloridocobalt (III) chloride - [Co(NH₃)₄(H₂O)Cl]Cl₂

C. Potassium tetrahydroxidozincate (II) - K₂[Zn(OH)₄]

D. Dichloridobis (ethane-1,2-diamine)cobalt(III) - [CoCl₂(en)₂]⁺', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q01-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 1', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.142Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q01-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 1","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2379, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Cheese is a gel (type of colloid). In it, the dispersed phase is liquid (water) and dispersion medium is solid (fats).

B. In a sol, solid particles are put in a continuous liquid to make the colloid. The dispersing medium is liquid and the dispersed phase is solid. Cell fluid contains many solid particles which are in a colloidal range flowing through it. So cell fluid is a sol.

C. In hair cream, both the dispersion medium and dispersed phase are liquids, hence it is an example of emulsion.

D. When the liquid particles are suspended in a gaseous medium, the nature of the colloid is a liquid aerosol. Hence clouds are aerosols.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 2', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.145Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q02-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 2","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2380, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Seven crystal systems and its lattice Parameters', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q03-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 3', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.148Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q03-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 3","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2381, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Molar conductance of KCl increase slowly with the decrease in concentration because of the weakening of inter-ionic attractions and increase in ionic mobilities.

B. Conductivity is directly proportional to the number of ions present per unit volume of the solution. When we dilute the acetic acid solution, its degree of dissociation increases', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q04-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 4', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.149Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q04-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 4","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2382, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Glucose on reaction with bromine water forms gluconic acid which confirms the presence of:', NULL, '[{"text":"COOH group","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"CHO group","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Five - OH groups","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ketonic group","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Glucose on oxidation with bromine water yields gluconic acid. This reaction confirms presence of aldehyde group because for formation of gluconic acid free aldehyde group must be present.

$ \begin{array}{c} \mathrm{CHO} \\ \mathrm{(CHOH)_{4} \xrightarrow{Br_{2}/H_{2}O} (O) \quad (CHOH)_{4}} \\ \mathrm{CH_{2}OH} \\ \mathrm{Glucose} \end{array} $

$ \begin{array}{c} \mathrm{COOH} \\ \mathrm{(CHOH)_{4}} \\ \mathrm{CH_{2}OH} \\ \mathrm{Gluconic~Acid} \end{array} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.149Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2383, 5, NULL, NULL, '$\begin{array}{l}\mathrm{Ph}-\mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{CH}_{3}\xrightarrow[\Delta]{\mathrm{alc.KCN}}?\\\mathrm{Cl}\\(+)\end{array}$

Product formed is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\begin{array}{c}\\mathrm{CN}\\\\(\\pm)\\end{array}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ph- $ \\begin{array}{c}CH \\\\ C N(+)\\end{array} $CH $ _{3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Ph - CH - CH_{3} $ \xrightarrow[\Delta]{alc.KCN} $ Ph - CH CH_{3} Cl (+)', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.150Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2384, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following hormone is also known as flight hormone?', NULL, '[{"text":"Adrenaline","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Androgens","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Thyroxine","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Insulin","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Adrenaline is a natural hormone that is produced by the body and secreted throughout the body and helps in regulation of sympathetic and parasympathetic response. It causes an increase in blood pressure, increased breathing, boosting up of energy, etc. This hormone is also called as fight and flight hormone.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.151Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2385, 5, NULL, NULL, 'An analysis of iron oxide shows that its formula is $ \mathrm{Fe}_{1.9}\mathrm{O}_{3} $. What percentages of iron exists as $ \mathrm{Fe}^{3+} $ and $ \mathrm{Fe}^{4+} $ ions:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ Fe^{3+} = 82.98\\% $ and $ Fe^{4+} = 17.02\\% $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ Fe^{3+} = 84.21\\% $ and $ Fe^{4+} = 15.79\\% $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ Fe^{3+} = 15.79\\% $ and $ Fe^{4+} = 84.21\\% $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ Fe^{3+} = 17.02\\% $ and $ Fe^{4+} = 82.98\\% $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Suppose, the number of Fe^{3+} ions in one formula unit of Fe_{1.9}O_{3} = x

So, number of Fe^{4+} ions per formula unit = (1.9 - x).

The number of O atoms per formula unit of Fe_{1.9}O_{3} = 3

In one formula unit of Fe_{1.9}O_{3}, total charge of cations = 3 x x + 4(1.9-x) and total charge of anions = -2x3 = -6

Since crystal of Fe_{1.9}O_{3} is electrically neutral, the sum

total positive charge and total negative charge is equal

to zero.

3 x x + 4(1.9 - x) -6 = 0 or x = 1.6

Hence, in the crystal of Fe_{1.9}O_{3}, the percentage of Fe^{3+}

ions = 1.6/1.9 x 100 = 84.21%

and the percentage of Fe^{4+} ions = (1.9 - 1.6)1.9 x 100 = 15.79%', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.151Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2386, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the name reaction given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"Gatterman Reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sandmeyer Reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Gatterman - Koch Reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dow''s Process","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Sandmeyer Reaction:

It converts aryl diazonium salts to aryl halides. An aromatic amino group is substituted with a nucleophile (such as halide anions, cyanide, thiols, water, and others) via diazonium salt intermediate. The reaction is catalyzed by cuprous compounds.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q09-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 9', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.152Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q09-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 9","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2387, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. Williamson synthesis:

It is used for the preparation of simple as well as

mixed ethers. Alkyl halide is heated with alcoholic

sodium or potassium alkoxide to form

corresponding ethers.

$$ \mathrm{R}-\mathrm{ONa}+\mathrm{X}-\mathrm{R}\xrightarrow{\Delta}\mathrm{R}-\mathrm{O}-\mathrm{R}^{\prime}+\mathrm{NaX} $$

Thus, methyl iodide, on heating with alcoholic sodium methoxide forms dimethyl ether.

B. Reimer-Tiemann reaction:

Phenol is converted to salicylaldehyde (ortho hydroxy benzaldehyde) by treatment with NaOH/chloroform. Thus Reimer-Tiemann reaction involves ortho-formylation of phenols.

$$ \mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{5}-\mathrm{OH}\xrightarrow[\mathrm{CHCl}_{3}]{\mathrm{aq~NaOH}}\mathrm{o}-\mathrm{Na}^{+}\mathrm{O}^{-}-\mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{4}-\mathrm{CHCl}_{2} $$

$\xrightarrow{\mathrm{NaOH}}\mathrm{o}-\mathrm{Na}^{+}\mathrm{O}^{-}-\mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{4}-\mathrm{CHO}\xrightarrow{\mathrm{H}^{+}}\mathrm{o}-\mathrm{HO}-\mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{4}-\mathrm{CHO}$

Major product is ortho isomer which is separated from para isomer by steam distillation. Ortho isomer predominates due to its stability due to intramolecular hydrogen bonding.

C. Dow''s process

D. The following reaction is called Schotten Baumann reaction.

$$ \mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{5}\mathrm{NH}_{2}\dot{+}\mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{5}\mathrm{COC}\mathrm{Cl}\xrightarrow{\mathrm{aq}\mathrm{NaOH}}\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{5}\mathrm{NHCOC}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{5}+\mathrm{HCl} $$

Schotten Baumann reaction is benzoylation of compounds containing an active hydrogen such as alcohols, phenols or amines with benzoyl chloride in the presence of dilute aq NaOH solution.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q10-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 10', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.153Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q10-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 10","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2388, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is the correct range of critical micelle concentrations (CMC) for soaps?', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 10^{2} $ to $ 10^{4} $ mol/L","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 10^{-5} $ to $ 10^{-8} $ mol/L","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 10^{-1} $ to $ 10^{-3} $ mol/L","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 10^{-4} $ to $ 10^{-3} $ mol/L","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Range of particle size for colloidal solution is 1 nm - 1000 nm.

CMC $ \Rightarrow $ $ 10^{-4} $ to $ 10^{-3} $

Min. Max.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.154Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2389, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '$ Cu^{+} $ ion has a 3 d $ ^{10} $ electronic configuration. It has a fully filled stable d $ ^{10} $ configuration, thus it requires high energy to remove an electron from the fully filled d orbital. Therefore, Cu has the highest second ionization enthalpy.

B. Zn^{2+} has a 3d^{10} electronic configuration. Zn^{2+} ion is highly stable due to the fully filled d^{10} configuration and thus it requires high energy to remove an electron from the fully filled d orbital. Therefore, Zn has the highest third ionization energy.

C. The M in M(CO) $ _{6} $ is Chromium. A stable complex is formed when its EAN (Effective atomic number) is equal to the atomic number of the nearest noble gas. The nearest noble gas is Kr having atomic number 36

EAN= Total electrons of metal + number of electrons given by ligand

Each CO ligand contributes two electrons.

(x)=36-12=24

24 is the atomic number of chromium.

D. Co is having highest number of unpaired electrons & therefore Co is having highest heat of atomization.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q12-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 12', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.154Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q12-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 12","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2390, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the following compounds in decreasing order of acidity:

(A) o-cresol

(B) Phenol

(C) m-nitrophenol

(D) o-nitrophenol

(E) Ethanol', NULL, '[{"text":"D > B > C > E > A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"E > A > B > C > D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C > D > A > B > E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D > C > B > A > E","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Order of Acidity- o-nitrophenol> m-nitrophenol > phenol> o-cresol> ethanol

o-nitrophenol is more acidic than phenol due to electron withdrawing nature of nitro group. o-cresol is less acidic than alcohol due to the electron-releasing nature of methyl group.

3-nitrophenol or m-nitrophenol is more acidic than phenol due to electron attracting nature of NO₂ group. As we all know NO₂ has both -I and -M effect, so after removal of H⁺ conjugate base will be formed and if it is stabilized it will make easier deprotonation.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.154Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2391, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The vapour pressure of pure Benzene is 0.900 bar. If a nonvolatile electrolytic solid is added, vapour pressure of the solution becomes 0.200 bar. If numbers of moles of solute is 1 and solvent is 2 respectively in solution, what is the value of van''t Hoff factor (i)?', NULL, '[{"text":"2.33","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"0.56","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1.56","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2.00","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '[Hint]: $ \mathrm{p}^{0}_{1}\text{-p}_{1}/\mathrm{p}^{0}_{1}=\mathrm{i}(\mathrm{n}_{2}/\mathrm{n}1) $

(900-200)/900 = I(1/2) = 1.56', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.155Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2392, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. Blood thus becomes negatively charged due to presence of negatively charged heparin in it. Thus, blood is a negatively charged.

B. Congo red is an acidic stain which is negative in charge.

C. Silver sol, As_{2}S_{3} sol, starch sol, silicic acid sol, congo red dye, gum, clay and charcoal are negatively charged sols.

D. Gold sol being a sol of gold (Au) metal is thus, a lyophobic. Metal sols are generally negatively charged. Therefore, gold sol is also a negative charged.

E. Fe(OH)₃ sol contains positively charged colloidal particles.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q15-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 15', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.155Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q15-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 15","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2393, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Out of the following which will not undergo S_{N}1 reaction pathway:', NULL, '[{"text":"1-Chloro-1,1,1-triphenylmethane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2-Iodo-2-methylpropane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-Bromo-3,3-dimethylbutane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3-Bromoprop-1-ene","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '1-Chloro-1,1,1-triphenylmethane is a tertiary halide.

Tertiary Halide undergoes $ S_{N}1 $ faster than secondary and Primary Halide because Carbocation formed in Tertiary Halide is more stable in case of Carbocation formed in Primary Halide.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.155Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2394, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The magnetic nature of elements depends on the presence of unpaired electrons. Identify the configuration of transition elements which shows highest magnetic moment:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 3d^{7} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 3d^{5} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 3d^{8} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 3d^{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The magnetic nature of elements depends on the presence of unpaired electrons. $ 3d^{5} $ configuration of transition elements which shows highest magnetic moment as it has maximum number of unpaired electrons (5 unpaired electrons).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.156Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2395, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Identify incorrect statement about $\mathrm{H}_{2}-\mathrm{O}_{2}$ fuel cell from the following:', NULL, '[{"text":"At cathode $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ is reduced to $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"At anode $H_{2}$ is oxidized to form water","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"The cell runs continuously even if reactants are not supplied","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Water is formed as a by product","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The reactants are continuously supplied from external source. Hence fuel cells run till reactants are active.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.156Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2396, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. Tollens'' test, also known as a silver-mirror test, is a qualitative laboratory test that is used to differentiate between an aldehyde and a ketone. It uses the fact that aldehydes can be more easily oxidized than ketones. This test cannot distinguish between an aldehyde and an $ \alpha $-hydroxy ketone (e.g., hydroxy acetone) [1-4]. During the process, two events occur. First, the aldehyde gets converted into carboxylic acid. Second, the Ag+ ions are reduced to Ag metal, which leaves a shiny appearance inside the test tube, indicating a positive result.

B. Benzene diazonium chloride on reaction with phenol in a basic medium gives p-Hydroxy azobenzene. This is an example of the coupling reaction.

In this type of aromatic electrophilic substitution, the aryldiazonium cation acts as the electrophile whereas the activated arene behaves as a nucleophile; and the resulting diazonium compound is also aromatic in most cases.

C. This is an example of Nucleophilic substitution reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q19-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 19', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.157Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q19-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 19","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2397, 5, NULL, NULL, 'A + B → Nylon 6, 6


Predict A and B:', NULL, '[{"text":"Ethylene glycol + adipic acid","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Pentamethylene diamine + adipic acid","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hexamethylene amine + tartaric acid","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hexamethylene diamine + adipic acid","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Nylon 6,6 is obtained by condensation polymerisation of adipic acid and hexamethylenediamine, Nylon 6, 6 is used in making sheets, bristles for brushes and in the textile industry.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.157Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2398, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'A. $ [CoF_{6}]^{3-} $ is an outer complex having sp $ ^{3} $d $ ^{2} $ hybridization because the complex ion contains weak field ligand so electrons are not paired up and will contain 4 unpaired electrons. Hence the compound is said to be paramagnetic.

B. $ [\mathrm{Co(CN)}_{4}]^{2-} $: oxidation state of Co is +2

Co2+-1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 3d⁷

C. $ [FeCl_{4}]^{-} $ is sp $ ^{3} $ hybridized and has tetrahedral geometry with 5 unpaired electrons.

D. Hybridization of the compound $ [\mathrm{Co}(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{4})_{3}]^{3-} $ is $ d^{2}sp^{3} $. As therefore is no unpaired electron, it is diamagnetic in nature.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q21-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 21', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.157Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q21-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 21","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2399, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II.

