(d)', NULL, '[{"text":"(II),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(III),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(IV),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Roasting is the process of converting an ore into oxide by heating in the presence of air. It is done for sulphide ores.

So. PbS $ \rightarrow $ PbO (Roasting)

B. Calcination is the process in which ore is heated below its melting point in the limited supply of oxygen

Decomposition of carbonate ore

CaCO_{3} \rightarrow CaO (Calcination)

C. Extraction of zinc: Zinc is extracted through carbon reduction of the ZnS.

ZnS $ \rightarrow $ Zn Carbon reduction

D. $ Cu_{2}S \rightarrow Cu $ (Self reduction)', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q24-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 24', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.158Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q24-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 24","kind":"table"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q24-table-2.jpg","alt":"Table for question 24","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
