2. Which of the following is the correct formula of a colligative property?', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{P_{1}\\cdot P_{1}}{P_{1}\\cdot\\dot{v}}=x_{1} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\Delta T_{b}=\\frac{K_{b}\\times1000\\times w_{2}}{M_{1}\\times w_{1}} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\Delta T_{f}=\\frac{K_{f}\\times1000\\times w_{2}}{M_{2}\\times w_{1}} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\pi-\\Delta T\\cdot PT $ (d) $ \\pi = \\Delta T_f RT $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'ethanol - acetone: It is a non-ideal solution and has a positive deviation. It is a minimum boiling azeotrope.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.164Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2405, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The amount of radioactive substance left after 75 hrs, when 100g of it is taken initially will be:

(half-life of radioactive substance is 15 hrs)

(a) 12.5 g

(b) 6.25 g

(c) 1.5625 g

(d) 3.125 g

35. The cell Zn\ | Zn^{2+} + (1M)\ | | Cu^{2+} + (1M) Cu. (E_{Cell}^{\circ} = 1.10V)

Was allowed to be completely discharged at 298 K. The relative concentration of Zn^{2+}/Cu^{2+} is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 9.65 \\times 10^{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Antilog 24.8","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"37.7","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 10^{37.3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Initial mass = M0 = 100 g

$ t_{1/2} $ = 15 hrs

to calculate, mass of the substance left undecayed

after 75 hrs (Mz = 75)

we know,

$ M(z) = M_0 e^{-\lambda t} $

$ M_0/2 = M_0 e^{-\lambda(15)} $

$ \lambda = 1/15 \ln(2) $

$ M_{(75)} = M_0 e^{-\lambda(75)} $

$ M_{(75)} = M_0 e^{-1/15 \ln(2),75} $

$ M_{(75)} = M_0 e^{-5 \ln(2)} $

$ M_{(75)} = 100/32 = 3.125 $ g', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.165Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
