Choose the correct answer from the options given below:

(a) (A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)

$$ \mathrm{A})-\mathrm{(I)},(\mathrm{B})-(\mathrm{II}),(\mathrm{C})-(\mathrm{IV}),(\mathrm{D})-(\mathrm{III}) $$

(c) (A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)

(d)', NULL, '[{"text":"(II),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(III),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(I),","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A. Adenine is a purine, one of the two families of nitrogenous bases.

B. Thymine is one of the pyrimidine bases found in the nucleic acid of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA), along with adenine, guanine, and cytosine (A, G, and C, respectively).

C. Uracil (U) is one of the four nucleotide bases in RNA

D. deoxyribose, also called d-2-deoxyribose, five-carbon sugar component of DNA (q.v.; deoxyribonucleic acid), where it alternates with phosphate groups to form the "backbone" of the DNA polymer and binds to nitrogenous bases.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q37-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 37', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.167Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q37-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 37","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2408, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List - I with List - II', NULL, '[{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. Phenelzine is an antidepressant (monoamine oxidase inhibitor).

B. Terfenadine, a bioprecursor prodrug, is an antihistamine used for the treatment of allergic conditions.

C. Codeine is used to relieve mild to moderate pain. It belongs to the group of medicines called narcotic analgesics (pain medicines).

D. Antibiotics are drugs obtained from living matter (microorganism). These are used to kill or prevent the growth of other micro-organism. Antibiotics are very specific in their action. Examples of antibiotics include salvarsan, azodye, prontosil, sulphapyridine etc.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q38-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 38', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.168Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q38-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 38","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2409, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following alkyl halides will undergo $ S_{N}2 $ reaction most readily?', NULL, '[{"text":"1-Bromo-2,2-dimethylpropane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-Bromo-2-methylbutane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-Bromobutane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-Bromo-3-methylbutane","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The steric hindrance to the nucleophile in the S N2 mechanism increases with a decrease in the distance of the substituents from the atom containing the leaving group. Further, the steric hindrance increases with an increase in the number of substituents. Therefore, the increasing order of steric hindrances in the given compounds is as below:

1-Bromobutane < 1-Bromo-3-methylbutane < 1-Bromo-2-methylbutane < 1-Bromo-2,2-dimethylpropane

Hence, the increasing order of reactivity of the given compounds towards SN2 displacement is:

1-Bromo-2,2-dimethylpropane < 1-Bromo-2-methylbutane < 1-Bromo-3-methylbutane < 1-Bromobutane', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.169Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2410, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The correct increasing order of acidic strength is:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ C_{6}H_{5}COOH < C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}COOH < NO_{2}CH_{2}COOH < FCH_{2}COOH $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}COOH < C_{6}H_{5}COOH < NO_{2}CH_{2}COOH < FCH_{2}COOH $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}COOH < C_{6}H_{5}COOH < FCH_{2}COOH < NO_{2}CH_{2}COOH $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ C_{6}H_{5}COOH < FCH_{2}COOH < C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}COOH < NO_{2}CH_{2}COOH $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '-NO_{2}- is more electronegative than fluorine. Thus NO_{2}CH_{2}COOH would be most acidic, followed by FCH_{2}COOH and C_{6}H_{5}COOH.

Higher the stability of conjugate base, higher is the acidity. Hence, C_{6}H_{5}COOH is more acidic than C_{6}H_{5}CH_{2}COOH.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q42-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 42', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.169Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q42-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 42","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q42-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 42","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q42-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 42","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q42-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 42","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2411, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The correct sequence of reagents for the conversion of 3-nitrobromobenzene to 3-nitrobenzoic acid is:', NULL, '[{"text":"Mg/ether, CO₂, H₃O³","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"KCN, LiAlH₄, NaOH","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"KMnO₄/OH⁻, dil.H₂SO₄, CO₂/H⁺","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"AgNO₃ (Ammonical), CO₂, H₃O⁺","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q43-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 43', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.170Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q43-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q43-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q43-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q43-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 43","kind":"figure"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2412, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following is most reactive towards nucleophilic addition reaction?', NULL, '[{"text":"Butanone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Propanone","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ethanal","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Propanal","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The +I effect of the alkyl group increases in the order: Ethanol < Propanol < Propanone < Butanone

The electron density at the carbonyl carbon increases with the increase in the +I effect. As a result, the chances of attack by a nucleophile decrease. Hence, the increasing order of the reactivities of the given carbonyl compounds in nucleophilic addition reactions is:

Butanone < Propanone < Propanal < Ethanal', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 44', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.171Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q44-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q44-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q44-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-07-shift-3/q44-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 44","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2413, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Single bond is not formed by two atoms of:', NULL, '[{"text":"P - P","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"N - N","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"As - As","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Sb - Sb","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The chemistry of nitrogen is dominated by the ease with which nitrogen atoms form double and triple bonds. A neutral nitrogen atom contains five valence electrons: $ 2s^{2} $ $ 2p^{3} $. A nitrogen atom can therefore achieve an octet of valence electrons by sharing three pairs of electrons with another nitrogen atom.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.172Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2414, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Maximum covalency of Nitrogen is:', NULL, '[{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"3","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"4","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"5","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Covalency of an atom in a covalent compound is the number of covalent bonds formed by an atom. Maximum covalency of Nitrogen is 4 (example - ammonium ions).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.172Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2415, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Nitrogen family show reducing characters. Least basic amongst the following is:

(A) SbH_{3}

(B) BiH_{3}

(C) NH_{3}

(D) PH_{3}', NULL, '[{"text":"(C) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '$ BiH_{3} $ is the least base because the size of a central atom of $ BiH_{3} $ is much larger than nitrogen which decreases its basicity.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.173Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2416, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Most stable hydride amongst the following is:

(A) NH_{3}

(B) PH_{3}

(C) AsH_{3}

(D) SbH_{3}

(E) BiH_{3}', NULL, '[{"text":"(A) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(B) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(C) & (D) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(D) & (E) Only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'NH₃ is the most stable hydride among the hydrides of group 15 elements because the strength of E-H (Here E = N, P, As, Sb, or Br) bond decreases down the group due to increase in size of the central atom.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.173Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2417, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Nitrogen family show reducing characters. Least basic amongst the following is:', NULL, '[{"text":"SbH_{3}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"BiH_{3}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"NH_{3}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"PH_{3}","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '$ BiH_{3} $ is the least base because the size of a central atom of $ BiH_{3} $ is much larger than nitrogen which decreases its basicity.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.174Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2418, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Mischmetall consists of a lanthanoid metal (95%) and Iron (~5%) and traces of S, Ca & Al. Mischmetall used for producing bullets contains:', NULL, '[{"text":"S based alloy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mg based alloy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Ca based alloy","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Al based alloy","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Misch metal is an alloy which consists of a lanthanoid metal (~95%) and iron(~5%) and traces of S,C, Ca and Al. It is used in Mg based alloy to produce bullets, shell and lighter-flint.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.176Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2419, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which solutions will have the highest boiling point?', NULL, '[{"text":"1M BaCl_{2} solution","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1M NaCl solution","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1M C_{6}H_{12}O_{6} solution","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1M (NH_{2})_{2}CO solution","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'BaCl_{2} solutions (T_{b} = T_{b}^{\circ} + \Delta T_{b}). As number of ions produced is maximum in BaCl_{2} solution. The colligative property $ \Delta T_{b} $ will be maximum in case of BaCl_{2}.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.178Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2420, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Molecules in solids are held together by dipole-dipole interactions. Identify the polar molecules from the following.

A. Solid SO_{2}

B. NH_{3}

C. Cl_{2}

D. HCl

E. He', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, C and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'A. The SO₂ molecule is Polar one. The molecule has a bent shape like H₂O with C₂ᵥ symmetry. It has a net dipole moment, which is the resultant vector of the two S-O moments. As a result, the SO₂ molecule is polar.

B. Ammonia is a polar molecule because it has a positive charge on one end and a negative charge on the other. This makes it polar because the positive and negative charges are not evenly distributed. The reason ammonia $ (NH_{3}) $ is a polar molecule is due to its uneven distribution of charges.

D. HCl is a polar molecule. This is because the Chlorine (Cl) atom in the HCl molecule is more electronegative and does not share the bonding electrons equally with Hydrogen (H).', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.179Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2421, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The main cause of basicity of oxoacids of phosphorous is:', NULL, '[{"text":"P-H bonds","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"P-OH bonds","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ H_{3}-PO_{3} $ bonds","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hydrogen bonds","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'The H atoms attached to oxygen in P-OH form are ionisable. Hence, we can say that basicity is the property exhibited by the H atoms that are attached to oxygen.

As a result, phosphorous acid, $ H_{3}PO_{3} $ is dibasic as it has two P-OH bonds. Similarly, phosphoric acid, $ H_{3}PO_{4} $ is tribasic as it has three P-OH bonds.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.180Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2422, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-I, C-III, D-II","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'I. Ethanol is a good solvent for fatty and waxy substances. Fats and waxes provide odour to the perfumes. Apart from being a good solvent, it is less irritating to the skin. So, it is used in perfumes.

II. Phenol is converted into picric acid (2, 4, 6-trinitro-phenol) by the reaction of phenol with conc. HNO_{3}.

2.4.6-Trinitrophenol (Picric acid)

III. Methanol, $ CH_{3}OH $ is also known as ''wood spirit'' as it was produced by the destructive distillation of wood.

IV. Soaps are prepared by the reactions of fatty acid with NaOH.

$$ \begin{array}{ccc}O&\quad&\quad\\ |&\quad&\quad\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\mathrm{O}-\mathrm{C}-\mathrm{OC}_{17}\mathrm{H}_{35}&\quad&\quad\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{OH}\\|\\|&\quad&\quad|\\|&\quad\\ \mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{O}-\mathrm{C}-\mathrm{OC}_{17}\mathrm{H}_{35}+3\mathrm{NaOH}\longrightarrow3\mathrm{C}_{17}\mathrm{H}_{35}\mathrm{COONa}+\mathrm{CHOH}\\ &\quad\text{(solidate)}\\ \\\mid&&\mid\\ \mathrm{CH}_{2}-\mathrm{O}-\mathrm{C}-\mathrm{OC}_{17}\mathrm{H}_{35}&&\mathrm{CH}_{2}\mathrm{OH}\\ &\quad\text{(glycerol)}\\ ||&\quad&\quad\\\mathrm{O}&&\end{array} $$

The glycerol (propan-1, 2, 3-triol) is the byproduct of soap industry and used in cosmetics.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q05-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 5', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.181Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q05-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 5","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2423, 5, NULL, NULL, '$ 2KClO_{3} \xrightarrow{653-873K} 2KCl + 3O_{2} $

On adding manganese dioxide to the above reaction, the subsequent decomposition takes place at', NULL, '[{"text":"Lower temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Higher temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"The same temperature","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Unaltered by temperature change","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'In this reaction, potassium chlorate is decomposed into potassium chloride and oxygen. This is a slow reaction that occurs in the temperature range of 653-873K. If we add manganese dioxide to this reaction, it takes place at an accelerated rate and in the temperature range of 473-633K. Hence manganese dioxide acts as a catalyst in the above reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.182Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2424, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Which of the following colligative property is associated with concentration in terms of molarity?', NULL, '[{"text":"Lowering of vapour pressure","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Depression in freezing point","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Osmotic pressure","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Elevation in boiling point","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '$ \pi=CRT $;

C= Molarity', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.182Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2425, 5, NULL, NULL, 'ZSM-5 is a catalyst used for', NULL, '[{"text":"Converting zinc into aluminium","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Converting alcohols into gasoline","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Converting zeolites into Zinc","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Converting Zinc into Zeolites","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'ZSM-5, a type of zeolite, is used to convert alcohols into gasoline.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.183Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2426, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The IUPAC Name for the complex Hg [Co (SCN) $ _{4} $]', NULL, '[{"text":"Mercury tetrathiocyanatocobaltate (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mercury tetrathiocyanatocobaltate (IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Tetracyanocobalt Mercuric (III)","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Tetrathiocyanato cobalt Mercuric (IV)","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The formula of coordination compound mercury tetrathiocyanato-cobaltate (III) is Hg[Co(SCN) $ _{4} $]. Cobaltate ends with ate. This means that Co is part of complex anion. Thiocyanato is SCN ligand. The prefix tetra means 4. Hg is cation.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.183Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2427, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Above graph is not applicable for which of the following reaction', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 2NH_3(g) \\xrightarrow[\\text{Pt catalyst}]{\\text{1130K}} N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ C_2H_4(g) + H_2(g) \\longrightarrow C_2H_6(g) $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ ^{226}_{88}Ra \\longrightarrow ^{4}_{2}He + ^{222}_{86}Rn $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ N_2O_5(g) \\longrightarrow 2NO_2(g) + \\frac{1}{2}O_2(g) $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The given reaction is zero order and the graph for zero order reaction.', NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q10-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 10', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.184Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q10-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 10","kind":"figure"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2428, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Extraction of gold and silver involves leaching the metal with CN $ ^{-} $ ion. This is also _ for gold for silver', NULL, '[{"text":"Oxidation reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Reduction reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Redox reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Disproportionation reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Extraction of silver and gold involves leaching process for cyanide ion present in that ore. This is an oxidation process because during leaching silver is oxidized to silver cation. The metal then recovered from these complexes by reduction or displacement method using a more electro positive zinc metal.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.185Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2429, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Gallium and Indium can be prepared by', NULL, '[{"text":"Zone refining","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Vapour phage refining","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Mond process","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Van Arkel Method","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Metals refined from zone refining: germanium, silicon, boron, gallium and indium.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.185Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2430, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Benzene $ \xrightarrow[\text{H}_2\text{SO}_4]{\text{HNO}_3} $ P $ \xrightarrow[\text{ethanol}]{\text{H}_2/\text{Pd}} $ Q $ \xrightarrow[\text{(2) CuCl}]{(\text{1) NaNO}_2/\text{HCl}} $ R.

$ \ce{ \chemfig{*6(=-=-=-)} -C(=O)-S-Cl } $ $ \xrightarrow[\text{O}][\text{O}]:\ce{S-CH2-CH2-COOH} $

A.', NULL, '[{"text":"B, A, D, E, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A, B, C, D, E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C, D, B, A, E","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, B, E, A, C","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, '/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-1.jpg', 'Figure for question 13', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.186Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-1.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-2.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-3.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-4.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-5.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-08-shift-3/q13-figure-6.jpg","alt":"Figure for question 13","kind":"figure"}]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2431, 5, NULL, NULL, 'A compound is formed by two elements P and Q. Atoms of the element Q (anions) make hcp lattice and those of element P (cations) occupies $ \frac{1}{8} $th of the tetrahedral voids. What is the formula of the compound?', NULL, '[{"text":"PQ_{4}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"PQ","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"PQ_{2}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"P_{3}Q3","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Let number of atoms of Q in lattice is x

Number of tetrahedral voids = 1/8(2× no. of atoms in hcp)

So number of atoms of P in lattice is 2/8. Hence chemical formula of the compound will be

Px/4Qx = PQ_{4}', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.186Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2432, 5, NULL, NULL, 'The correct shape & hybridisation for XeF_{2} are:', NULL, '[{"text":"linear, sp^{3} d","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"linear, sp^{3} d^{2}","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"trigonal bipyramidal sp^{3} d","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"trigonal bipyramidal sp^{3} d^{2}","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'XeF $ _{2} $ has sp $ ^{3d} $ a hybridization suggesting a Trigonal pyramidal geometry. But as the molecule has 3 lone pairs, hence the shape of the molecule is given as, linear.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.187Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2433, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Feron-12 is manufactured from tetrachloromethane by', NULL, '[{"text":"Wurtz reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Finkelstein reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Swarts reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\beta $-elimination reaction","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Freon-12 is made by $ CCl_{4} $ by the Swarts reaction as shown below:

$ 3CCl_{4} + 2SbF_{3} \rightarrow 3CCl_{2}F_{2} + 2SbCl_{3} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.187Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2434, 5, NULL, NULL, 'What will happen during the electrolysis of aqueous solution of $ CuSO_{4} $ by using platinum electrodes?

A. Copper will deposit at cathode.

B. Copper will deposit at anode

C. Oxygen will be released at anode

D. Copper will dissolve at anode', NULL, '[{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'During the electrolysis of an aqueous solution of CuSO_{4} by using platinum electrodes, the copper will get deposited at the cathode and oxygen will be released at anode.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.188Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2435, 5, NULL, NULL, 'If KMnO_{4} is reduced by oxalic acid in the acidic medium, then the oxidation number of Mn changes from:', NULL, '[{"text":"+4 to +2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"+6 to +4","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"+7 to +2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"+7 to +4","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Reaction involved:

$ \begin{array}{c}

\mathrm{KMnO}_{4} + \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{4} + \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{SO}_{4} \rightarrow \mathrm{K}_{2} \mathrm{SO}_{4} + \mathrm{MnSO}_{4} + \mathrm{CO}_{2} + \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O} \\

\mathrm{Assiqn} \quad \mathrm{the} \quad \mathrm{oxidation} \quad \mathrm{number} \quad \mathrm{to} \quad \mathrm{Mn} \\

\mathrm{Let} \quad \mathrm{the} \quad \mathrm{oxidation} \quad \mathrm{number} \quad \mathrm{of} \quad \mathrm{Mn} \quad \mathrm{be}^{\prime} \quad \mathrm{x}^{\prime}. \\

\mathrm{Oxidation} \quad \mathrm{number} \quad \mathrm{of} \quad \mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-} = \mathrm{O} = -2, \quad \mathrm{K} = +1.

\end{array} $

In $ \mathrm{KMnO}_{4} $: $ 1 + x + 4 \times (-2) = 0 $

$ x + 1 - 8 = 0 $ or $ x = +7 $

In $ \mathrm{MnSO}_{4} $: $ x + (-2) = 0 $

$ x = +2 $ in the reaction thus:

$ \begin{array}{c}

+7 \\

\mathrm{KMnO}_{4} + \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{4} + \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{SO}_{4} \rightarrow \mathrm{K}_{2} \mathrm{SO}_{4} + \mathrm{MnSO}_{4} + \mathrm{CO}_{2} + 8 \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O} \\

\mathrm{When} \quad \mathrm{KMnO}_{4} \quad \mathrm{is} \quad \mathrm{reduced} \quad \mathrm{with} \quad \mathrm{oxalic} \quad \mathrm{acid} \quad \mathrm{in} \quad \mathrm{acidic} \\

\mathrm{solution}, \quad \mathrm{the} \quad \mathrm{oxidation} \quad \mathrm{number} \quad \mathrm{of} \quad \mathrm{Mn} \quad \mathrm{changes} \quad \mathrm{from} +7 \quad \mathrm{to} +2.

\end{array} $', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.188Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2436, 5, NULL, NULL, 'In a coordination entity the central atoms or ions are referred to as:', NULL, '[{"text":"Neutral entity","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lewis base","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Lewis acid","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Amphoteric entity","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'In complex compounds, central atom is bonded with legends through the coordinate bond in which lone pair of ligand is coordinated in the valence shell of central metal.

Lewis acid => an electron pair acceptor', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.188Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2437, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Experimentally determined molar mass is always lower than the true value in case of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Strong electrolytes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Weak electrolytes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Non-electrolytes","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Dimers","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'When there is dissociation of solute into ions, in dilute solutions (ignoring interionic attractions) the number of particles increases. As the value of colligative properties depends on the number of particles of the solute, the experimentally observed value of colligative property will be higher than the true value, therefore the experimentally determined (observed) molar mass is always lower than the true value. For KCl(electrolyte) the experimentally determined molar mass is always lower than the true value when water is used as solvent. Glucose (non-electrolyte) does not show a large variation from the true value.', NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.189Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2438, 5, NULL, NULL, '$ \ce{C4H8O2 + CH3MgBr ->[H3O+] C4H10O} $

Ester(A) (2 Parts) $ \xrightarrow{\ce{Alcohol(B)}} $

The alcohol (B) react the fastest with Lucas reagent.

The ester (A) & alcohol (B) are respectively:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\ce{CH3COC2H5} $; $ \\ce{(CH3)3COH} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{HCOC3H7} $; $ \\ce{(CH3)2CHOH} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{CH3COC2H5} $; $ \\ce{(CH3)2CHOH} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\ce{HCOC3H7} $; $ \\ce{(CH3)3COH} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2023, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:05.189Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2439, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Match List I with List II', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-IV, C-III, D-II","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'A.

