(c) Numpy (d) Series

36. Consider the ''Sale'' Table and ''Model'' Table from the Bike Showroom and answer the questions.

Choose the correct SQL query to display the sum of commission earned by Emp_ID E2, E8 and E6', NULL, '[{"text":"Select * from Sale where sum(Commission) in E2, E8, E6;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select sum(Commission) from Sale where Emp_ID in (''E2'', ''E8'', ''E8'');","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select sum(Commission) from Sale where Emp_ID between [''E1'', ''E8'');","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select * from Sale where sum(Commission) = Emp_ID(''E2'', ''E8'', ''E6'');","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'matplot lib $ \rightarrow $ is a comprehensive library for creating static animated and interactive visualizations in python.', NULL, NULL, 2022, '/local-papers/assets/computer-science-2022/q35-table-1.jpg', 'Table for question 35', NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.290Z', NULL, NULL, '[{"url":"/local-papers/assets/computer-science-2022/q35-table-1.jpg","alt":"Table for question 35","kind":"table"},{"url":"/local-papers/assets/computer-science-2022/q35-table-2.jpg","alt":"Table for question 35","kind":"table"}]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3962, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the correct query to display the customer ID and number of bikes purchased if the customer has purchased more than 1 bikes from Sale Table:', NULL, '[{"text":"Select CustID, count(*) \"No of bike\" From Sale Group by CustID;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select * from Sale having count(*) > 1;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select CustID, count(*) from Sale Group By CustID having count(*) > 1;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select CustID, count(*) from Sale Group By InvoiceNo;","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Select Cust ID, count (*) from sale grouping cust ID. having count (*) > 1;

This query shows only Customer ID having bought more than 1 bike.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.291Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3963, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the correct query to display number of bikes purchased by each customer from Sale Table:', NULL, '[{"text":"Select * from Sale;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select CustID, Count(*) As \"No. of bikes\" from Sale Group by CustID;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select CustID, count \"No of bikes\" from Sale;","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Select BikeID from Sale;","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Select Cust ID, count (*) As "no. of bikes" from sale group by Cust ID:

Count (*) will count the no. of times a cust ID repeats and will show a table which Cust ID. no. of bikes as a column of table.

39. (*) Sql query to display the sole price of only those bikes which are manufactured by Yamaha.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.291Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3964, 7, NULL, NULL, 'With reference to the tables MODEL and SALE from the database BIKE show room, which operation can be performed on the two tables?', NULL, '[{"text":"Union","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Intersection","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cartesian Product","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Difference","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'i. Union (◯) → show all values and common only once.

ii. Intersection $ (\cap) \rightarrow $ shows common to both tables

iii. Cartesian product (×) → multiplication of table 1 × table 2 rows.

iv. Difference (-) → subtract common of two table from table one and show only first table. Answer is (a) union because only option that satisfy the condition. Result table will be (Table sale + Table model - Bike ID (Common))', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.293Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3965, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Aditi submitted project and presented work of Kamakshi as her own work. This act of Aditi is an example of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Copyright Infringement","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hacking","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Plagiarism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Cracking","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'i. Copyright Infringement → is the use or production of copyright protected material without the permission of the copyright holder.

iii. Plagiarism $ \rightarrow $ The act of copying another persons ideas, words or work and pretending they are your own;

ii. Hocking $ \rightarrow $ Hocking refers to activities that seek to compromise digital devices, such as computers, smartphones, tablets and even entire networks.

iv. Cracking → Trying to get into computer system in order to steal, corrupt, or illegitimately view data. From the above context given plagiarism is the act perform by Aditi.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.294Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3966, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Aditi''s social account shows some posts made by Aditi, though Aditi has not actually posted them. This act of posting content by someone else on your name is an example of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Ransomware","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Copyright Infringement","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Patent Violation","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Identify theft","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'i. Ransomware $ \rightarrow $ A type of malicious software designed to block access to a computer system mitt a sum of money x paid.

ii. Patent violation → violation of a patent owner''s rights with respect to some invention.

iii. Identity theft $ \rightarrow $ When some one steal your information like name, number, id etc.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.295Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3967, 7, NULL, NULL, 'The act of Aditi of copying data from internet without obtaining permission from the owner [or without paying for it, if it is being sold] is an example of:', NULL, '[{"text":"Plagiarism","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Trademark Infringement","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Copyright Infringement","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Hacking","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'This act is called copyright infringement. Copyright infringement $ \rightarrow $ The act of copying any data or work protected by copyright without permission for the usage of his own work.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.296Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3968, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Aditi should manage the ewaste properly:

(A) She should not throw the ewaste in water

(B) She should reuse the electronic waster after making slight modification

(C) She can sell her ewaste to an NGO which recycles the ewaste into some useful product

(D) She can burn the ewaste and get rid of it

(E) She can throw all her ewaste in the domestic garbage bin', NULL, '[{"text":"(A), (D) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (C) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (E) only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"(A), (B) and (D) only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, '(2) $ \rightarrow $ A, B, C

i. Ewaste should not be burnt, it generate toxic gases which are harmful.

ii. Ewaste should not be thrown directly to the domestic garbage as it can harmful for humans does well as animals.

Option A, B, C are correct for Ewaste management.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.297Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3969, 7, NULL, NULL, 'The term which has been derived from the literal practice of secretly listening to the conversations of people by standing under roof of a house?', NULL, '[{"text":"Snooping","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Routing","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Buffering","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Evasdropping","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'i. Snooping → look around place secretly, in order to disorder things or find information about someone or something.

ii. Routing $ \rightarrow $ Deciding route for a signal.

iii. Buffering $ \rightarrow $ Temporary storage.

iv. Evasdropping $ \rightarrow $ Practice of actually standing under the caves of a house, listening to conversations inside.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:17.298Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3970, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Identify the statistical function for analysis of data provided by pandas:', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\max() $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"rename()","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\text{tail}() $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\text{mod}() $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Tail () → method returns a specified no. of last rows. → Tail method returns the last 5 rows is a number is not specified.

→ Tail is a function in pandas used for analysis of data.

