(E) 4', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D and E only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'If $ f(x) = |x - a| $

then $ f(x) $ is not differentiable at x = a', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.902Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4861, 3, NULL, NULL, 'A window is in the form of a rectangle surmounted by an equilateral triangle. If the perimeter of the window is 10m. Find the side of triangle to admit maximum light. Write the steps to solve this problem in correct order.

A. Assume side of triangle as x and other side of rectangle as y

B. Write perimeter: $3x + 2y = 10$ and area (A) = $xy + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}x^{2}$

C. Put $\frac{\mathrm{d}A}{\mathrm{d}x}=0$ to get value of $x$

D. Write area (A) in terms of x and find $\frac{\mathrm{d}A}{\mathrm{d}x}$

E Check $\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2}A}{\mathrm{d}x^{2}}<0$ at value of x. Then x is required side of triangle

Choose the correct order from the option given below:

(a) A, B, D, C, E (b) B, A, C, D, E

(c) B, D, A, C, E (d) A, B, C, D, E

$$\int e^{2x}\sin x\,dx =$$', NULL, '[{"text":"$\\frac{e^{2x}}{4}(2\\sin x - \\cos x) + C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{e^{2x}}{5}(2\\cos x - \\sin x) + C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{e^{2x}}{4}(2\\sin x + \\cos x) + C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{e^{2x}}{5}(2\\sin x - \\cos x) + C$","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '$A = \text{Assume the sides } x, y$

$B = \text{Write perimeter and area}$

$C = \text{Equate area to zero}$

$D = \text{Derivate the area}$

$E = \text{Check} \frac{d^{2}A}{dx^{2}} < 0$ at critical points.', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.903Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4862, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Match List-I with List-II

List-I List-II

A. $ \int \frac{1}{\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}} dx $

B. $ \int \frac{-1}{(a^{2}+x^{2})} dx $

C. $ \int \frac{1}{x \sqrt{x^{2}-a^{2}}} dx $

D. $ \int \frac{-1}{\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}} dx $

I. $ \cos^{-1}\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)+C $

II. $ \frac{1}{a}\sec^{-1}\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)+C $

III. $ \frac{1}{a}\cot^{-1}\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)+C $

IV. $ \sin^{-1}\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)+C $', NULL, '[{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'By using formula of integration $ A \to \mathrm{IV}, B \to \mathrm{III}, C \to \mathrm{II}, D \to \mathrm{I} $ (d) is correct answer.

(c) Let $I = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\frac{dx}{1+\tan^{n}x}$, put $\tan x = \frac{\sin x}{\cos x}$

$I = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\frac{\cos^{n}x}{\sin^{n}x + \cos^{n}x}dx \quad \ldots\quad(i)$

By definite integral properly

$I = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\frac{\cos^{n}\left(\frac{\pi}{2} - x\right)}{\sin^{n}\left(\frac{\pi}{2} - x\right) + \cos^{n}\left(\frac{\pi}{2} - x\right)}$

$\Rightarrow I = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\frac{\sin^{n}x}{\cos^{n}x + \sin^{n}x}dx \quad \ldots\quad(ii)$

Add equations (i) and (ii),

$2I = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\frac{\cos^{n}x + \sin^{n}x}{\cos^{n}x + \sin^{n}x}dx = \int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}1dx$

$$ 2I=\left[\begin{array}{c}x\end{array}\right]_{0}^{\pi/2}=\frac{\pi}{2}\quad\Rightarrow\quad I=\frac{\pi}{4} $$', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.903Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4863, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Write the values of the following definite integration in increasing order

A. $ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\sin^{5}x\,dx $

B. $ \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\log\left(\frac{4+3\sin x}{4+3\cos x}\right)dx $

C. $ \int_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{3}}\frac{1}{1+\sqrt{\tan x}}\,dx $

D. $ \int_{0}^{1}xe^{x}dx $', NULL, '[{"text":"B<D<A<C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D<B<C<A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B<A<C<D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B<C<A<D","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '(A) Let

$$ I=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\sin^{5}x dx=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}(1-\cos^{2}x)^{2}\sin x dx $$

$$ \Rightarrow I=-\int\limits_{1}^{0}\left(1-t^{2}\right)^{2}dt=\frac{1}{5}-\frac{2}{3}+1=\frac{8}{15} $$

$$ \begin{aligned}&(B)Let I=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\log\left(\frac{4+3\sin x}{4+3\cos x}\right)dx\\&=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\log\left(\frac{4+3\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-x\right)}{4+3\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-x\right)}\right)dx\\&\Rightarrow I=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\log\left(\frac{4+3\cos x}{4+3\sin x}\right)dx\\ \end{aligned} $$

$$ \begin{aligned}&2I=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi/2}\log\left(\frac{4+3\sin x}{4+3\cos x}\right)\left(\frac{4+3\cos x}{4+3\sin x}\right)d x\\ &\Rightarrow2I=0\Rightarrow I=0\\ \end{aligned} $$

$$ \begin{aligned}&(C)\text{Let}I=\int\limits_{\pi/6}^{\pi/3}\frac{1}{1+\sqrt{\tan x}}dx\\&\quad=\int\limits_{\pi/6}^{\pi/3}\frac{\sqrt{\cos x}}{\sqrt{\sin x}+\sqrt{\cos x}}dx\\&=\int\limits_{\pi/6}^{\pi/3}\frac{\sqrt{\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{\pi}{3}-x\right)}}{\sqrt{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{\pi}{3}-x\right)}+\sqrt{\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{\pi}{3}-x\right)}}dx\\&\Rightarrow I=\int\limits_{\pi/6}^{\pi/3}\frac{\sqrt{\sin x}}{\sqrt{\cos x}+\sqrt{\sin x}}dx\\&\quad\Rightarrow2I=\int\limits_{\pi/6}^{\pi/3}\frac{\left(\sqrt{\cos x}+\sqrt{\sin x}\right)}{\sqrt{\cos x}+\sqrt{\sin x}}dx=\frac{\pi}{3}-\frac{\pi}{6}\\&\quad\Rightarrow I=\frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{\pi}{3}-\frac{\pi}{6}\right]=\frac{\pi}{12}\end{aligned} $$

$$ \begin{aligned}&(D)\operatorname{Let}I=\int\limits_{0}^{1}x\,e^{x}\,dx\\ &\Rightarrow I=x e^{x}-\int\limits_{0}^{1}e^{x}\,dx\\ &\Rightarrow I=\begin{bmatrix}x e^{x}-e^{x}\end{bmatrix}=(\mathrm{e}^{1}-e^{1})-(0-1)=1\\ &\operatorname{So},D>A>C>B\\ \end{aligned} $$', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.904Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4864, 3, NULL, NULL, '$ \int \frac{\sin(x + \alpha)}{\sin x} \, dx = $', NULL, '[{"text":"$ x \\cos \\alpha + \\sin \\alpha \\log(\\sin x) + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ x \\cos \\alpha - \\sin \\alpha \\log(\\sin x) + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ x \\sin \\alpha + \\cos \\alpha \\log(\\sin x) + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ x \\sin \\alpha - \\cos \\alpha \\log(\\cos x) + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '$ \int \frac{\sin(x + \alpha)}{\sin x} dx = \int \left( \frac{\sin x \cos \alpha + \cos x \sin \alpha}{\sin x} \right) dx $

$ = \int \cos \alpha \, dx + \int \cot x \sin \alpha \, dx $

$ = x \cos \alpha + \sin \alpha \log (\sin x) + C $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.905Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4865, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The solution of differential equation $ xy \, dy = (x^2 + y^2) \, dx \, is $', NULL, '[{"text":"$ y^2 = -x^2 \\log(Cx) $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ y = x^2 \\log x $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ y^2 = x \\log(Cx) $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ y^2 = 2x^2 \\log(Cx) $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '$ \frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{x^{2} + y^{2}}{xy} $

Let $ y = Vx \Rightarrow \frac{dy}{dx} = V + x \frac{dV}{dx} $

$$V + x\frac{dv}{dx} = \frac{x^{2} + V^{2}x^{2}}{Vx^{2}}$$

$$\Rightarrow V + x\frac{dV}{dx} = \frac{1 + V^{2}}{V} \Rightarrow x\frac{dV}{dx} = \frac{1}{V}$$

$$\Rightarrow VdV = \frac{dx}{x}$$

$$\Rightarrow \frac{V^{2}}{2} = \log x + \log c \Rightarrow \frac{y^{2}}{2x^{2}} = \log c$$

(a) (A) distance of (3, 4, 5) from (0, 4, 0) is

$ d=\sqrt{(3-0)^{2}+0+(5-0)^{2}}=\sqrt{34} $

(B) $ B \to III $

(C) Projection $ =\frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{b}|}=\frac{2}{\sqrt{6}} $

(D) $ \cos\theta = \frac{\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b}}{|\vec{a}||\vec{b}|} = \frac{1}{3} \Rightarrow \theta = \cos^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right) $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.905Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4866, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The shortest distance of the point (3,-2,1) from the plane x+2y-2z+9=0 is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"12","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"2","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Given the plane, $ x + 2y - 2z + 9 = 0 $

Now, required distance

$ =\frac{\left|3\cdot1+(-2)\cdot2+1\cdot(-2)+9\right|}{\sqrt{1^{2}+2^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} $

$ =\frac{\left|3-4-2+9\right|}{\sqrt{1+4+4}}=\frac{6}{3}=2 $ unit', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.906Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4867, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Arrange the distance between the following planes to the plane $ x + y - z + 2 = 0 $ in ascending order:

A. $ x + y - z + 5 = 0 $

B. $ 2x + 2y - 2z + 5 = 0 $

C. $ 3x + 3y - 3z + 9 = 0 $

D. $ \frac{1}{2}x + \frac{1}{2}y - \frac{1}{2}z + 1 = 0 $', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, C, D","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, B, C, A","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, A, D, C","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, B, A, C","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given the plane $ x + y - z + 2 = 0 $

(A) The plane $ x + y - z + 5 = 0 $

So, required distance

$ =\frac{|5-2|}{\sqrt{1^{2}+1^{2}+1^{2}}}=\frac{3}{\sqrt{3}}=\sqrt{3} $ unit

(B) The plane $ x + y - z + \frac{5}{2} = 0 $

So, required distance

$$ = \frac{\left|\frac{5}{2} - 2\right|}{\sqrt{1+1+1}} = \frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{6} \text{ unit} $$

(C) The plane is $ x + y - z + 3 = 0 $

So, required distance

$$ = \frac{\left|3 - 2\right|}{\sqrt{1+1+1}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} \text{ unit} $$

(D) The plane is $ x + y - z + 2 = 0 $

So, required distance

$$ = \frac{\left|2 - 2\right|}{\sqrt{1+1+1}} = 0 \text{ unit So } D, B, C, $$

37. (bonus), Let $ \frac{x-4}{2}=\frac{y}{3}=\frac{z+2}{4}=t $

$ \Rightarrow x=2t+4, y=3t, z=4t-2 $

Now, $ 2(2t+4)-2(3t)+4t-2=0 $

$\Rightarrow 4t+8-6t+4t-2=0$

$\Rightarrow 2t+6=0 \Rightarrow t=-3$

So, the point is $(-2,-9,-14)$.

Now, required distance

$=\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-9)^{2}+(-14)^{2}}$

$=\sqrt{4+81+196}=\sqrt{281}$ unit', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.907Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4868, 3, NULL, NULL, 'If A and B are independent events such that P(A) = $ \frac{1}{4} $ and P(B) = $ \frac{1}{2} $, then P(A'' / B'') is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{3}{4} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{8} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Given, $ P(A)=\frac{1}{4} $, $ P(B)=\frac{1}{2} $

Now,

$ P\left(\frac{A^{\prime}}{B^{\prime}}\right)=\frac{P(A^{\prime}\cap B^{\prime})}{P(B^{\prime})}=\frac{1-P(A\cup B)}{1-P(B)} $

$ = \frac{1 - (P(A) + P(B) - P(A \cap B))}{1 - \frac{1}{2}} $

$ = 2\left(1 - \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{4} \times \frac{1}{2}\right) = \frac{3}{4} $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.907Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4869, 3, NULL, NULL, 'A random variable has the following probability distribution:

$ P(X=x) \quad k \quad \frac{1}{4} \quad 6k \quad 4k \quad k $

Which of the following statements are correct?

A. $ k = \frac{1}{10} $

B. $ P(X=3) = \frac{1}{4} $

C. $ P(X<2) = \frac{11}{16} $

D. $ P(1<X<4) = \frac{5}{8} $

E. $ P(X=4) = \frac{1}{8} $', NULL, '[{"text":"A, B, E only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, C, D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B, D only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"D, E only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, '(A) We know, P(x=0≤x≤4)=1

$ \Rightarrow k+\frac{1}{4}+6k+4k+k=1 \Rightarrow 12k=\frac{3}{4} $

$ \Rightarrow k=\frac{1}{16} $

(B) P(x=3)=4 $ \times\frac{1}{16}=\frac{1}{4} $

(C) P(x<2)=k+\frac{1}{4}=\frac{1}{16}+\frac{1}{4}=\frac{5}{16} $

(D) P(1<x<4)=6k+4k=10k= $ \frac{10}{16}=\frac{5}{8} $

(E) P(x=4)=k= $ \frac{1}{16} $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.908Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4870, 3, NULL, NULL, 'In a linear programming problem, Maximize $ z = 3x + 9y $, the corner points are $ (0, 10) $, $ (5, 5) $, $ (15, 15) $ and $ (0, 20) $, z is maximum at

A. $ (0,10) $

B. $ (5,5) $

C. $ (15,15) $

D. $ (0,20) $', NULL, '[{"text":"A and B only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"A and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"B and C only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"C and D only Passage Rahul went to a park with his younger brother and observed that park is circular and a pavement running around it. He asked the gardener about the radius of the park and found it to be 15m. And the pavement is 2m broad. Answer the following questions based on the above information.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Given, $ z = 3x + 9y $

Now, $ Z_{(0,10)} = 0 + 9 \times 10 = 90 $

$ Z_{(5,5)} = 3.5 + 9.5 = 60 $

$ Z_{(15,15)} = 3.15 + 9.15 = 180 $

$ Z_{(0,20)} = 0 + 9.20 = 180 $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.908Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4871, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The area of the circular park, using integration, is given by

(a) $ \int_{0}^{15}\sqrt{225-x^{2}}dx $

(b) $ \int_{0}^{15}\sqrt{15-x^{2}}dx $

(c) $ \int_{0}^{15}\sqrt{225-x^{2}}dx $

(d) $ \int_{0}^{15}\sqrt{15-x^{2}}dx $

The integral $\sqrt{225-x^{2}}$ can be solved using $t$', NULL, '[{"text":"$\\frac{x}{2}\\sqrt{x^{2}-a^{2}}-\\frac{a^{2}}{2}\\log\\left|x+\\sqrt{x^{2}-a^{2}}\\right|+C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{x}{2}\\sqrt{x^{2}+a^{2}}+\\frac{a^{2}}{2}\\log\\left|x+\\sqrt{x^{2}+a^{2}}\\right|+C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{x}{2}\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}+\\frac{a^{2}}{2}\\sin^{-1}\\frac{x}{a}+C$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$\\frac{x}{2}\\sqrt{a^{2}-x^{2}}-\\frac{a^{2}}{2}\\sin^{-1}\\frac{x}{a}+C$","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Equation of circle, $ x^{2} + y^{2} = (15)^{2} $

$ x = 15\sin\theta $, $ dx = 15\cos\theta\,d\theta $

$ A = 4\int\limits_{0}^{r}\sqrt{r^{2}-x^{2}}\,dx $ where $ r=15 $

$ A = 4\int\limits_{0}^{15}\sqrt{225-x^{2}}\,dx $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.911Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4872, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The area of the pavement running around the circular park, using integration, is given by', NULL, '[{"text":"$4\\int_{0}^{17}\\sqrt{17-x^{2}}dx$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$4\\int_{0}^{17}\\sqrt{289-x^{2}}dx$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$$ \\left(4\\int\\limits_{0}^{17}\\sqrt{17-x^{2}}\\ d x\\right)-\\left(4\\int\\limits_{0}^{15}\\sqrt{15-x^{2}}\\ d x\\right) $$","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\left(4\\int\\limits_{0}^{17}\\sqrt{289-x^{2}} \\mathrm{d}x\\right)-\\left(4\\int\\limits_{0}^{15}\\sqrt{225-x^{2}} \\mathrm{d}x\\right) $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Area of pavement = Total area - area of park

$ A = 4 \int_{0}^{17} \sqrt{289 - x^{2}} dx - 4 \int_{0}^{15} \sqrt{225 - x^{2}} dx $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.912Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4873, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The area of the circular pavement is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ 289\\pi $ sq units","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 225\\pi $ sq units","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 514\\pi $ sq units","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ 64\\pi $ sq units","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '$ A = 4 \int_{0}^{17} \sqrt{289 - x^{2}} dx - 4 \int_{0}^{15} \sqrt{225 - x^{2}} dx $

