The area enclosed by the curve $ y^{2}=4ax $ and its latus rectum is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{8}{3}a^{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{4}{3}a^{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{3}a^{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{1}{12}a^{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, '$f(a)=1$ and $f(a)=3$, which is not possible for any function', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.923Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4886, 3, NULL, NULL, '$ \int \frac{xe^{x}}{(x+1)^{2}} dx = $', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{e^{x}}{x+1} + c $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{e^{x}}{x-1} + c $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x}{x+1} + c $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x}{x-1} + c $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '$ \int \frac{xe^x}{(x+1)^2} dx = \int e^x \left[ \frac{x+1-1}{(x+1)^2} \right] dx $

$ \therefore \int e^x [f(x) + f''(x)] dx = e^x f(x) + C $

$ = \int e^x \left[ \frac{1}{x+1} - \frac{1}{(x+1)^2} \right] dx = \frac{e^x}{1+x} + C $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.924Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4887, 3, NULL, NULL, 'The solution of the differential equation

$ (x+1)\frac{dy}{dx}=1+y\text{ is} $', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{1+y+y^{2}}{1+x^{2}}=C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\log(x+1)-\\log\\left(y+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x+1}{y+1}=C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\log(1+y)-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\log(x+1)=C $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Given differential equation,

$$(x+1)\frac{dy}{dx}=1+y\Rightarrow\frac{dx}{1+x}=\frac{dy}{1+y}$$

$$\Rightarrow\ln(1+x)=\ln(1+y)+\ln C\Rightarrow\ln\left(\frac{1+x}{1+y}\right)=\ln C$$

$$\Rightarrow\frac{1+x}{1+y}=C$$', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.925Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4888, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Derivative of $ x^{3} + 1 $ with respect to $ x^{2} + 1 $ is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ \\frac{2x}{3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x}{3} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x}{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{3x}{2} $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Let $ f(x)=x^{3}+1 $

$ g(x)=x^{2}+1 $

$ \frac{f''(x)}{g''(x)}=\frac{3x^{2}}{2x}=\frac{3}{2}x $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.927Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4889, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Solution of the differential equation $ (x + xy)dy - y(1-x^2)dx = 0 $ is', NULL, '[{"text":"$ y = \\log \\frac{x}{y} - \\frac{x^2}{2} + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ y = \\log \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{x^2}{2} + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ y = \\log xy - \\frac{x^2}{2} + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"$ \\frac{x^2}{2} + \\frac{x^2}{2} + C $","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'The given differential equation

$ (x + xy)dy - y(1 - x^2)dx = 0 $

$ x(1 + y)dy - y(1 - x^2)dx = 0 $

$ \int \frac{(1 + y)}{y} dy = \int \frac{(1 - x^2)}{x} dx $

$ \log y + y = \log x - \frac{x^2}{2} + C $

$ y = \log \frac{x}{y} - \frac{x^2}{2} + C $', NULL, NULL, 2022, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:28.930Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4890, 3, NULL, NULL, 'In linear programming, the optimal function is attained at the points given by', NULL, '[{"text":"intersection of the inequalities with the x-axis only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"intersection of the inequalities with the axes only","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"corner points of the feasible region","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"intersection of the inequalities with the y-axis only","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'The optimal values of the objective function is attained at the corner points of the feasible region.

(d) Since, $xRy, |x-y| \leq 1$

For reflexive $(a,a) \Rightarrow |a-a| = 0 \leq 1$.

$\therefore$ Relation is reflexive,

For symmetric $(a,b) \Rightarrow |a-b| \leq 1$.

$(b,a) \Rightarrow |b-a| \leq 1$.

$\therefore$ Relation is symmetric.

For transitive $(a,b) \Rightarrow |a-b| \leq 1$

$$ (b,c)\Rightarrow|b-c|\leq1 $$

$$ \nearrow\mid a-c\mid\le1 $$

