“The representative walked out as the negotiation broke ___ and no compromise could be made.”', NULL, '[{"text":"down","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"in","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"off","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"with","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Concept:

The phrasal verb break down means to fail, collapse, or stop functioning successfully.

Step 1: Understand the context.

The sentence states that no compromise could be made.

This means the negotiations failed.

Step 2: Recall the phrasal verb.

Negotiations broke down

means

Negotiations failed.

Step 3: Choose the correct option.

down

Therefore,

Option (A)

Quick Tip: Break down = fail or collapse.

Example:

Peace talks broke down after several rounds of discussion.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.389Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5406, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Fill in the blanks with the correct word from the options given below:

“Even if he had been doing his job, as a man of character he ___ not have cooperated with standard.”', NULL, '[{"text":"standardly","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"would","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"will not","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"often","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Concept:

The phrase

would not have + past participle

is used in conditional sentences referring to unreal situations in the past.

Step 1: Observe the sentence structure.

The sentence begins with:

Even if he had been doing his job...

This is a past unreal condition.

Step 2: Identify the required auxiliary verb.

The correct structure is:

would not have cooperated

Step 3: Reject the other options.

• standardly = adverb, unsuitable

• will not = incorrect tense

often = adverb, grammatically incorrect

Therefore,

Option (B)

Quick Tip: Third Conditional:

 $$  If+had+V_{3},would~have+V_{3} $$', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.390Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5407, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the appropriate word from the options given below:

“It is really difficult to deal ___ those people who do not want to listen to others.”', NULL, '[{"text":"at","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"about","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"after","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"with","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 3, 'Concept:

Certain verbs require specific prepositions. The verb deal is commonly followed by the preposition with when referring to handling people, situations, or problems.

Step 1: Recall the standard expression.

deal with somebody

means

handle or manage somebody

Step 2: Apply it to the sentence.

It is really difficult to deal with those people who do not want to listen to others.

Step 3: Eliminate incorrect options.

• deal at — incorrect

• deal about — incorrect

• deal after — incorrect

• deal with — correct expression

Hence,

Option (D)

Quick Tip: Remember:

deal with a problem

deal with a person

The preposition used with “deal” is almost always “with”.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.390Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5408, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Given below are four sentences. Choose the one which is grammatically correct:', NULL, '[{"text":"I gave him a few coins I had.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"I gave him few coins I had.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"I gave him the few coins I had.","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"I gave him the fewer coins I had.","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Concept:

The determiners few, a few, and the few have different meanings and usages.

• Few = almost none; emphasizes scarcity.

• A few = some; a small number but enough.

• The few = the small number that exist; all of them.

Step 1: Analyse Option (A).

I gave him a few coins I had.

This means that only some of the coins were given, not necessarily all. The sentence is grammatically acceptable but does not convey the intended meaning of giving all the coins possessed.

Step 2: Analyse Option (B).

I gave him few coins I had.

The expression is awkward and incomplete in this context. It incorrectly uses few without the appropriate sense required by the sentence.

Step 3: Analyse Option (C).

I gave him the few coins I had.

Here, the few coins I had means all the small number of coins that I possessed. This is grammatically correct and conveys a complete and meaningful idea.

Step 4: Analyse Option (D).

I gave him the fewer coins I had.

The word fewer is comparative and requires comparison between two quantities. No comparison is present here, making the sentence incorrect.

Therefore,

I gave him the few coins I had.

Hence,

Option (C)

Quick Tip: Few = almost none.

A few = some.

The few = all the small number available.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.390Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5409, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the appropriate word from the options given below:

The director is a perfectionist, ___ he is seldom satisfied with average performance.', NULL, '[{"text":"hence","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"however","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"nevertheless","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"but","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Step 1: Understand the first clause.

He is seldom satisfied with average performance.

This is a natural consequence of being a perfectionist.

Step 3: Determine the relationship between the clauses.

The second clause is the result of the first clause.

A word indicating result or consequence is required.

hence

means “therefore” or “for this reason.”

Step 4: Eliminate the other options.

• however = shows contrast

• nevertheless = shows concession

• but = shows opposition

None of these express result.

Thus the correct sentence is:

The director is a perfectionist, hence he is seldom satisfied with average performance.

Therefore,

Option (A)

Quick Tip: Hence = therefore = consequently.

Use it when the second statement is a result of the first statement.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.391Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5410, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Fill in the blanks with the appropriate Phrasal Verb from the options given below:

A snake might be hidden in this garden. You are advised to ___ the grass.', NULL, '[{"text":"keep out","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"keep under","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"keep off","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"keep up","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 2, 'Concept:

Phrasal verbs often have meanings that differ from the literal meanings of the individual words.

Step 1: Understand the situation.

The sentence warns that a snake may be hidden in the garden.

Therefore, the advice is to avoid stepping on or going near the grass.

Step 2: Examine the phrasal verb meanings.

• Keep out = stay outside.

• Keep under = control.

• Keep off = avoid stepping on or stay away from.

• Keep up = continue.

Step 3: Select the most suitable phrasal verb.

The common warning expression is:

Keep off the grass.

It means:

Do not walk on the grass.

This fits the context perfectly.

Hence,

Option (C)

Quick Tip: Keep off the grass = Do not walk on the grass.

This is a very common warning sign found in parks and gardens.

##### Passage for Questions 41–45

Read the given passage and answer the questions that follow:

##### Declining Number of Elephants

All is not well with India''s elephants. A population estimation exercise by the Wildlife Institute of India has suggested a disturbing decline in their number. The 2025 count is 22,446, 17% lower than in 2017, when the count was 27,312. Incidentally, the Centre informed the Lok Sabha in 2024 that India''s pachyderm population, as per a synchronised estimation, was 29,964. These surveys are not comparable because of methodological differences. Experts have also said that the DNA model may

have under-estimated the elephant count. These counters are valid, but there is enough and more evidence to be concerned about the health of the Indian elephants.

At least three inferences in the SAIF report ask for close reading. One, the once-contiguous elephant population in the Western Ghats is rapidly splintering due to changing land use, including expanding commercial plantations, invasive plants, farmland fencing, human encroachment and mushrooming developmental projects, all of which impact elephant survival and migration. Two, habitats in East Central India face fragmentation and deterioration from unmitigated mining and infrastructure projects. Habitat degradation and human use have prompted long-ranging elephants to venture into human dwellings, escalating human-wildlife conflict.

Three, the North East holds the second-largest elephant population in India but exploitation of natural resources since colonial times, driven by the productive nature of floodplains and geopolitics, has led to habitat loss and rising conflict with humans. The frequent reports of such conflicts and accidents on rail tracks from states such as Kerala, West Bengal and Assam confirm the anxieties recorded by the report. Project Elephant, established in 1992, needs a renewed push.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.391Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5411, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Choose the word that is closest in meaning to Taciturn.', NULL, '[{"text":"Reserved","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Energetic","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Reckless","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Curious","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, '### Step 1: Understanding the Question:

