The fusion band ___ playing since 9 a.m.', NULL, '[{"text":"have been","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"has been","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"were","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"are","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Concept: Subject-verb agreement depends on whether the subject is singular or plural.

Step 1: Identify the subject.

The subject is:

The fusion band

“Band” is a collective noun treated as singular here.

Step 2: Identify the tense.

The phrase:

since 9 a.m.

indicates an action continuing from the past to the present.

Hence:

Present Perfect Continuous Tense

Step 3: Choose correct auxiliary verb.

For singular subject:

has been

is correct.

Thus:

has been

Quick Tip: Remember:

Singular Subject  $ \rightarrow $ has been

Plural Subject  $ \rightarrow $ have been

“Since” usually indicates perfect tense.', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.587Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
