Despite many difficulties, she managed to ___ the challenge successfully.', NULL, '[{"text":"pull off","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"break down","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"give away","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"call out","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Concept: Phrasal verbs are combinations of verbs and prepositions/adverbs that create special meanings.

Step 1: Understand the sentence meaning.

The sentence indicates:

• She faced many difficulties

• Yet she succeeded

Thus, the required phrasal verb should mean:

“to succeed in doing something difficult”

Step 2: Analyze the options.

• Pull off → Successfully achieve something difficult

• Break down → Stop functioning or become emotional

• Give away  $ \rightarrow $ Donate or reveal

• Call out → Shout or summon

Thus:

Pull off

Quick Tip: Remember:

Pull off  $ \rightarrow $ Achieve successfully

Example:

“She pulled off a difficult performance.”', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.588Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
