The British Royal Society became a subject of laughter because of its ___ attitude.', NULL, '[{"text":"vain","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"wane","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"vein","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"vane","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Concept: Homophones are words that sound similar but have different meanings.

Step 1: Understand the sentence context.

The sentence suggests:

• The society was laughed at

• Due to pride or excessive self-importance

##### Step 2: Understand meanings of options.

• Vain  $ \rightarrow $ Excessively proud

• Wane  $ \rightarrow $ Decrease gradually

• Vein  $ \rightarrow $ Blood vessel

• Vane → Device showing wind direction

Only “vain” fits the context.

Thus:

vain

##### Quick Tip: Remember:

Vain  $ \rightarrow $ Proud / Arrogant

Do not confuse with:

Vein  $ \rightarrow $ Blood vessel', NULL, NULL, 2026, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T21:00:37.588Z', NULL, NULL, '[]', 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
