<table border=1 style=''margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;''><tr><td colspan="2">Column I</td><td colspan="2">Column II</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>1.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Eloquent</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>P.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Fluent or persuasive in speaking</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>2.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Vivacious</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Q.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Extremely unpleasant; repulsive</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>3.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Odious</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>R.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Lively, animated, and full of energy</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>4.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Penchant</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>S.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>A strong or habitual liking for something</td></tr></table>


Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', NULL, '[{"text":"1-P, 2-R, 3-Q, 4-S","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-R, 2-P, 3-S, 4-Q","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-P, 2-Q, 3-R, 4-S","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"1-S, 2-R, 3-Q, 4-P","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 0, 'Step 1: Match “Eloquent.”

“Eloquent” means:

Fluent or persuasive in speaking

Thus:

 $$ 1\to p $$ 

#### Step 2: Match “Vivacious.”

“Vivacious” means:

Lively, energetic, and animated

Thus:

 $$ 2\to R $$ 

##### Step 3: Match “Odious.”

“Odious” means:

Extremely unpleasant or hateful

Thus:

 $$ 3\to Q $$ 

##### Step 4: Match “Penchant.”

