INSERT OR REPLACE INTO questions ("id", "subject_id", "topic_id", "passage_id", "text", "text_hi", "options", "options_hi", "correct_option", "explanation", "explanation_hi", "difficulty", "year", "image_url", "image_alt", "explanation_image_url", "explanation_image_alt", "status", "supersedes_id", "created_by", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "assets_json", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5938, 11, NULL, NULL, 'Which among the following Acts introduced the system of Dyarchy in the provinces?', NULL, '[{"text":"Government of India Act, 1909","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Government of India Act, 1919","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Government of India Act, 1935","image_url":null,"alt":null},{"text":"Indian Councils Act, 1892","image_url":null,"alt":null}]', NULL, 1, 'Concept:

Chronology-based questions are extremely important in CUET History, especially from Modern India and the Gandhian phase of the National Movement.

To solve such questions correctly, students must remember the timeline of important movements led by Mahatma Gandhi.

Step 1: Identifying the year of Champaran Satyagraha.

Champaran Satyagraha was Gandhi''s first major movement in India.

It took place in:

It was launched to support indigo farmers in Bihar who were being exploited by European planters.

Thus, this is the earliest event among the given options.

Step 2: Identifying the year of Non-Cooperation Movement.

The Non-Cooperation Movement was launched by Mahatma Gandhi in:

1920

This movement aimed at boycotting British institutions, courts, schools and foreign goods. Hence this comes after Champaran Satyagraha.

Step 3: Identifying the year of Civil Disobedience Movement.

The Civil Disobedience Movement started with the famous Dandi March.

It was launched in:

1930

Thus, it occurred after the Non-Cooperation Movement.

Step 4: Identifying the year of Quit India Movement.

Quit India Movement was launched during World War II.

It began in:

1942

This was the last mass movement led by Gandhi against British rule.

Hence, it is the latest event.

Step 5: Arranging all events in correct order.

Therefore, chronological order becomes:

Champaran Satyagraha → Non-Cooperation Movement → Civil Disobedience Movement → Quit India Mo

Hence:

Therefore, the correct answer is:

(A) 3,2,1,4



