    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(C) Australopithecines</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(III) 1,00,000-40,000 years ago</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(D) Homo erectus</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(IV) About 15 million years ago</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A) - (I), (B) - (II), (C) - (III), (D) - (IV)"},{"id":"B","text":"(A) - (Ⅳ), (B) - (Ⅲ), (C) - (Ⅱ), (D) - (Ⅰ)"},{"id":"C","text":"(A) - (Ⅳ), (B) - (I), (C) - (II), (D) - (III)"},{"id":"D","text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (I), (C) - (IV), (D) - (III) 4. (A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)"}]', 0, 'B', 'Ramapithecus (15 mya), Neanderthal (100k-40k ya), Australopithecines (2 mya), Homo erectus (1.5 mya).', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[26]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.506Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (120, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q29', 29, 29, 'Baculoviruses are pathogens that attack', '[{"id":"A","text":"Birds and other mammals"},{"id":"B","text":"Bacteria and other fungi"},{"id":"C","text":"Plants and other algae"},{"id":"D","text":"Insects and other arthropods"}]', 0, 'D', 'Correct Answer: (4) Insects and other arthropods

Explanation:

Baculoviruses are used as biopesticides targeting insects and arthropods.

- They are host-specific and do not harm humans, plants, or vertebrates

Why others are wrong:

Other options include organisms which are not targeted by it.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[27]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.506Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (121, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q30', 30, 30, 'The second trophic level in an aquatic ecosystem is:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Phytoplanktons"},{"id":"B","text":"Fishes"},{"id":"C","text":"Large fishes"},{"id":"D","text":"Zooplanktons"}]', 0, 'D', 'Correct Answer: (4) Zooplanktons

Explanation:

Zooplanktons are primary consumers in aquatic ecosystems.

- They feed on phytoplankton (producers)

- Belong to the second trophic level

Why others are wrong:

- (1) Phytoplankton: Producers (first trophic level)

- (2) Fishes: Consumers (secondary consumers)

- (3) Large fishes: Higher trophic levels.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[27]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.506Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
