- All three received the Nobel Prize

CUET Tip: Remember key discoveries and scientific achievements.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[34]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (129, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q38', 38, 38, 'Arrange the given taxa of invertebrates in terms of their increasing numbers.

(A) Other animal groups

(B) Molluscs

(C) Insects

(D) Crustaceans', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A), (B), (C), (D)"},{"id":"B","text":"(A), (C), (B), (D)"},{"id":"C","text":"(D), (B), (A), (C)"},{"id":"D","text":"(C), (B), (D), (A)"}]', 0, 'C', 'Explanation:

This sequence follows the correct order of invertebrates occurrence as per NCERT diagrams.

CUET Tip: Practice NCERT diagrams.

Invertebrates

Vertebrates

Plants

Angiosperms

Figure 13.1 Representing global biodiversity: proportionate number of species of major taxa of plants, invertebrates and vertebrates', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[35]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (130, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q39', 39, 39, 'Match List-I with List-II:

<table border="1" style="margin: auto; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);">
      <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">List-I (Structures)</th>
      <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">List-II (Characteristics)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(A) Heterochromatin</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(I) A set of positively charged basic proteins</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(B) Nucleosomes</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(II) Densely packed and inactive genetic material</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(C) Histones</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(III) Transcriptionally active genetic material</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(D) Euchromatin</td><td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #444;">(IV) DNA is wrapped around the histone octamer to form this structure</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A) - (II), (B) - (IV), (C) - (I), (D) - (III)"},{"id":"B","text":"(A) - (I), (B) - (III), (C) - (II), (D) - (IV)"},{"id":"C","text":"(A) - (I), (B) - (II), (C) - (IV), (D) - (III)"},{"id":"D","text":"(A) - $ (\\mathrm{III}) $, (B) - $ (\\mathrm{IV}) $, (C) - $ (\\mathrm{I}) $, (D) - $ (\\mathrm{II}) $"}]', 0, 'A', 'Heterochromatin (II), Nucleosomes (IV), Histones (I), Euchromatin (III).', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[36]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (131, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q40', 40, 40, 'Identify one of the given factors which does not affect Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium.', '[{"id":"A","text":"Mutation"},{"id":"B","text":"Genetic drift"},{"id":"C","text":"Reproduction"},{"id":"D","text":"Gene flow"}]', 0, 'C', 'Explanation:

Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium is affected by:

- Gene migration

- Genetic drift

- Mutation

- Genetic recombination

- Natural selection

Reproduction does not disturb allele frequencies directly.

Why others are wrong:

- (1), (2), (4): All are valid factors that affect equilibrium', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[37]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (132, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q41', 41, 41, '4. The use of bio-resources by multinational companies and other organisations with proper authorisation from the countries and people concerned without compensatory payment.', '[{"id":"A","text":"1"},{"id":"B","text":"2"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'C', 'Correct Answer: (3) The use of bio-resources by multinational companies and other organisations without proper authorisation from the countries and people concerned without compensatory payment.

Explanation:

Biopiracy refers to unauthorized exploitation of biological resources and traditional knowledge.

- Often done by multinational companies

- Violates ethical and legal norms

Why others are wrong:

- (1), (2), (4): Do not capture the full scope of unauthorized use and lack of compensation

CUET Tip: Link ethics and law concepts from biotechnology.', 'pa93f1a8d2bd0', 'null', '[]', '[]', '[38]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (133, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q42', 42, 42, '4. Human alpha-lactalbumin', '[{"id":"A","text":"1"},{"id":"B","text":"2"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'D', 'Correct Answer: (4) Human alpha-lactalbumin

Explanation:

Rosie, the transgenic cow, produced milk enriched with human alpha-lactalbumin.

- Improves nutritional quality for infants

- Example of transgenic animal application', 'p5080a5077ff9', 'null', '[]', '[]', '[40]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (134, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q43', 43, 43, '4. Prevention of reverse transcription of mRNA', '[{"id":"A","text":"1"},{"id":"B","text":"2"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'A', 'Correct Answer: (1) Prevention of translation of mRNA

Explanation:

RNA interference (RNAi) silences gene expression by:

- Binding complementary double-stranded RNA to mRNA

- Preventing translation

Why others are wrong:

- (2) Preventing transcription: RNAi acts post-transcription

- (3) Blocking replication: RNAi doesn''t affect DNA replication

- (4) Preventing reverse transcription of mRNA: Not related to RNA

CUET Tip: Focus on gene silencing methods', 'p40603ff4cc7a', 'null', '[]', '[]', '[42]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (135, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q44', 44, 44, '4. Dipterans', '[{"id":"A","text":"1"},{"id":"B","text":"2"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'C', 'Correct Answer: (3) Crustaceans

Explanation:

Bt toxins from Bacillus thuringiensis affect:

- Lepidopterans (moths)

- Coleoptera (beetles)

- Diptera (flies, mosquitoes)

Crustaceans are not affected.

CUET Tip: Memorise host ranges for bioinsecticides.', 'p97ac4257e07f', 'null', '[]', '[]', '[43]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:38.507Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (136, 'biology-2025-05-20-shift-1', 'q45', 45, 45, '4. Antigen-antibody interaction', '[{"id":"A","text":"1"},{"id":"B","text":"2"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'D', 'Correct Answer: (4) Antigen-antibody interaction

Explanation:

ELISA detects infections by identifying:

- Antigens or antibodies in the sample

