In Sufism, the *shaikh* was revered as *wali*. What does the term *''wali''* mean?', '[{"id":"A","text":"Friend of People"},{"id":"B","text":"Friend of Holy Spirits"},{"id":"C","text":"Friend of God"},{"id":"D","text":"Friend of Disciples"}]', 0, 'C', 'After the shaikh''s death, his tomb became a pilgrimage site, symbolizing his union with God. This led to the shaikh being revered as a wali, or "friend of God."

