The pollen tube enters the embryo sac through:', '[{"id":"A","text":"chalazal end"},{"id":"B","text":"laterally"},{"id":"C","text":"antipodals"},{"id":"D","text":"micropylar end"}]', 0, 'D', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q42-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q42-figure-1.jpg","page":4,"alt":"Figure for question 42"}]', '[4]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.512Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2135, 'biology-2023-06-01-shift-3', 'q43', 43, 42, 'Answer the question from the diagram of typical anatropous ovule

The embryo sac is also known as:', '[{"id":"A","text":"megaspore"},{"id":"B","text":"female gametophyte"},{"id":"C","text":"megasporophyll"},{"id":"D","text":"megagamete"}]', 0, 'B', 'Embryo sac is also known as the female gametophyte or megagametophyte.

Sol. There are two layers in the seed coat - (i) outer layer (testa) that is usually hard and develops from the outer integument and (ii) the inner layer (tegmen) which forms from the inner integument when it becomes thin and papery.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q43-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-01-shift-3/q43-figure-1.jpg","page":4,"alt":"Figure for question 43"}]', '[4]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.512Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
