Figure showing packaging Of DNA Helix. Observe the figure and answer the following questions.

The number of base pairs (bp) in a typical nucleosome of DNA helix is:', '[{"id":"A","text":"100 bp"},{"id":"B","text":"200 bp"},{"id":"C","text":"500 bp"},{"id":"D","text":"1000 bp"}]', 0, 'B', 'A typical nucleosome contains 200 bp of DNA helix.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q41-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q41-figure-1.jpg","page":4,"alt":"Figure for question 41"}]', '[4]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.522Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
