The function of filiform apparatus is to:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Help in germination of pollen grains"},{"id":"B","text":"Guide the entry of pollen tube into ovule"},{"id":"C","text":"Help in the development of embryo"},{"id":"D","text":"Formation of male gametes"}]', 0, 'B', 'The function of the filiform apparatus is to guide the pollen tube into the synergids.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q46-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q46-figure-1.jpg","page":5,"alt":"Figure for question 46"}]', '[5]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.523Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2188, 'biology-2023-06-05-shift-3', 'q47', 47, 46, 'The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question.

The ploidy of parts (D) and (E) are:', '[{"id":"A","text":"(D)-n (E)-2n"},{"id":"B","text":"(D)-2n (E)-n"},{"id":"C","text":"(D)-n (E)-n"},{"id":"D","text":"(D)-n (E)-3n The figure given above shows the growth of pollen tube. Observe the figure and answer the following question. (a) Pollen tube and synergids respectively Identify the part (A) and (B). (b) Synergids and female gamete respectively (d) Pollen tube and female gamete respectively"}]', 0, 'C', 'D is egg cell and is haploid and, E is synergists and is also haploid.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q47-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/biology-2023-06-05-shift-3/q47-figure-1.jpg","page":5,"alt":"Figure for question 47"}]', '[5]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.523Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
