(Gattermann Koch reaction)', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A), (B), (C), (D) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(B), (C), (D), (E) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(E), (A), (D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(A), (B), (C), (E) only"}]', 0, 'D', 'Balz-Schiemann Reaction

Fluorobenzene Nitrogen Boron trifluoride', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q50-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-11-shift-3/q50-figure-1.jpg","page":5,"alt":"Figure for question 50"},{"id":"q50-figure-2","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-11-shift-3/q50-figure-2.jpg","page":5,"alt":"Figure for question 50"}]', '[5]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.643Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2558, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q01', 1, 1, 'Which of the following statements is not applicable to chemisorption?

(A) It is independent of temperature

(B) It is highly specific

(C) It is slow

(D) It is irreversible', '[{"id":"A","text":"(B) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(C) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(A) only"}]', 0, 'D', 'Chemisorption first increases and then decreases with temperature.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2559, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q02', 2, 2, 'Which isomerism is shown by the following pairs?

CH_{3}CH_{2}CH_{2}OH and CH_{3}CH_{2}OCH_{3}', '[{"id":"A","text":"Position isomerism"},{"id":"B","text":"Functional isomerism"},{"id":"C","text":"Structural isomerism"},{"id":"D","text":"Chain isomerism"}]', 0, 'B', '$ CH_{3}CH_{2}OCH_{3} $ and $ CH_{3}CH_{2}CH_{2}OH $ have different functional groups, hence, they are functional isomers.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2560, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q03', 3, 3, 'Which will form the most stable complex?', '[{"id":"A","text":"NCS"},{"id":"B","text":"CN $ ^{·} $"},{"id":"C","text":"H $ _{2} $O"},{"id":"D","text":"C $ _{2} $O $ _{4}^{2-} $"}]', 0, 'D', 'As $ C_2O_4^{2-} $ is a bidentate chelating ligand, it forms rings and hence $ C_2O_4^{2-} $ will form the most stable complex.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2561, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q04', 4, 4, 'How many Cr-O bonds in dichromate ions are of the same bond length and are in resonance?', '[{"id":"A","text":"8"},{"id":"B","text":"6"},{"id":"C","text":"3"},{"id":"D","text":"4"}]', 0, 'B', 'In Cr2O72- ion, 6(Cr-O) bonds have the same bond length 163 pm because of the resonance and 2(Cr-O) bonds have a bond length of 179 pm.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2562, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q05', 5, 5, 'If time taken for a first order reaction to get 90% complete is 24 min, its t99.9% will be:', '[{"id":"A","text":"240 min"},{"id":"B","text":"48 min"},{"id":"C","text":"120 min"},{"id":"D","text":"72 min"}]', 0, 'D', '$ t\,90 = 2.303/k\log(100/10) $

k = 0.09595

t99.9 = 2.303/0.09595 $ \log(100/0.1) = 72.00 $ min', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2563, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q08', 6, 6, 'In process of froth floatation, which is used for the removing gangue from sulphide ones. Depressant used is:

(a) Xanthates

(b) Cresols

(c) NaCN

(d) Aniline

Zeolite can be used to soften hard water when:', '[{"id":"A","text":"$ Ca^{2+} $ or $ Mg^{2+} $ ion in zeolite are replaced by $ Na^{+} $ions in hard water"},{"id":"B","text":"$ Ca^{2+} $ ions in zeolite are replaced by $ Mg^{2+} $ ions in hard water"},{"id":"C","text":"$ Na^{+} $ ions in zeolite are replaced by $ Ca^{2+} $ and $ Mg^{2+} $ ions in hard water"},{"id":"D","text":"None is correct"}]', 0, 'C', 'It uses NaCN as a depressant in the mixture of ZnS and PbS, where ZnS forms soluble complex and PbS form froth.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q08-figure-1","kind":"figure","path":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3/q08-figure-1.jpg","page":1,"alt":"Figure for question 8"}]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2564, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q10', 7, 7, 'Indium is mainly refined by:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Vapour phase refining"},{"id":"B","text":"Distillation"},{"id":"C","text":"Zone refining"},{"id":"D","text":"Liquation"}]', 0, 'C', 'Ga, In, Si, Ge are refined by zone refining or vacuum refining. This method is very useful for producing semiconductor and other metals of very high purity.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2565, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q11', 8, 8, 'Match the Items List-I and List-II:', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)"},{"id":"B","text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)"},{"id":"C","text":"(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)"},{"id":"D","text":"(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)"}]', 0, 'D', '[A] The instantaneous rate is the rate of a reaction at a period of time that is so short that the concentrations of reactants and products change by a negligible amount.

[B] Average rate: the average rate of a reaction is defined as a rate of change of consideration of reactant (or of a product) over a specific measurable period of time.

[C] The mathematical expression which describes the reaction rate in terms of molar concentrations of the reactants as determined experimentally is called rate law

[D] For a zero-order reaction, the rate law is rate = k, where k is the rate constant.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[{"id":"q11-table-1","kind":"table","path":"/local-papers/assets/chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3/q11-table-1.jpg","page":1,"alt":"Table for question 11"}]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.644Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2566, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q13', 9, 9, 'In corrosion:

(A) A metal is oxidised by loss of electrons to oxygen

(B) It is an Electrochemical phenomenon

(C) The object under corrosion behaves as anode

(D) Coating the metal with Zn can save iron object from corrosion', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A), (B) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(A), (B), (C) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(A), (B), (C), (D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(B), (C), (D) only"}]', 0, 'C', '[A] In corrosion, a metal is oxidized by loss of electrons to oxygen and the formation of oxides

[B] Corrosion is a process of conversion of a metal into its compounds by continuous interaction with atmospheric air and water vapour. This is an electrochemical reaction in which metals lose electrons and oxygen accepts them.03-Jul-2022

[C] Corrosion occurs at the anode

[D] Galvanization is the process of applying a protective zinc coating to steel or iron, to prevent rusting.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.645Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (2567, 'chemistry-2023-06-13-shift-3', 'q14', 10, 10, 'Excess of Lead from human body can be removed by using which of the following chelating agents?', '[{"id":"A","text":"D-Penicillamine"},{"id":"B","text":"DMG"},{"id":"C","text":"Desferrioxime B"},{"id":"D","text":"EDTA"}]', 0, 'D', 'Health care providers treat adults with lead levels greater than 45 mcg/dL of blood and children who can''t tolerate the drug used in conventional chelation therapy most commonly with a chemical called calcium disodium ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA).', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:51.645Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
