Migration Siberian Cranes :: Bear', '[{"id":"A","text":"Regulation"},{"id":"B","text":"Hibernation"},{"id":"C","text":"Aestivation"},{"id":"D","text":"Diapause"}]', 0, 'B', 'Hibernation is the state of an organism to conserve energy and the metabolic functions of the body slows down.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.533Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3677, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q11', 11, 11, 'Development of analogous structure or organs are a result of _', '[{"id":"A","text":"Divergent evolution"},{"id":"B","text":"Convergent evolution"},{"id":"C","text":"Adaptive radiation"},{"id":"D","text":"Saltation"}]', 0, 'B', 'Analogous structures develop due to convergent evolution where in organisms belonging to different species are exposed to the same environmental conditions and they adapt similarly.

ovt as tu8 : tostoo su noitgo novig sdi to onon :oM', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.533Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3678, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q12', 12, 12, 'The treatment of the bacterial cell with divalent cations leads to', '[{"id":"A","text":"Increase in hydrophilic nature of DNA molecule"},{"id":"B","text":"Decreases efficiency with which DNA enters the bacterium"},{"id":"C","text":"Change in permeability of cell wall"},{"id":"D","text":"Increased efficiency with which DNA enters the bacterium"}]', 0, 'D', 'When the cell is treated with a specific solution of divalent cation calcium, it increases the efficiency of the cell to take up the foreign DNA through the pores in the cell wall. DNA is a hydrophilic molecule; it cannot pass through cell membranes. In order to force bacteria to take up the plasmid, the bacterial cells are first made ''competent'' to take up DNA.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.533Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3679, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q13', 13, 13, 'A person complaining of stomach ache, weakness and sustained high fever was recommended Widal test by the doctor. Identify the pathogen responsible for the disease the person is suffering from:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Streptococcus pneumonia"},{"id":"B","text":"Rhino Virus"},{"id":"C","text":"Salmonella typhi"},{"id":"D","text":"Plasmodium vivax"}]', 0, 'C', 'Widal test is used to diagnose typhoid. In this case, the person is suffering from typhoid which is caused by Salmonella Typhi bacteria.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.534Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3680, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q14', 14, 14, 'If 100 deaths take place in a population of 10,00,000 per year, then the death rate will be', '[{"id":"A","text":"0.001 per person per year"},{"id":"B","text":"0.0001 per person per year"},{"id":"C","text":"0.1 per person per year"},{"id":"D","text":"1 per person per year"}]', 0, 'B', 'The death rate

=(Number of deaths per year / Total population)

= $ \frac{100}{10,00,000} $

= $ \frac{1}{10000} $

=0.0001 per person per year', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.534Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3681, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q15', 15, 15, 'The genetic variation shown by medicinal plant Rauwolfia vomitoria growing in Himalayan ranges, is an example of', '[{"id":"A","text":"Ecosystem Diversity"},{"id":"B","text":"Ecological Diversity"},{"id":"C","text":"Species Diversity"},{"id":"D","text":"Genetic Diversity"}]', 0, 'D', 'The diversity shown by the medicinal plant Rauwolfia vomitoria growing in different Himalayan ranges is an example of genetic diversity.

The diversity at the ecosystem level is called ecological diversity.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.534Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3682, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q16', 16, 16, 'Prime contaminant of lake for eutrophication is', '[{"id":"A","text":"Dissolved oxygen"},{"id":"B","text":"Algal bloom"},{"id":"C","text":"Nitrate and phosphate"},{"id":"D","text":"Fungi and Bacteria"}]', 0, 'C', 'Eutrophication is when the availability of nutrients increases excessively, the growth of algae starts. This excessive alga can take up the whole oxygen in the water and thus the aquatic animals start to get deprived of oxygen. The nitrates from nitrogen and phosphates from phosphorus are when washed away from the fields, they get mixed with lakes and rivers causing eutrophication there.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.534Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3683, 'biology-2022-08-20', 'q17', 17, 17, 'In Verhulst Pearl logistic growth curve equation, $ \frac{\mathrm{d}N}{\mathrm{d}t} = rN\left(\frac{K-N}{K}\right) $, ''r'' refers to:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Population density at time t"},{"id":"B","text":"Population density at time Zero"},{"id":"C","text":"Intrinsic rate of natural increase"},{"id":"D","text":"Carrying capacity"}]', 0, 'C', 'Verhulst-Pearl Logistic Growth curve equation is,

$ \frac{\mathrm{d}N}{\mathrm{d}t} = rN\left(\frac{K-N}{K}\right), $

where

N = Population density at time t

r = Intrinsic rate of natural increase

K = carrying capacity.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.534Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
