(B) Database is the skeleton of the database that represents the structure

(C) Meta data is data about constraint

(D) We may not retrieve the data through queries', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A) and (B) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(B) and (C) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(C) and (D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(D) and (A) only"}]', 0, 'A', '(A) → Database Schema is the logical design of database is correct.

(B) → Databox is the skeleton of the database that represents the structure.

Types of database Schema.

