(A)(B)(C)(D)', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)"},{"id":"B","text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)"},{"id":"C","text":"(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)"},{"id":"D","text":"(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)"}]', 0, 'C', 'i. Bus Topology is a single backbone shared among the noces

ii. Star Topoloty is like central networking device like switch and hubs.

iii. Ring Topology: Each node is connected to two other devices, one each and either side.

iv. Tree topology: There are Multiple branches and also known as hybrid topology.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.589Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3945, 'computer-science-2022', 'q12', 11, 11, 'In context of network type Local Area Network (LAN), which of the following statement(s) are correct:

(A) It covers a small area, within a building or a campus

(B) Less congestion

(C) Less fault tolerance

(D) It operates on the principle of broadcasting

(E) Speed of LAN is slower than MAN and WAN', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A), (B) and (C) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(C), (D) and (E) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(B), (C) and (D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(A), (B) and (D) only"}]', 0, 'D', 'LAN $ \rightarrow $ Local Area network.

(A) LAN is a group of devices connected in small geographic area within building or a campus.

(B) LAN has ww congestion as compared to WAN

(C) LAN has higher fault tolerance.

(D) It operates on the principle of broadcasting.

(E) Speed of LAN is faster than MAN and WAN So, option (A, B, D) are correct but option (C and E) are wrong', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.589Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3946, 'computer-science-2022', 'q13', 12, 12, 'Identify the type of error which is raised when variable name is not defined?', '[{"id":"A","text":"TypeError"},{"id":"B","text":"NameError"},{"id":"C","text":"ValueError"},{"id":"D","text":"SyntaxError"}]', 0, 'B', 'i. TypeError: In Phyton TypeError is an Exception that occurs when the data type of an object in an operation is inappropriate.

ii. NameError: In Python NameError occurs when we try to access a variable or function that is not defined or before it is defined.

To solve the error, variable name should be spelled correctly and access the variable only after defining it.

iii. ValueError: It is an exception that occurs when a function receives an argument of the correct data type but an inappropriate value.

It usually occurs in mathematical operations that require certain kind of values.

iv. SyntaxError: It occurs when teh Interpreter encounters invalid syntax in code.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.589Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (3947, 'computer-science-2022', 'q14', 13, 13, 'Which of the following is a 12 digit hexadecimal number that uniquely identifies a machine on a network?', '[{"id":"A","text":"MAC address"},{"id":"B","text":"IP address"},{"id":"C","text":"Processor Number"},{"id":"D","text":"ISP Code"}]', 0, 'A', 'i. Mac address: Media Access control (MAC) address is a 12 digit hexadecimal number assigned to each device connected to the network.

ii. IP address: IP address is a unique address that identifies a device on the internet or a local network.

iii. Processor number: It is four digit processor number, in which first digit represents the generation, Example 9800 is a $ 9^{th} $ gen processor, while one labelled 8800 is $ 8^{th} $ gen technology.

iv. ISP code: Internet Service provider (ISP) is a company that provides individuals and organizations access to the internet and other related services.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.589Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
