(d)', '[{"id":"A","text":"(III),"},{"id":"B","text":"(IV),"},{"id":"C","text":"(II),"},{"id":"D","text":"(I)"}]', 0, 'B', 'ii. Degree $ \rightarrow $ refers to no. of attribute/column in a table.

i. Primary key $ \rightarrow $ Column which can uniquely identify each tuple in a table.

iii. Cardinality → refers to the number of tuples/rows in a table.

iv. Unique $ \rightarrow $ keyword used in sql quires in which all the values in a column distinct.

