A. Karnad is an

B. Oral tales of India are

C. Karnad''s plays and drama

List I

List II

I. Indian playwright

II. Wonderfully dramatized by Karnad.

III. Given a new interpretation to the historical, mythical and oral tales and stories

D. The uncanny ability IV. His capability to remake of Karnad is the past in the image of the present', '[{"id":"A","text":"A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I"},{"id":"B","text":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II"},{"id":"C","text":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV"},{"id":"D","text":"A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III"}]', 0, 'C', 'Step 1: Let''s read the passage once to remember the central idea and the key words.

Step 2: Let''s try to match the fragment A with the fragments of list II. A matches with I.

Step 3: Let''s see which option/options has/have A matching with I. It''s only one: c. Hence the answer is (c).', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[2]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:58:59.617Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
