them what is the code for ''BIRD''', '[{"id":"A","text":"60"},{"id":"B","text":"32"},{"id":"C","text":"33"},{"id":"D","text":"24"}]', 0, 'C', 'DOG = 4 + 15 + 7 = 26, FLY = 6 + 12 + 25 = 43

So, BIRD = 2 + 9 + 18 + 4 = 33', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[3]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.890Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4567, 'general-test-2022-10-06-shift-1', 'q26', 26, 25, 'Which of the following seas has highest salinity in the world?', '[{"id":"A","text":"Dead Sea"},{"id":"B","text":"Black Sea"},{"id":"C","text":"Red Sea"},{"id":"D","text":"Mediterranean Sea"}]', 0, 'A', '"Dead Sea" has highest salinity in the world.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[3]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.890Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4568, 'general-test-2022-10-06-shift-1', 'q27', 27, 26, 'If the sugar price is increased by 25% by how much percent consumption should be reduced that expense remains same.', '[{"id":"A","text":"25%"},{"id":"B","text":"20%"},{"id":"C","text":"30%"},{"id":"D","text":"35%"}]', 0, 'B', 'Let original price of sugar = Rs. 100

∴ Price of sugar for today = Rs. 100 + Rs. 25 = Rs. 125

In order to bring down the price to original i.e., Rs. 100, its price should be decreased by = Rs. 125 - Rs. 100 = Rs.25

∴ On Rs. 125, the price should be decreased by = Rs.25

On Re.1, the price should be decreased by = Rs. $ \frac{25}{125} $

On Rs. 100, the price should be decreased by = Rs. $ \frac{25}{125} \times 100 = Rs.\frac{1}{5} \times 100 = Rs. $

∴ Price should be decreased by 20%', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[3]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.890Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (4569, 'general-test-2022-10-06-shift-1', 'q28', 28, 27, 'Mohan''s Mother is three times as old as Mohan. After 6 years, his mother will be two times as old as he will be them, find the age of Mohan.', '[{"id":"A","text":"18 years"},{"id":"B","text":"6 years"},{"id":"C","text":"3 years"},{"id":"D","text":"16 years"}]', 0, 'B', 'Let Mohan''s age be = x years

Mohan''s mother age = 3x years

After 6 years

Mohan''s age = x + 6 years

Mohan''s mother age = 3x + 6

It is given that after 6 years

$ \Rightarrow 3x + 6 = 2(x + 6) $

= 3x + 6 = 2x + 12

= x = 6 years

$ \therefore $ Age of Mohan is 6 years', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[3]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.890Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
