2. -13.6 (II) I excited state

3. 0 (III) Ground state

4. -0.85 (IV) III excited state', '[{"id":"A","text":"(1)-(II), (2)-(III), (3)-(I), (4)-(IV)"},{"id":"B","text":"(1)-(III), (2)-(I), (3)-(II), (4)-(IV)"},{"id":"C","text":"(1)-(IV), (2)-(I), (3)-(III), (4)-(II)"},{"id":"D","text":"(1)-(I), (2)-(II), (3)-(III), (4)-(IV)"}]', 0, 'A', 'In hydrogen atom, For ground state,

$$ E_{1}=\frac{-13.6}{1^{2}}=-13.6eV $$

$$ \frac{10}{1}=0.2\times\frac{ 皿 }{ 皿 } $$

For I^{st} excited state,

