For III^{rd} excited state,

$$ E_{4}=\frac{-13.6}{4^{2}}=-0.85eV $$

For infinity,

$$ E_{\infty}=\frac{-13.6}{\infty^{2}}=0 $$', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[6]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.969Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5037, 'physics-2022-08-26', 'q41', 31, 31, 'A particular radioactive sample has a half-life of 12 years. The fraction of it that remains undecayed after 48 years, will be:', '[{"id":"A","text":"$ \\frac{1}{4}^{th} $ of its initial amount"},{"id":"B","text":"$ \\frac{1}{8}^{th} $ of its initial amount"},{"id":"C","text":"$ \\frac{1}{16}^{th} $ of its initial amount"},{"id":"D","text":"$ \\frac{1}{32}^{th} $ of its initial amount"}]', 0, 'C', 'We have,

$$ \begin{aligned}&N=\frac{N_{0}}{2^{n}}\\ &N=\frac{N_{0}}{2^{\left(\frac{48}{12}\right)}}=\frac{N_{0}}{2^{4}}=\frac{N_{0}}{16}\\ \end{aligned} $$', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[6]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.969Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5038, 'physics-2022-08-26', 'q42', 32, 32, 'Choose the correct statements from the following based on the properties of atomic nucleus.

on the properties of atomic nucleus.

I. Radius of a nucleus of man no. A depends on its mass number as $R \propto A^{3}$

II. Radius of nucleus and mass number are related as $R \propto A^{\frac{1}{3}}$

III. Density of nuclei is always a constant

IV. Density of nuclei depends on its mass number A

V. Density of nuclei depends on its size, volume', '[{"id":"A","text":"I and III only"},{"id":"B","text":"II and III only"},{"id":"C","text":"II and IV only"},{"id":"D","text":"II and V only"}]', 0, 'B', 'We have, $R = R_{0} A^{1/3} \Rightarrow R \propto A^{1/3}$ and, density of nucleus is constant if we ignore isotopic effect.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[6]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.969Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5039, 'physics-2022-08-26', 'q43', 33, 33, 'The constancy of the binding energy in the range $30 < A < 170$ in binding energy curve, is a consequence of the given fact:', '[{"id":"A","text":"Nuclear forces are charge independent"},{"id":"B","text":"Nuclear forces are short ranged"},{"id":"C","text":"Nuclear forces are the strongest forces"},{"id":"D","text":"Nuclear forces are the attractive in nature"}]', 0, 'B', 'For medium and large size nuclei, the distance between nucleons will increase which lead to decrease in nuclear force. As nuclear force will decrease by same amount in nuclei between $A=30$ and $A=170$ because of short range of nuclear force. So, binding energy is constant for $30 < A < 170$.', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[6]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.969Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (5040, 'physics-2022-08-26', 'q45', 34, 34, 'For transistor action, which of the following statements are correct:

(A) The base region must be very thin and lightly doped

(B) Base emitter and collector regions should have same size but different doping concentration

(C) The collector junction is reverse biased and emitter junction is forward biased

(D) Base, emitter and collector regions should have different sizes, but same doping concentration

(E) Both the emitter junction as well as the collector junction are forward biased', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A) and (C) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(A), (B) and (D) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(B), (C) and (D) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(B) and (C) only (d) (B) and (C) only"}]', 0, 'A', 'Transistor operate in proper way, when

(a) The emitter should be forward biased and collector should be reverse biased.

(b) Base in thin and lightly doped.

(c) Emitter size is moderate (larger than base) but slightly smaller than collector (due to heat dissipation from collector region)', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[6]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:06.970Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
