Quick Tip: When squaring numbers in scientific notation, remember to square the base number
normally (32 = 9) and multiply the exponent power by 2 (10−15×2 = 10−30). Keeping your exponent
tracks separate makes verification much easier!', NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[1]', 'keyed', '[]', '2026-11-05T20:59:19.970Z', NULL, NULL, 'ai_draft', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
