(D) Hallucinations

(E) Conduct disorder

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', '[{"id":"A","text":"(A), (B) & (E) only"},{"id":"B","text":"(A), (B) & (D) only"},{"id":"C","text":"(A), (B) & (C) only"},{"id":"D","text":"(A), (D) & (E) only"}]', 0, 'C', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[24]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.145Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7449, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q21', 21, 21, 'Beth, aged 18, has been trying to keep a secret from her family and friends. She is a binge eater. When others are not around, she gorges on cakes, ice cream and other food so fast that she hardly has time to chew. Once she begins there is no stopping until her stomach aches. After her binge, Beth feels disgusted with herself and makes herself vomit, then takes a double dose of laxative. Her life is totally dominated by her obsession with food. Beth is suffering from which disorder?', '[{"id":"A","text":"Anorexia Nervosa"},{"id":"B","text":"Body Dysmorphic Disorder"},{"id":"C","text":"Bulimia Nervosa"},{"id":"D","text":"Conduct disorder"}]', 0, 'C', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[25]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.145Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7450, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q22', 22, 22, 'According to Holmes and Rahe, arrange stressful life events in sequence from highest to lowest in terms of their severity:

(A) Unexpected accident or trauma

(B) Break-up with friend

(C) Illness of family member

(D) Death of a close family member

## (E) Change in eating habits

Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', '[{"id":"A","text":"(D), (A), (C), (B), (E)"},{"id":"B","text":"(D), (C), (A), (B), (E)"},{"id":"C","text":"(D), (B), (A), (C), (E)"},{"id":"D","text":"(B), (D), (A), (E), (C)"}]', 0, 'A', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[26,27]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.145Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7451, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q23', 23, 23, 'Which one is not a characteristic of crowding experience?', '[{"id":"A","text":"Loss in privacy"},{"id":"B","text":"loss of control over social interaction"},{"id":"C","text":"Negative view of the space around the person"},{"id":"D","text":"Feeling of comfort"}]', 0, 'D', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[28]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.147Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7452, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q24', 24, 24, 'Match List-I with List-II

<table border=1 style=''margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;''><tr><td colspan="2">List – I</td><td colspan="2">List – II</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>A.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Self-esteem</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>I.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>The extent to which individuals believe that they themselves control their life&#x27;s outcomes.</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>B.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Self-efficacy</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>II.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Judgements about our own value or worth.</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>C.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Social-Self</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>III.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>The way we perceive ourselves and the ideas we hold about our competencies and attributes.</td></tr><tr><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>D.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Self-concept</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>IV.</td><td style=''text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;''>Familial or relational self.</td></tr></table>

## Choose the correct answer from the options given below:', '[{"id":"A","text":"A - II, B - III, C - IV, D - I"},{"id":"B","text":"A - II, B - IV, C - I, D - III"},{"id":"C","text":"A - II, B - I, C - IV, D - III"},{"id":"D","text":"A - II, B - IV, C - III, D - I"}]', 0, 'C', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[29]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["contains_table_data","missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.147Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7453, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q25', 25, 25, 'Who devised the concept of Intelligence Quotient (IQ)?', '[{"id":"A","text":"Alfred Binet"},{"id":"B","text":"Theodore Simon"},{"id":"C","text":"William Stern"},{"id":"D","text":"Lewis Terman"}]', 0, 'C', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[30]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.147Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO practice_questions ("id", "paper_slug", "question_key", "source_question_no", "position", "stem", "options_json", "options_are_images", "correct_option", "explanation", "passage_key", "match_list_json", "arrangement_json", "assets_json", "source_pages_json", "review_status", "review_flags_json", "created_at", "updated_at", "deleted_at", "explanation_source", "explanation_status", "reviewed_by", "reviewed_at") VALUES (7454, 'psychology-2024-07-19-shift-1', 'q26', 26, 26, 'While judging a personality pageant, raters gave high scores to contestants who were already famous because of their presence in popular T.V. serials or advertisements and tended to give low scores to those who were not so popular. This phenomena is called', '[{"id":"A","text":"Halo effect"},{"id":"B","text":"Recency effect"},{"id":"C","text":"Primacy effect"},{"id":"D","text":"Rosenthal effect"}]', 0, 'A', NULL, NULL, 'null', '[]', '[]', '[31]', 'verified_against_ocr', '["missing_explanation"]', '2026-11-05T20:59:25.148Z', NULL, NULL, 'none', 'unreviewed', NULL, NULL);
